{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:27:51.102Z","ordinal":419281,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17e67-723e-7dc2-ac38-d1653a875521","author":"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/current_main_rc_path_audit\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED.** The check conclusions and PR identities match, but the current Linux job steps differ from the checkpoint wording:\n\n- #268 is running `scripts/package-linux.sh`.\n- #276 is running `npm --prefix cli test`.\n- #277 is running `cargo test --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml`.\n\nLines 7 and 11 should describe the Linux jobs as in progress without assigning all three the same step, or name their current steps accurately. `git diff --check` passes. Diff SHA-256: `b0f614270af121656096810a8fab81e948176fd33b780a438a7c0a3def44c049`."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e33-4871-7821-919e-a68cb04742bc","create_time":1793122071.1024072}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":20350}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:28:01.395Z","ordinal":419282,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0df1baf3481a090135379287baa56","status":"completed","call_id":"call_82099d5bbcbd4493a6feec851bc9d4dc","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-readiness-20261027/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\\n@@\\n-**Readiness PR #268:** GitHub reports PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) open at exact head `d37746f20da27a8b11a9c25c14c08fe0db197add`, based on current `main` `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. On that exact head, JavaScript/TypeScript check run `40544627915`, CodeQL check [122332399521](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/122332399521), and Node 22/24 jobs in run `40544627770` passed; the `linux-x86_64` package/test job in that same run remains in progress at `npm --prefix cli test`. An independent review accepted the correction to stale branch attribution; final review of this checkpoint, terminal Linux CI, and required merge gates remain pending. No merge is claimed.\\n+**Readiness PR #268:** GitHub reports PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) open at exact head `d37746f20da27a8b11a9c25c14c08fe0db197add`, based on current `main` `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. On that exact head, JavaScript/TypeScript check run `40544627915`, CodeQL check [122332399521](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/122332399521), and Node 22/24 jobs in run `40544627770` passed; the `linux-x86_64` package/test job in that same run remains in progress. An independent review accepted the correction to stale branch attribution; final review of this checkpoint, terminal Linux CI, and required merge gates remain pending. No merge is claimed.\\n@@\\n-**Other release-path PRs:** PR [#276](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/276) records a synthetic-only qualification-host preflight (10/10) bound to `ceabfcc`; its Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass, while its Linux package/test CI is in progress at `npm --prefix cli test`. Its evidence does not establish custodian access, held-out qualification, or acceptance. PR [#277](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/277) addresses configured Git-hook execution during checkpoint and retention operations. An independent read-only review of exact head `54d0f9f5be930a782f4a44abea15d015be6c4d3f` found a config-change race in per-hook suppression and silent success accounting after retention ref-deletion failures; findings were posted for the active implementation owner. Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks now pass; its Linux package/test job is in progress at `npm --prefix cli test`. Neither PR is merged.\\n+**Other release-path PRs:** PR [#276](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/276) records a synthetic-only qualification-host preflight (10/10) bound to `ceabfcc`; its Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass, while its Linux package/test CI remains in progress. Its evidence does not establish custodian access, held-out qualification, or acceptance. PR [#277](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/277) addresses configured Git-hook execution during checkpoint and retention operations. An independent read-only review of exact head `54d0f9f5be930a782f4a44abea15d015be6c4d3f` found a config-change race in per-hook suppression and silent success accounting after retention ref-deletion failures; findings were posted for the active implementation owner. Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks now pass; its Linux package/test CI remains in progress. Neither PR is merged.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e33-4871-7821-919e-a68cb04742bc","create_time":1793122075.694547}}}
