{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:40:28.566Z","ordinal":419745,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-eb929716-5e62-436f-9ced-43286cc1e3dd","process_id":"56608","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'E5|OpenRouter|ChatGPT|standalone|provider' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/README.md docs/v1.0.0/evidence docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10 -g '*.md' | head -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'E5|OpenRouter|ChatGPT|standalone|provider' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/README.md docs/v1.0.0/evidence docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10 -g '*.md'","query":"E5|OpenRouter|ChatGPT|standalone|provider","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"rg: docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:5:**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** There are 31 blocker requirements, none of them met. Task-quality, standalone and real-terminal qualification are **unverified**: no qualifying evidence exists yet. The contest entry was submitted, is frozen, and is tracked separately.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:28:| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:46:4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:43:| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:46:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:113:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:122:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:134:4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:149:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:153:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:331:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:36:| REQ-AGT-31..39 | CTX-003..011 | Durable vs retrieved distinction; role policy; budget vs actual route capacity, fail closed (`ContextBudgetError`); cross-boundary failover re-admission; same-boundary failover cheap; compaction removes only disposable; admission evidence; resume≠recovery; manual==auto compaction semantics | P2 §12 | DEMONSTRATED / SBIS (CTX-006: client.ts executeWithFailover; egress.test) | P (WP05 qual for CTX-006) | 10-12 I-05 (provider context-length 400 ends turn), CTX-02 (steering truncated after compaction; fixed ee70f68), d88a897 false-absence; 10-13 compaction ledger self-assessed only |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:74:| REQ-AGT-53 | Compaction A–D | No default step/time ceiling; state-aware repetition; durable compaction commit (archive→task→session, fsync); queued `/compact`; provider-advertised capacity; labelled token counts | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md; reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md | \"Met\"/\"Met (scripted)\"; 1 completed live run (run 3, REGRESSION_FREE); **\"Independent acceptance is pending\"** (ledger line 3) | **N** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:75:| REQ-PRV-11 | Standalone | Works identically without homelab-ai gateway; counting optional; labelled estimates | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:7-9; handoff doc | \"Accepted under scripted evidence\"; **no live run against LM Studio/llama.cpp/vLLM standalone** (ledger \"Not done\"; release notes Known limits) | N |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:129:| HIST-04 | S2 | Extensions, standalone | cli/src/plugins.ts:47-54 | SOURCE: home plugin dirs include `~/.config/opencode/plugins` — every `*.js/*.mjs` there is imported in-process at turn start; USER_MANUAL.md:295 lists only `~/.config/nexus/`, `~/.nexus/` | Another product's plugins execute inside Nexus with full authority, undocumented | Remove the opencode dir or make it opt-in + documented |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:133:| HIST-08 | S2 | Standalone local inference | reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md \"Not done\"; docs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:33 | DOC-CLAIM: all live evidence is homelab gateway (llama.cpp behind aihost). No live run on plain LM Studio/vLLM/llama.cpp/Ollama although quickstart's first-run path is LM Studio | Primary documented setup unqualified | v1 must include live standalone qualification on ≥2 servers |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:195:| REQ-PRV-V1-01 | Live standalone qualification on ≥2 non-homelab OpenAI-compatible servers | HIST-08; standalone requirement | BLOCKER | Recorded runs with manifest; T2 subset pass ≥ pre-registered threshold |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:229:| Live standalone run; live capacity/worker-change observation; live TUI `/compact` queue | compaction ledger \"Not done\" | Not done | Open |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:231:| Live qualification of openai, anthropic, copilot, compatible providers | CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE | Not run | Open |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:237:- **Supported workflows:** interactive Ratatui TUI (`nexus`), REPL (`nexus repl`, `--approve`), headless `nexus run` with JSON/exit codes (0 verified, 2 REGRESSION_FREE), resume (`-r`, `/resume`), `nexus doctor`, `nexus trust`, providers/connect, `/team` and `nexus operation` durable multi-unit work, checkpoints/undo, MCP client + `serve-mcp`, skills/plugins, eval.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:239:- **homelab-ai:** optional gateway (capability discovery, tokenize, admitted-count headers); Nexus must and claims to work standalone; standalone proven only by scripted fixtures.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:9:| cli/src/providers.ts, provider_cli.ts, model_catalog.ts, credentials.ts, oauth.ts, config.ts, usage.ts, search_web.ts, onboard.ts | full read |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:11:| cli/src/core/provider_recovery.ts, provider_capabilities.ts | full read |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:14:| cli/test/{client_robustness,cloud_providers,credential_boundary,credential_home,egress,output_truncation_recovery,provider_capabilities,provider_connect,provider_recovery,provider_recovery_agent,config}.test.ts | test-name inventory; targeted runs (sec. 8) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:18:- Config (config.ts:16-40): env load order = install `cli/.env` (no override) -> `~/.config/nexus/config.env` (override) -> **cwd `.env` (override:true, any key)**. Credential authority snapshot (operator env + config.env) taken before cwd `.env` (client.ts:77-101); provider selection, provider base URL, disclosure authorization and stored-token binding use that snapshot. Everything else (TLS/Node env, timeouts, recovery policy, LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT/FALLBACKS, provider key env vars) reads live `process.env`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:19:- Two connection kinds: (a) legacy \"appliance/endpoint\" path (no provider id): OpenAI Chat Completions, `/v1` appended, fallback list, `X-Task-Class`, gateway token file / config.env key scoped by origin (client.ts:123-133), no receipts, no spending limits; (b) provider connections (providers.ts:46-116): openrouter, openai (Responses), anthropic (Messages), compatible, chatgpt (unofficial OAuth), copilot (unofficial OAuth); pinned endpoint, own key only, `redirect:\"error\"`, receipts in `<ws>/.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl`, spending limits (usage.ts).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:20:- Trust boundaries: disclosure gate = `disclosureClass` (providers.ts:181) -> `classifyDestination` (egress.ts:107) string-based; cloud destinations require authorization (client.ts:509-520); every outbound body passes `InformationFlowBoundary.evaluateEgress`. Credentials: env -> `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json` (0600, atomic, credentials.ts:68-75) -> other clients' files read-only.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:21:- Failure model: client classifies every failure into kind/condition/execution (client.ts:184-197, provider_recovery.ts:91-131); client does no retry except (i) param-drop 400 retry, (ii) one OAuth refresh on 401, (iii) gateway-token reload on 401, (iv) immediate failover only when NOT_EXECUTED+temporary, (v) empty-stream non-stream re-request. Waiting/backoff/replay is in ProviderRecoveryController (provider_recovery.ts:277-384): 20 min deadline, 1-15 s jittered backoff, Retry-After honoured, probe (`GET /models`) before UNKNOWN replay, max 2 UNKNOWN replays.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:22:- Capability discovery (client.ts:939-965, provider_capabilities.ts): `/models` entry -> gateway (`limits_version`, `/v1/tokenize`) or vLLM `max_model_len`; otherwise operator `--context-limit` or 65536/8192 client defaults. `/tokenize` only for gateway advertisements.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:28:| PRV-01 | S2 | config / cloud credentials | cli/src/config.ts:36-39 (cwd `.env` loaded with `override:true`, no key filter) | RUNTIME R2: a project `.env` with `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0` turns a self-signed-cert rejection into HTTP 200 with the Authorization header delivered. | Opening an untrusted repo silently disables TLS verification for every later fetch, including cloud API keys/OAuth tokens -> MITM credential theft. Same channel sets LOCAL_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS, recovery policy, provider key vars (credentials.ts:243 reads live env), LOCAL_LLM_FALLBACK_ENDPOINTS. | Fix before v1: allowlist the keys a project `.env` may set (endpoint/model/task-class) or load it into a separate map; never let it set `NODE_*`, `*_PROXY`, `HOME`, credential vars. Add regression test. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:30:| PRV-03 | S3 | error reporting / redaction | cli/src/client.ts:1636 (`shown = providerId ? redact+bound : body`); also 903, 1689 | RUNTIME R3: local endpoint 500 with 200 KB body -> InferenceError.message length 200095, contains `sk-ant-api03…` verbatim; agent prints it (agent.ts:4684-4686) and stores it in the failure record. | Huge HTML/proxy error pages flood the terminal/state; secrets echoed by a proxy/gateway reach logs. | Apply the same bound+redact to the legacy path and to listModels/embedding errors. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:33:| PRV-06 | S2 | standalone local inference | core/provider_capabilities.ts:29,72 (only `context_length`/`max_model_len` parsed; default 65536); agent.ts:4684-4689 (CAPACITY_REJECTED ends the turn) | SOURCE; INFERENCE on server behaviour: LM Studio `/v1/models` and llama.cpp `/v1/models` do not carry `max_model_len`, so standalone sizing is the 65536 default unless `--context-limit` is set. | On LM Studio/llama.cpp with a smaller loaded context the first large turn fails with a context error instead of compacting; user must know `--context-limit`. | Release-required: discover llama.cpp `/props` n_ctx and LM Studio `/api/v0/models` loaded context, or on CAPACITY_REJECTED compact and retry once with an actionable message. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:34:| PRV-07 | S3 | failure classification | core/provider_recovery.ts:82,106 | RUNTIME R1: llama.cpp body (`type: exceed_context_size_error`, \"exceeds the available context size\") -> REQUEST_REJECTED; vLLM body -> CAPACITY_REJECTED. | llama.cpp overflow not recognised as capacity (no `capabilitiesStale`, wrong guidance). | Add `exceed_context_size_error` and /context size/ to capacity rules. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:36:| PRV-09 | S3 | empty stream | client.ts:1472-1476 (re-request), 1118-1135 (non-stream payload has no `max_tokens`) | RUNTIME R1 `empty`: chatHits=2, nonStream=1. Covered by provider_recovery test 16 (intentional). | A server that streams an empty completion is executed twice; the second request is uncapped on local endpoints (runaway generation possible). | Keep but send the same `max_tokens`; record it as a second execution in receipts/UI. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:37:| PRV-10 | S3 | timeouts | client.ts:744-747, 1627-1630 | SOURCE + RUNTIME (stall aborted at 1519 ms with LOCAL_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=1500). | Single 900 s whole-request timeout: a stalled stream blocks 15 min; a legitimate >15 min local generation is killed and classified timeout/UNKNOWN -> replayed up to 2x (provider_recovery.ts:331-337). | Add idle (inter-chunk) and first-byte timeouts; make total timeout optional. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:38:| PRV-11 | S4 | homelab assumptions | client.ts:63-69 (`~/.config/opencode/t5820-client-token`), providers.ts:161 + client.ts:644-647 (X-Task-Class to every endpoint), client.ts:947 (`X-Nexus-Purpose`), CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md (`/model appliance engineering/b0`) | SOURCE | Harmless for standalone (token scoped to config.env origin; servers ignore headers) but homelab names leak into product/docs. | Rename/genericise before v1 docs; make gateway token path configurable. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:40:| PRV-13 | S4 | config | client.ts:785-793 (`addFallbackEndpoint` always appends /v1, ignores provider/pin) | SOURCE | Inconsistent with constructor normalisation; could add a fallback to a pinned provider connection if called. | Reuse normalizeEp + pin check. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:44:| PRV-17 | S4 | docs | docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md Limitations (\"No model catalog cache\") vs model_catalog.ts:51,86; Credentials (\"error bodies are bounded and redacted\") true only for provider connections (PRV-03); Authority claim (PRV-02); USER_MANUAL.md:3 \"direct parity with OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code\" | DOC-CLAIM vs SOURCE | Docs overstate guarantees. | Correct docs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:54:err-frame ERR provider_error_frame TEMPORARILY_UNAVAILABLE    drop ERR network_error (UND_ERR_SOCKET other side closed)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:79:- Positive completion evidence required before any tool call runs: Chat Completions needs finish_reason or [DONE] (client.ts:1436-1443); Anthropic needs message_stop and all blocks closed (anthropic.ts:218); Responses needs response.completed and completed function_call items (openai_responses.ts:101,152). RUNTIME R1 (no-finish -> stream_incomplete) + TEST (cloud_providers \"stream cut inside a tool call\").\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:82:- Cancellation propagates: AbortSignal combined with timeout on all inference fetches (client.ts:1627-1630), reader cancelled on error; RUNTIME R1 slow-abort -> `aborted` in 327 ms; recovery sleep/probe cancellable (provider_recovery.ts:203-219, 356-370).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:83:- Well-specified failure taxonomy and bounded recovery: NOT_EXECUTED vs UNKNOWN, Retry-After/retry-after-ms/x-ratelimit-reset parsing, 20 min deadline, max 2 UNKNOWN replays, probe before replay, iteration bound (provider_recovery.ts). TEST provider_recovery 23/23, provider_recovery_agent 15/15.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:84:- Credential scoping: stored gateway token bound to config.env origin; provider keys bound to provider origin; no cross-provider borrowing; redirects refused on provider connections; credentials.json 0600 atomic write; other clients' tokens never refreshed. TEST credential_boundary 4/4, credential_home 1/1, cloud_providers, provider_connect 12/12.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:85:- Project `.env` cannot select a cloud provider / base URL (config.ts:53-63, 66-72); TEST cloud_providers.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:86:- Standalone default works without the gateway: default endpoint `http://localhost:1234/v1` (config.ts:12; tracked cli/.env = LM Studio defaults, key \"local\"); `/tokenize`, admission headers and gateway advertisement are optional and absent-safe (provider_capabilities.ts:184-195; client.ts:977). TEST provider_capabilities \"standalone\" case.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.