{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:40:29.638Z","ordinal":419748,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17e73-0546-7d30-85d3-ff769cbca249","call_id":"call_4c399dc21a564d4499f7046dd8235931","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT1: {\"chunk_id\":\"0269d4\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000028075,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":6684,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6684)\\nTotal output lines: 80\\n\\nrg: docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:5:**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** There are 31 blocker requirements, none of them met. Task-quality, standalone and real-terminal qualification are **unverified**: no qualifying evidence exists yet. The contest entry was submitted, is frozen, and is tracked separately.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:28:| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:46:4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:43:| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:46:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:113:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:122:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:134:4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:149:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:153:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:331:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:36:| REQ-AGT-31..39 | CTX-003..011 | Durable vs retrieved distinction; role policy; budget vs actual route capacity, fail closed (`ContextBudgetError`); cross-boundary failover re-admission; same-boundary failover cheap; compaction removes only disposable; admission evidence; resume≠recovery; manual==auto compaction semantics | P2 §12 | DEMONSTRATED / SBIS (CTX-006: client.ts executeWithFailover; egress.test) | P (WP05 qual for CTX-006) | 10-12 I-05 (provider context-length 400 ends turn), CTX-02 (steering truncated after compaction; fixed ee70f68), d88a897 false-absence; 10-13 compaction ledger self-assessed only |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:74:| REQ-AGT-53 | Compaction A–D | No default step/time ceiling; state-aware repetition; durable compaction commit (archive→task→session, fsync); queued `/compact`; provider-advertised capacity; labelled token counts | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md; reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md | \\\"Met\\\"/\\\"Met (scripted)\\\"; 1 completed live run (run 3, REGRESSION_FREE); **\\\"Independent acceptance is pending\\\"** (ledger line 3) | **N** |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:75:| REQ-PRV-11 | Standalone | Works identically without homelab-ai gateway; counting optional; labelled estimates | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:7-9; handoff doc | \\\"Accepted under scripted evidence\\\"; **no live run against LM Studio/llama.cpp/vLLM standalone** (ledger \\\"Not done\\\"; release notes Known limits) | N |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:129:| HIST-04 | S2 | Extensions, standalone | cli/src/plugins.ts:47-54 | SOURCE: home plugin dirs include `~/.config/opencode/plugins` — every `*.js/*.mjs` there is imported in-process at turn start; USER_MANUAL.md:295 lists only `~/.config/nexus/`, `~/.nexus/` | Another product's plugins execute inside Nexus with full authority, undocumented | Remove the opencode dir or make it opt-in + documented |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:133:| HIST-08 | S2 | Standalone local inference | reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md \\\"Not done\\\"; docs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:33 | DOC-CLAIM: all live evidence is homelab gateway (llama.cpp behind aihost). No live run on plain LM Studio/vLLM/llama.cpp/Ollama although quickstart's first-run path is LM Studio | Primary documented setup unqualified | v1 must include live standalone qualification on ≥2 servers |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:195:| REQ-PRV-V1-01 | Live standalone qualification on ≥2 non-homelab OpenAI-compatible servers | HIST-08; standalone requirement | BLOCKER | Recorded runs with manifest; T2 subset pass ≥ pre-registered threshold |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:229:| Live standalone run; live capacity/worker-change observation; live TUI `/compact` queue | compaction ledger \\\"Not done\\\" | Not done | Open |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:231:| Live qualification of openai, anthropic, copilot, compatible providers | CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE | Not run | Open |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:237:- **Supported workflows:** interactive Ratatui TUI (`nexus`), REPL (`nexus repl`, `--approve`), headless `nexus run` with JSON/exit codes (0 verified, 2 REGRESSION_FREE), resume (`-r`, `/resume`), `nexus doctor`, `nexus trust`, providers/connect, `/team` and `nexus operation` durable multi-unit work, checkpoints/undo, MCP client + `serve-mcp`, skills/plugins, eval.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:239:- **homelab-ai:** optional gateway (capability discovery, tokenize, admitted-count headers); Nexus must and claims to work standalone; standalone proven only by scripted fixtures.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:9:…3184 tokens truncated…whose `name`/`tool`/`action` is an offered tool is executed. Examples: \\\"an agent would normally call {\\\"name\\\":\\\"run_command\\\",...} but I did not\\\" → `run_command rm -rf build` executed. A model quoting a file that contains `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_file\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"path\\\":\\\"/etc/shadow\\\"}}` in a json fence → executed. The few-shot exemplars teach exactly this fenced format. The parser falls back to text even when the provider supports native tool calls. | Prompt-injection amplifier: content the model merely echoes becomes an action, unapproved by default (SEC-01). | RELEASE-REQUIRED: enable text-embedded parsing only for connections without native tool calling (capability flag). Restrict it to `<tool_call>` tags or a sole fenced block that makes up the whole reply. Never parse prose `{…}`. Add negative tests. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:62:| VER-11 | S4 | Malformed native tool_calls | parser.ts:336-345 | RUNTIME (probe P4). A `tool_calls` entry without `function` throws a TypeError from `parseModelResponse`. The call at agent.ts:4701 is not wrapped, so the error propagates out of runTurn (see AGT-08). Unknown native tool names pass through to dispatch. | A turn crashes on one malformed provider frame. | Validate the shape and drop invalid entries with a notice to the model. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:118:- Admission uses exact provider counts when advertised, with calibration and a strict mode (agent.ts:2236-2300).\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:145:| R-VER-12 | Malformed provider tool_calls never crash a turn. | failure | RELEASE-REQUIRED | parseModelResponse with `[{id:\\\"a\\\"}]` returns 0 calls and a notice. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:25:| cli/src/protocol.ts | targeted (providerRecoveryNotice 306-325) |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:62:| TUI-06 | S2 | Onboarding / unreachable endpoint | protocol.ts:306-315; startup screen | RUNTIME s1a: endpoint 127.0.0.1:9 -> startup shows no endpoint status; first prompt loops \\\"Inference provider temporarily unavailable (network_error); waiting Ns ... Work is preserved.\\\" 7x in 28s, no endpoint URL, no fix hint (`nexus doctor`, LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT, `/connect`), no bound seen | New user with wrong/absent endpoint sees an indefinite wait without actionable guidance | Probe endpoint at session start; error text names endpoint + `nexus doctor`; bound recovery for never-reachable endpoints (coordinate with provider scope) |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:97:TUI-06 (`s1_startup.py`, LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9/v1): screen at 28s shows 7× \\\"Inference provider temporarily\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:98:unavailable (network_error); waiting {1,1,3,5,9,8,8}s before checking again.\\\" + footer \\\"waiting for the inference provider\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:99:0:27\\\"; Ctrl-C -> \\\"Provider recovery cancelled … ◌ Cancelled  You stopped the turn during provider wait.\\\"\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:146:| TUI-R5 | Unreachable/misconfigured endpoint is reported at startup with endpoint, cause and fix (`nexus doctor`, config path), and a never-reachable provider ends the turn with guidance within a bounded time | onboarding/failure (TUI-06) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | s1a: startup screen names endpoint as unreachable; turn ends ≤ N min with guidance text |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/BRIEF.md:6:Product: Nexus Code = local coding client/harness. TypeScript agent + sidecar (cli/), Rust harness-core tools + Ratatui nexus-tui (core/). Local inference (OpenAI-compatible: vLLM/LM Studio/llama.cpp, homelab \\\"gateway\\\" at 10.0.8.5) is first class; cloud providers optional. Must work standalone without homelab-ai.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:23:| cli/src/operation_cli.ts, provider_cli.ts | command names only (grep). The doctor redaction path was exercised at RUNTIME. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:15:| src/core/provider_recovery.ts | full read |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:30:- `AutonomousAgent.runTurn` (agent.ts:4254-4995) is the single main loop. Per step: steering drain (4450) -> capability refresh (4555) -> `admitWithFindings` (compaction ladder + model-written findings, 2767) -> `measureAdmission` (provider token count, 2237) -> `ProviderRecoveryController.run` around streaming inference (4614) -> parse -> tool dispatch (parallel only if every call is in `READ_ONLY_TOOLS`, 4800; else sequential with approval) -> `observe` into `ExecutionTracker` -> `endStep` (progress evaluation + durable `persistProgress`).\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:48:| AGT-05 | S3 | Duplicated subagent loop | agent.ts:5298-5431 vs 4401-4915 | SOURCE. Second loop diverges: no `refreshCapabilities`/`measureAdmission` (provider token counting, strict counting ignored), no empty-reply retry (first empty reply = \\\"stopped without a report\\\"), no backoff for polls, no steering, offers `[...HARNESS_TOOLS, read_findings]` (all tool groups, no MCP/plugin) while parsing against `getEffectiveTools()` names (5362) — offered and accepted tool sets differ; no cancellation-record semantics for in-flight tools. | Behaviour of delegated work differs subtly from main turns; context/strict-count guarantees don't hold inside subagents. | Refactor to one step function shared by both loops (RELEASE-REQUIRED or documented limitation). |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:57:| AGT-14 | S4 | Swallowed durable-write errors | agent.ts:4022-4032, 4051-4058, 3836-3840, 3853-3867, 4240-4243, 1182-1185 | SOURCE. `recordOperationStart/End`, plan/requirements checkpoints, provider-recovery checkpoints `catch {}` silently (unlike `persistProgress`, which reports once). Failure of `recordOperationStart` removes crash detection of an in-flight tool without telling anyone. | Recovery may miss an interrupted tool. | Route through the same reported-failure path. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:79:- No default cumulative step ceiling: `DEFAULT_CONTINUATION.maxTotalSteps/maxTurnMinutes = +Infinity` (types.ts:127-133); `maxSteps` is a segment/checkpoint (agent.ts:4379-4381, 4435-4445). Step-position notices only appear under an operator-set limit (`stepPosition`, 766; `stepNotedContent` 2932-2933). Subagents have no step allowance; model-supplied `max_steps` ignored (3584-3585). Recovery/iteration bounds that remain (provider `maxIterations` 1000, operation runner 10 000, compaction attempts 5) are resource-safety valves with explicit reasons, not completion substitutes.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:84:- Provider recovery separates waiting/probing from replay; UNKNOWN execution replayed at most `maxUnknownReplays` after a probe; NOT_EXECUTED can yield to the scheduler (provider_recovery.ts).\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:10:  open-ended \\\"Inference provider temporarily unavailable (network_error); waiting Ns\\\" loop (28s+, 7 retries) with no\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:12:  stopped the turn during provider wait\\\"). Continuation lines \\\"Work is preserved.\\\" wrap to column 0 (not indented).\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT2: {\"chunk_id\":\"6545b4\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000028436,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1295,\"output\":\"--- .git/nexus-claims/GATEWAY/owner.json\\n{\\n  \\\"agent\\\": \\\"/root\\\",\\n  \\\"host\\\": \\\"mike-dev\\\",\\n  \\\"branch\\\": \\\"v1/rc10-terminal-manual-xterm\\\",\\n  \\\"base\\\": \\\"16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0\\\",\\n  \\\"since\\\": \\\"2026-10-27T13:23:35Z\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": \\\"operator-led installed RC10 manual terminal cell xterm 80x24 using pinned OpenRouter; synthetic scratch workspace only; no held-out content; release when this cell stops\\\"\\n}\\n--- .git/nexus-claims/CLOUD/owner.json\\n4659:2026-10-27T02:03:16.248277Z CLAIM GATEWAY /root synthetic RC10 approval-overlay timing repro; local mock only\\n4660:2026-10-27T02:03:49Z RECOVERED agent=/root host=mike-dev boot_id=8928bf1f-8ae0-441b-8070-f05ef8823a5e worktree=/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-scripted-terminal branch=v1/rc10-scripted-terminal head=5bf40f4f79cac92f85543e4c89422cbf897ee6b9 pr=none claims=SUITE,GATEWAY,FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc10_overlay_states interrupted=Detail-probe-processes-absent; dryrun6-captured-8-of-9-overlays; later-Detail-harness-attempts-stopped-at-synthetic-command-approval next=archive-supplemental-evidence-update-readiness-commit-local-only; no-power-loss-claim\\n4662:2026-10-27T02:03:49Z RELEASE GATEWAY agent=/root outcome=synthetic localhost mock-only probes complete; no provider inference used\\n4665:2026-10-27T02:06:21Z CLAIMS agent=/root host=mike-dev boot_id=8928bf1f-8ae0-441b-8070-f05ef8823a5e branch=v1/rc10-scripted-terminal head=4eea8160428be89a1ce78d72f8184104cd35c3f4 SUITE,GATEWAY scope=bounded_installed_RC10_synthetic_local_mock_cancellation_timing_comparison\\n4669:2026-10-27T02:08:44Z RELEASE GATEWAY agent=/root result=synthetic_localhost_mock_only; no_provider_inference_or_heldout_payloads\\n4671:2026-10-27T02:09:51Z CLAIMS agent=/root branch=v1/rc10-scripted-terminal head=d00e1cbad6da4b3ec288097da292a1cd13f3753b SUITE,GATEWAY scope=one installed_RC10_synthetic_approval_flow_continuation_to_Detail_overlay\\n4675:2026-10-27T02:12:06Z RELEASE GATEWAY agent=/root result=localhost synthetic mock only; no provider or held-out use\\n4679:2026-10-27T02:17:19+00:00 RECOVERY: released unused SUITE and GATEWAY claims for RC10 overlay matrix; matrix was not started because FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc10_terminal_scripted was actively owned for PR264 checksum/gateway attribution correction. Observed owner status: committed, checksummed, pushed to PR #264 for review/CI. No files in its dirty worktree were changed by this recovery action.\\n4682:2026-10-27T02:34:25+00:00 RECOVERY OBSERVATION: RC10 OpenRouter task on ubuntu-desktop, under existing CLOUD/GATEWAY and RC10_OPENROUTER_E5_20261027 claims, is terminal, not live. Local SSH PID 4123001 disappeared; remote /proc scan found no surviving nexus-rc10-qualification process. Retained /tmp/nexus-rc10-openrouter-live-task-supported-20261027/run.json (sha256 a4628d77dbab686a51ae895e267dffb9eae3e55b60d7f6f105120eb259b78e94) and run.stderr (sha256 5efbc86f08afde86322e575384858ef9e53c1e715872395f27aecfd4589710ac). Sanitized result: process completed exit 2, success=false, turn outcome/reason REGRESSION_FREE, configured verifier reports PASSED, but unverifiedChangesPending=true and validationReceipts empty; synthetic workspace has modified src/slug.py and untracked src/__pycache__. Classify E5 task as INCOMPLETE, not pass. No output/log content or held-out payload read; no remote files changed or removed.\\n4711:2026-10-27T04:13:39Z RELEASE GATEWAY /root v1/rc10-provider-verify; exact RC10 OpenRouter provider verification and synthetic live-task evidence recorded in PR #265, merged into main at 14a9c15297c3c50dd8fbda86e34aeae447bb5a5d; no held-out qualification claimed.\\n4853:2026-10-27T14:30Z CANDIDATE_PREP UPDATE_PLAN_TURN_REGRESSION branch=v1/update-plan-turn-regression base=c64499d98f2867fb76f73c1949fcdaf2ad2f83c5 file=cli/test/update_plan_turn_result.test.ts uncommitted test_only=true REDACTED no_test_result no_implementation_edits\\n4879:2026-10-27T14:36:52Z SUITE_AVAILABLE requester=KimiCode-defect-scan owner=/root release_confirmed=true local_test_processes=none reason=safe_boundary; current_GITHUB_CI_isolated=true; GATEWAY_claim=still_held_for_RC10_terminal_no_live_inference_started\\n4912:2026-10-27T16:54:00Z claim /root CLOUD v1/rc10-openrouter-qualification-20261027 exact installed RC10 pinned OpenRouter verify and synthetic live task\\n4915:2026-10-27T17:02:00Z update /root CLOUD preserve failed attempt; retry only in fresh clean committed synthetic baseline\\n4918:2026-10-27T17:06:14Z HANDOFF CLOUD RC10 E5 reconciliation: exact v1.0.0-rc.10 installed in isolated prefix /home/mike/.local/nexus-rc10-qualification; archive SHA-256 444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7, revision 16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0, installer required attestation verification and completed successfully. Existing merged PR265 evidence already satisfies OpenRouter provider verify and one correct synthetic live task on this exact tag/archive; verified README, receipts, and pass record on origin/main. Current duplicate attempt remains incomplete and preserved; no retry/spend needed. Remote task process confirmed exited; CLOUD claim released.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT3: {\"chunk_id\":\"24a4ea\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000036518,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":41,\"output\":\"rg: docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10: IO error for operation on docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793122829.6385763}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
