{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:41:01.455Z","ordinal":419776,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e56f6803-87dc-42d4-80b8-355978ca70a6","process_id":"23327","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","cat docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md && cat docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/SHA256SUMS && sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-readiness-20261027","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/SHA256SUMS","name":"SHA256SUMS","path":"docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/SHA256SUMS"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# RC10 OpenRouter provider verification\n\nDisposition: `PASS` for the three provider verification checks performed against the exact installed RC10 artifact. This does not by itself establish provider live-task acceptance; see `../openrouter-live-task/README.md`.\n\n- Candidate: `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source commit `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`.\n- Installed RC10 reported `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)` on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`).\n- Provider/model: OpenRouter, `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`.\n- Result time: `2026-10-27T02:27:10.627Z`.\n- Passed checks: streamed completion, tool call, and tool-result round trip.\n- Three provider receipts are preserved in `openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl`; each records the exact model and provider-reported cost `$0`.\n- Verification JSON and receipt hashes: `3b14fdc568ca9daa6f10582e090bbab447ab230a4aae42d24dac95166374e88e` and `de74a7052f03a63faddacc2dc8bb1cd0288328d633ed203ceecd4d3e0737d9e1`.\n\nThese records cover the provider verification path only. The synthetic task and its failed attempts are separately documented, and all held-out, long-task, fault-injection, terminal, cross-runner, independent acceptance, and stable-release gates remain outside this result.\nb5b3bfd365ab950aad840889fde2947673710b790906a931456439935975c313  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md\nde74a7052f03a63faddacc2dc8bb1cd0288328d633ed203ceecd4d3e0737d9e1  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl\n3b14fdc568ca9daa6f10582e090bbab447ab230a4aae42d24dac95166374e88e  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json\n# RC10 human terminal acceptance worksheet\n\n**Status: PENDING HUMAN EXECUTION.** This is a blank worksheet. No terminal matrix cell has been run or accepted by this document.\n\n## Candidate identity to verify on the operator host\n\n- Tag: `v1.0.0-rc.10`\n- Full source commit: `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`\n- Linux x86_64 archive: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.10.tar.gz`\n- Published archive SHA-256: `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`\n- Release: https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10\n\nThe operator must install the published artifact on the host used for this matrix, then record the installed `nexus --version`, archive digest, installation location, host, and UTC time below. Do not use a checkout build or a different RC.\n\n| Operator record | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Operator | |\n| UTC date/time | |\n| Host OS and version | |\n| Installed artifact location | |\n| Installed archive filename | |\n| Installed archive SHA-256 | |\n| `nexus --version` output | |\n| xterm version | |\n| kitty version and keyboard protocol state | |\n| tmux version / GNOME Terminal host version | |\n| VS Code version / integrated terminal profile | |\n| GNOME Terminal version | |\n| Evidence directory | |\n\n## Run procedure for every cell\n\nFollow [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](../../../../../v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3) against the installed candidate at the exact terminal and size listed in the row.\n\n1. Launch Nexus and confirm the live TUI appears.\n2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste three lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm terminal echo and display restore without stray escape codes.\n7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n\nFor each row, attach a genuine screenshot of the approval panel and a genuine screenshot of the restored post-exit terminal. Record exact observations, commands where applicable, and any failure disposition. Automated PTY evidence does not fill these manual rows.\n\n## Terminal × size matrix\n\nEach cell remains pending until the operator performs the procedure and records both screenshots. Mark exactly one verdict per cell.\n\n| # | Terminal | Size | Verdict | Evidence / result reference | Approval screenshot | Post-exit screenshot | Notes / failure disposition |\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | PENDING | | | | |\n\n## Operator disposition\n\n- Completed cells: `0 / 15`\n- Overall result: `PENDING`\n- Operator acceptance and UTC timestamp: __________________________________\n- Open failures or limitations: ___________________________________________\n\nDo not change the overall result to PASS until all 15 cells contain operator verdicts and the required screenshot references, then apply the acceptance rules in `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":662313024}},"started_at_ms":1793122860792,"completed_at_ms":1793122861455}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:41:02.493Z","ordinal":419777,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17e73-859d-7e20-a198-4d6910786c15","call_id":"call_73ada17459b5409eba6e42710724cae1","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# RC10 OpenRouter provider verification\n\nDisposition: `PASS` for the three provider verification checks performed against the exact installed RC10 artifact. This does not by itself establish provider live-task acceptance; see `../openrouter-live-task/README.md`.\n\n- Candidate: `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source commit `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`.\n- Installed RC10 reported `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)` on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`).\n- Provider/model: OpenRouter, `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`.\n- Result time: `2026-10-27T02:27:10.627Z`.\n- Passed checks: streamed completion, tool call, and tool-result round trip.\n- Three provider receipts are preserved in `openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl`; each records the exact model and provider-reported cost `$0`.\n- Verification JSON and receipt hashes: `3b14fdc568ca9daa6f10582e090bbab447ab230a4aae42d24dac95166374e88e` and `de74a7052f03a63faddacc2dc8bb1cd0288328d633ed203ceecd4d3e0737d9e1`.\n\nThese records cover the provider verification path only. The synthetic task and its failed attempts are separately documented, and all held-out, long-task, fault-injection, terminal, cross-runner, independent acceptance, and stable-release gates remain outside this result.\nb5b3bfd365ab950aad840889fde2947673710b790906a931456439935975c313  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md\nde74a7052f03a63faddacc2dc8bb1cd0288328d633ed203ceecd4d3e0737d9e1  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl\n3b14fdc568ca9daa6f10582e090bbab447ab230a4aae42d24dac95166374e88e  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json\n# RC10 human terminal acceptance worksheet\n\n**Status: PENDING HUMAN EXECUTION.** This is a blank worksheet. No terminal matrix cell has been run or accepted by this document.\n\n## Candidate identity to verify on the operator host\n\n- Tag: `v1.0.0-rc.10`\n- Full source commit: `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`\n- Linux x86_64 archive: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.10.tar.gz`\n- Published archive SHA-256: `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`\n- Release: https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10\n\nThe operator must install the published artifact on the host used for this matrix, then record the installed `nexus --version`, archive digest, installation location, host, and UTC time below. Do not use a checkout build or a different RC.\n\n| Operator record | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Operator | |\n| UTC date/time | |\n| Host OS and version | |\n| Installed artifact location | |\n| Installed archive filename | |\n| Installed archive SHA-256 | |\n| `nexus --version` output | |\n| xterm version | |\n| kitty version and keyboard protocol state | |\n| tmux version / GNOME Terminal host version | |\n| VS Code version / integrated terminal profile | |\n| GNOME Terminal version | |\n| Evidence directory | |\n\n## Run procedure for every cell\n\nFollow [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](../../../../../v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3) against the installed candidate at the exact terminal and size listed in the row.\n\n1. Launch Nexus and confirm the live TUI appears.\n2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste three lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm terminal echo and display restore without stray escape codes.\n7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n\nFor each row, attach a genuine screenshot of the approval panel and a genuine screenshot of the restored post-exit terminal. Record exact observations, commands where applicable, and any failure disposition. Automated PTY evidence does not fill these manual rows.\n\n## Terminal × size matrix\n\nEach cell remains pending until the operator performs the procedure and records both screenshots. Mark exactly one verdict per cell.\n\n| # | Terminal | Size | Verdict | Evidence / result reference | Approval screenshot | Post-exit screenshot | Notes / failure disposition |\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | PENDING | | | | |\n| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | PENDING | | | | |\n\n## Operator disposition\n\n- Completed cells: `0 / 15`\n- Overall result: `PENDING`\n- Operator acceptance and UTC timestamp: __________________________________\n- Open failures or limitations: ___________________________________________\n\nDo not change the overall result to PASS until all 15 cells contain operator verdicts and the required screenshot references, then apply the acceptance rules in `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1