1-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a17ded-e7ae-7300-8479-0fca92a43367","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_user_login"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e1affbf081a0a8a73b169f34d85a","order":20374,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17e71-9987-7f71-8993-9cfde97a0528","text":"The last turn advanced the readiness record, but its CI snapshot may now be stale. I’m refreshing the live PR checks and owner/custody state before selecting the next safe action.","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e1cd62a481a0af155b89b26d11f4","order":20375,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17e72-0d16-7901-8df5-019e5012eed6","text":"The readiness update was pushed to PR #268 as `2cf9e994` by the owner/coordinator process; I verified the branch ancestry and that it preserves the earlier commit. Its new exact-head Node 22/24 checks are still pending, while CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript pass. #276 and #277 Linux jobs also remain active; I’m not altering their claimed files.","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e1d67ab881a0a7fe3099b4194535","order":20376,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17e72-30a6-7070-9698-09fd61b19238","text":"PR #277 has not changed since the review comment, while its owner’s claim remains active and may be running in another process namespace. I’m sending a safe-boundary status request asking whether the two findings are being addressed or need an explicit handoff; I will not edit its claimed files without that handoff.","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e208d3d881a08c7fdd8e5a01b28b","order":20377,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17e72-f5bc-77a0-a656-e469893519b5","text":"While CI runs, I found one possible independent lane: RC10’s existing provider bundle covers OpenRouter, while broader provider/standalone qualification is still listed as incomplete. I’m checking the approved E5 contract and claims before deciding whether another exact-RC10 provider run can proceed safely without interfering with the paused terminal cell.","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e2c16c3c81a099b2338628093573","order":20378,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17e75-c417-7a43-83de-b554b1e09a9d","text":"The approved provider matrix explicitly requires a ChatGPT sign-in verification repeated on the installed RC; RC10 currently has only the OpenRouter row evidenced. The current host has the exact RC10 launcher (`16ee8ca`) and the isolated test workspace can use a read-only link to the existing Codex sign-in file without exposing its contents. I’ll claim the small-spend cloud lane and run the three-step, workspace-free verification with bounded request/token limits.","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e2d56ee081a0ad5f3f02fec1fc7a","order":20379,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17e76-1405-7fb0-816f-4f70848dcf3b","text":"The first RC10 ChatGPT verification attempt stopped before any provider request (exit 2, no verification JSON). I’m inspecting its sanitized setup error and will correct the isolated invocation if the failure is environmental; this attempt remains preserved and does not count as qualification.","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e2fea49881a0b60359fca9441cf2","order":20380,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17e76-b7a5-7413-9e91-9982c7188c27","text":"The verification never reached ChatGPT: RC10’s startup halted on an invalid upgrade journal in its install prefix. I’m checking only the journal’s metadata and structural validation conditions, plus whether an upgrade process is active. I won’t run recovery or alter the installation while the cause is unclear; a clean isolated RC10 setup may let the provider check proceed independently.","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e34b105c81a0a0093f3955b7461f","order":20381,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17e77-e086-7e73-8751-44e2460c22b3","text":"The host’s installed RC10 package is exact, but its shared upgrade journal is valid only under the original user home, so the isolated verification process rejected it before contacting the provider. I’ve confirmed the official RC10 archive digest from GitHub and will use a fresh isolated install of that same published artifact for the required provider check, preserving the existing install and its journal untouched.","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":20382,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted c