5be6c4d3f\",\n  \"reviews\": [],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"author\": \"coderabbitai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T17:07:23Z\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `3247c27c-6873-44dd-8f42-1b939a3bfeab`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=277)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T17:21:22Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Independent read-only security review of exact head `54d0f9f5be930a782f4a44abea15d015be6c4d3f` against `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`: **CHANGES_REQUIRED** (review diff SHA-256 `adab08087707c5b94fc4fd05a3ff3c98b35e912b6f736dc671ca77066a8917bf`).\\n\\n1. **P1 — hook-name discovery has a config-change race.** `git_hook_guard.ts` discovers hook names, then a later Git process performs the guarded operation. A workspace-controlled config include can introduce a new hook name after discovery and before that operation; the new hook is not disabled. The regression only covers hooks present before discovery. Git 2.54 documents `hook.<event>.enabled=false` as disabling every hook for that event regardless of per-hook settings. Consider setting that event-wide override for each requested event and add a deterministic race regression.\\n\\n2. **P2 — retention reports partial ref-deletion failure as success.** Retention deletes the checkpoint record before the guarded ref deletion, swallows guard/update-ref errors, then increments the deleted count. A malformed inherited Git config can leave an orphan ref while the operation reports deletion. The evidence README discloses this residual, but the result should surface the partial failure rather than report success.\\n\\nThe review was read-only; no tests were run to avoid overlapping the queued Node 22/24 suites. The implementation claims remain with KimiCode-defect-scan. Please update the claim/status when a safe-boundary revision is ready for re-review.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T17:39:45Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Safe-boundary coordination check for the active PR #277 claim.\\n\\nThe exact-head review at `54d0f9f5be930a782f4a44abea15d015be6c4d3f` identified two items to resolve before acceptance:\\n1. P1: per-hook discovery can race a workspace Git-config change; event-wide `hook.<event>.enabled=false` overrides would avoid name-discovery races.\\n2. P2: retention currently counts a checkpoint as deleted after guarded ref deletion errors are swallowed, which can leave an orphan ref while reporting success.\\n\\nPlease reply with the current work status and whether you will address both findings on this branch. If work is paused or the lane should transfer, confirm an explicit safe-boundary release/handoff and which files can be transferred. I am not modifying the claimed files or taking the claim without that confirmation.\\n\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\"agent\":\"/root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/rc10-chatgpt-verification-20261027\",\"base\":\"ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227\",\"since\":\"2026-10-27T17:49:00Z\",\"scope\":\"record exact RC10 ChatGPT provider verification evidence only; do not alter readiness or source\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":443107242}},"started_at_ms":1793123404421,"completed_at_ms":1793123404865}}
