{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:51:59.023Z","ordinal":420329,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e4be12d481a0b7c10f419296b06a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_3a6fd85fdc56430bb121803e27502f80","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -l 'defect-retention-configured-hooks-current|core_retention|git_hook_guard' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims --glob 'owner.json' | while read f; do echo ===$f; cat \\\"$f\\\"; done; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code log -1 --format='%H %cI %s' origin/main; gh pr view 277 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json body | jq -r '.body' | head -40\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1000}); text(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793123518.0756724}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:51:59.100Z","ordinal":420330,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e4bc8f2481a0ad01297c6916dc72","usage":{"input_tokens":99107,"cached_input_tokens":97408,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":241,"reasoning_output_tokens":89,"total_tokens":99348},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":11943979,"cached_input_tokens":11821568,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":49164,"reasoning_output_tokens":31308,"total_tokens":11993143},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7737803871,"cached_input_tokens":7655274624,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":22122569,"reasoning_output_tokens":12808803,"total_tokens":7759926440}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:52:00.572Z","ordinal":420331,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a1755672-1fd0-4dfe-b707-bb180e69dee0","process_id":"58992","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -l 'defect-retention-configured-hooks-current|core_retention|git_hook_guard' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims --glob 'owner.json' | while read f; do echo ===$f; cat \"$f\"; done; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code log -1 --format='%H %cI %s' origin/main; gh pr view 277 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json body | jq -r '.body' | head -40"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -l 'defect-retention-configured-hooks-current|core_retention|git_hook_guard' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims --glob 'owner.json' | while read f; do echo ===$f; cat \"$f\"; done; git -C /home/mike/nexus-code log -1 --format='%H %cI %s' origin/main; gh pr view 277 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json body | jq -r '.body' | head -40"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"7a860c091297abc13371d92ae9633a9f06d67f7a 2026-10-27T13:49:27-04:00 Merge pull request #277 from mikeholownych/v1/defect-retention-configured-hooks-current\n## Defect\n\nGit 2.54 added hooks declared in repository config (`hook.<name>.event` / `.command`). They are **not** disabled by `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`, so a workspace-controlled config could execute code during:\n\n- retention checkpoint ref deletion (`reference-transaction`),\n- checkpoint creation (`reference-transaction` from ref updates, `post-index-change` from dirty `git stash create`),\n- checkpoint pruning (`reference-transaction`),\n- checkpoint restore (`reference-transaction` + `post-index-change` from `reset --hard`).\n\nThe earlier retention-only fix used `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`; an inherited `GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS` outranks that channel and could re-enable the hook.\n\n## Fix\n\nNew shared `cli/src/core/git_hook_guard.ts`:\n\n- reads effective `hook.*.event` entries (including `include.path`),\n- appends `hook.<name>.enabled=false` for the requested events to **`GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS`** (Git's own command-line channel, higher precedence than `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`),\n- single-quote shell-quotes keys/values (`'\\''` escaping), preserving friendly names with `=`, spaces or quotes,\n- leaves the environment untouched when no configured hook matches,\n- rethrows a config read failure so callers fail closed.\n\nCall sites pass only the events their command can raise: retention ref deletion; checkpoint create (both events), prune (`reference-transaction`), restore (both). Traditional hooks stay off via the existing `-c core.hooksPath=/dev/null` argv override, which also outranks inherited parameters.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Checkpoint regression (Git 2.54+)**: declares config hooks for both events, proves they fire on raw `git update-ref`/`git stash create`, then asserts create/restore/prune do not run them. Fails against the pre-fix checkpoint source (`checkpoint creation executed a configured hook`); each call site is independently localized by the reviewer (restore-only and prune-only reverts fail their own assertions).\n- **Retention regression** sets an inherited `GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS` re-enable value; the old `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` implementation fails (`gc executed a configured Git hook`), the shared guard passes.\n- Checkpoint + retention suites: **34/34 on Git 2.54.0** and **34/34 on host Git 2.43.0**; `tsc`, `git diff --check` clean.\n- Independent security review **ACCEPT** on `54d0f9f`, including fail-closed probes (injected config-read failure leaves no checkpoint/restore and runs no hook), quoting fuzzing, worktree-scope hooks and inherited config channels. The retention portion (`a3b2d9b`, `a4bcf90`) was also independently ACCEPTed.\n\n## Residual risk\n\n- Configuration-defined hooks exist only on Git versions that support them; older Git keeps the `core.hooksPath` control.\n- Malformed inherited `GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS` makes Git reject the config and the command fails; no hook runs, but checkpoint prune has already unlinked the record, so the ref is orphaned permanently (an orphan-ref sweep is a separate improvement).\n- Inherent TOCTOU: a hook added to config between the guard read and the command is not disabled.\n- Filter drivers (`filter.*` via `.gitattributes`) remain a documented limitation for stash/reset; they are not hooks.\n\nEvidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-SHARED-20261027/`, plus updates to the retention/checkpoint evidence records.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":438067870}},"started_at_ms":1793123520133,"completed_at_ms":1793123520572}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:52:01.597Z","ordinal":420332,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17e7d-943d-7390-82bc-5ab6dbaae619","call_id":"call_3a6fd85fdc56430bb121803e27502f80","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"7a860c091297abc13371d92ae9633a9f06d67f7a 2026-10-27T13:49:27-04:00 Merge pull request #277 from mikeholownych/v1/defect-retention-configured-hooks-current\n## Defect\n\nGit 2.54 added hooks declared in repository config (`hook.<name>.event` / `.command`). They are **not** disabled by `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`, so a workspace-controlled config could execute code during:\n\n- retention checkpoint ref deletion (`reference-transaction`),\n- checkpoint creation (`reference-transaction` from ref updates, `post-index-change` from dirty `git stash create`),\n- checkpoint pruning (`reference-transaction`),\n- checkpoint restore (`reference-transaction` + `post-index-change` from `reset --hard`).\n\nThe earlier retention-only fix used `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`; an inherited `GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS` outranks that channel and could re-enable the hook.\n\n## Fix\n\nNew shared `cli/src/core/git_hook_guard.ts`:\n\n- reads effective `hook.*.event` entries (including `include.path`),\n- appends `hook.<name>.enabled=false` for the requested events to **`GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS`** (Git's own command-line channel, higher precedence than `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`),\n- single-quote shell-quotes keys/values (`'\\''` escaping), preserving friendly names with `=`, spaces or quotes,\n- leaves the environment untouched when no configured hook matches,\n- rethrows a config read failure so callers fail closed.\n\nCall sites pass only the events their command can raise: retention ref deletion; checkpoint create (both events), prune (`reference-transaction`), restore (both). Traditional hooks stay off via the existing `-c core.hooksPath=/dev/null` argv override, which also outranks inherited parameters.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Checkpoint regression (Git 2.54+)**: declares config hooks for both events, proves they fire on raw `git update-ref`/`git stash create`, then asserts create/restore/prune do not run them. Fails against the pre-fix checkpoint source (`checkpoint creation executed a configured hook`); each call site is independently localized by the reviewer (restore-only and prune-only reverts fail their own assertions).\n- **Retention regression** sets an inherited `GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS` re-enable value; the old `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` implementation fails (`gc executed a configured Git hook`), the shared guard passes.\n- Checkpoint + retention suites: **34/34 on Git 2.54.0** and **34/34 on host Git 2.43.0**; `tsc`, `git diff --check` clean.\n- Independent security review **ACCEPT** on `54d0f9f`, including fail-closed probes (injected config-read failure leaves no checkpoint/restore and runs no hook), quoting fuzzing, worktree-scope hooks and inherited config channels. The retention portion (`a3b2d9b`, `a4bcf90`) was also independently ACCEPTed.\n\n## Residual risk\n\n- Configuration-defined hooks exist only on Git versions that support them; older Git keeps the `core.hooksPath` control.\n- Malformed inherited `GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS` makes Git reject the config and the command fails; no hook runs, but checkpoint prune has already unlinked the record, so the ref is orphaned permanently (an orphan-ref sweep is a separate improvement).\n- Inherent TOCTOU: a hook added to config between the guard read and the command is not disabled.\n- Filter drivers (`filter.*` via `.gitattributes`) remain a documented limitation for stash/reset; they are not hooks.\n\nEvidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-SHARED-20261027/`, plus updates to the retention/checkpoint evidence records.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793123521.597057}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
