s/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RETENTION_JSON_METADATA/source-sha256.json\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RETENTION_JSON_METADATA/types.txt\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RETENTION-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-20261027/README.md:5:PR #269 disabled traditional repository hook scripts with `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`. Git 2.54 added named hooks defined in configuration, and those hooks are not disabled by `core.hooksPath`. The first 2.54 regression confirmed that a `reference-transaction` configuration hook still ran during checkpoint ref deletion even with `hooksPath` disabled. Git 2.54's per-hook `hook.<name>.enabled` setting is the compatible control.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RETENTION-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-20261027/README.md:11:The regression configures a hook named `retention=extra` through an included file, verifies both the traditional and configuration hooks are active before collection on Git 2.54+, sets the inherited re-enable parameter, verifies neither hook runs during collection, and confirms the reference is actually deleted.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RETENTION-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-20261027/README.md:13:Git's [2.54 release notes](https://github.com/git/git/blob/master/Documentation/RelNotes/2.54.0.adoc) document configuration-defined hooks; the [hook configuration reference](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config#Documentation/git-config.txt-hookltfriendly-namegtcommand) describes per-hook enablement.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RETENTION-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-20261027/README.md:19:- Git 2.54.0 (`/var/tmp/nexus-git-2.54.0`): retention hook, shell-injection and confinement tests **17/17 passed**, including the `retention=extra` hook and the inherited `GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS` re-enable case ([log](git254-current-tests.log)).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RETENTION-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-20261027/README.md:21:- Negative control: against the first correction that used only `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`, the same test fails with `AssertionError: gc executed a configured Git hook` on Git 2.54; the current patch passes.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RETENTION-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-20261027/README.md:29:- The shared guard and checkpoint coverage are recorded with a 34/34 run on Git 2.54 and 2.43 in `DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-SHARED-20261027`. The full suite and release qualification were not part of this focused check; exact-head hosted CI covers integration.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-SHARED-20261027/README.md:7:| Affected behavior | Git 2.54 added hooks declared in repository config (`hook.<name>.event` / `.command`). `core.hooksPath=/dev/null` does not disable them. Retention reference deletion, checkpoint creation (stash/ref update), pruning and restore (reset) could therefore execute a workspace-controlled hook even after PR #269/#270. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-SHARED-20261027/README.md:8:| Severity | High on Git 2.54+: arbitrary code execution from repository config during ordinary cleanup/checkpoint operations. Older Git has no configuration hooks and is unaffected. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-SHARED-20261027/README.md:30:- New checkpoint regression (Git 2.54+ only): a config include declares `reference-transaction` and `post-index-change` hooks; preconditions prove both fire on a raw `git update-ref`/`git stash create`, then checkpoint create, restore and prune must not run them. Against the pre-fix checkpoint source it fails with `checkpoint creation executed a configured hook`; it passes with the shared guard.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-SHARED-20261027/README.md:32:- Checkpoint + retention suites (checkpoint hook/index-lock/confinement and retention hook/shell/confinement): **34/34 pass on Git 2.54.0** ([log](git254-checkpoint-retention.log)) and **34/34 on host Git 2.43.0** ([log](git243-checkpoint-retention.log)).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CHECKPOINT-GIT-HOOKS-20261026/README.md:45:  `reference-transaction`/`post-index-change` events, with a Git 2.54 regression. See\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28448}},"started_at_ms":1793123799507,"completed_at_ms":1793123799508}}
