{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:01:01.850Z","ordinal":420809,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17e85-d299-7520-b8fc-37249139b961","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for the current diff, SHA-256 `cc615270eb0ce139e712e89fbb67bdaed11f2f2f2eac4914b637ee5174ff77b3`.\n\nThe event-wide `hook.<event>.enabled=false` override closes the hook-discovery race, and the new test injects a hook immediately before ref deletion. Retention now preserves the record and reports an error when ref deletion fails.\n\nOne race remains: `validateCheckpointConfined` closes its pinned directory handles at [retention.ts:1093–1099](/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/cli/src/core/retention.ts:1093). Git then deletes the ref at lines 1189–1199, and `deleteCheckpointConfined` reopens and validates the record afterward. A record or parent replacement between those steps can still delete the ref before final cleanup rejects and preserves the changed record. The added regression replaces the record before `executeRetention` starts, so it covers the earlier validation check, not this interval. Keep the validated handles/guard live across ref deletion and cleanup, or restore the ref if final cleanup rejects; add a regression that replaces the record immediately before the wrapped `update-ref`.\n\nI did not run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793124061.849884}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":20404}}
