{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:03:24.845Z","ordinal":420944,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17e88-012c-7d53-8c57-6d2e83d0273b","call_id":"call_994512b5da914e88bb482f69615b383c","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for evidence file SHA-256 `8fa49c2369f42f2f09707bc1f21a60f515501d30222939925731afc80bfec7cc`.\\n\\nThe three archived receipts match the check IDs and usage summaries, identify the RC10 ChatGPT provider calls, and contain no credential values or workspace content. The evidence satisfies the ChatGPT verify-on-RC row while keeping its claim limited to that provider gate. No provider tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since `2026-10-26T12:18:17Z`, Issue #1 gained coordinator comments #6415806863 and #6423073471. The issue was last updated at `2026-10-26T17:37:53Z`; all 22 comments are from the coordinator, with no custodian response or handoff. The claims search also shows no active custodian/author claim.\\n\\nAt current `origin/main@303ea322a7148b4a9d1a8231d7ce1c8f824bbae4`, the evaluator still rejects legacy `hidden.command` for qualification (`eval/validate.mjs:49`); the README still requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeat custody checks, and a new manifest identity. The `2026-10-27T05:30:30Z` release-loop record reports RC10 published but still lists `blackbox_v1_custodian_sealing` as a blocker.\\n\\nNo private material was accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for the current diff, SHA-256 `cc615270eb0ce139e712e89fbb67bdaed11f2f2f2eac4914b637ee5174ff77b3`.\\n\\nThe event-wide `hook.<event>.enabled=false` override closes the hook-discovery race, and the new test injects a hook immediately before ref deletion. Retention now preserves the record and reports an error when ref deletion fails.\\n\\nOne race remains: `validateCheckpointConfined` closes its pinned directory handles at [retention.ts:1093–1099](/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/cli/src/core/retention.ts:1093). Git then deletes the ref at lines 1189–1199, and `deleteCheckpointConfined` reopens and validates the record afterward. A record or parent replacement between those steps can still delete the ref before final cleanup rejects and preserves the changed record. The added regression replaces the record before `executeRetention` starts, so it covers the earlier validation check, not this interval. Keep the validated handles/guard live across ref deletion and cleanup, or restore the ref if final cleanup rejects; add a regression that replaces the record immediately before the wrapped `update-ref`.\\n\\nI did not run tests.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793124204.84499}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
