{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:05:47.584Z","ordinal":421112,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17e8a-2ec0-7ea0-b665-ce5a97176aa2","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** for base `7a860c091297abc13371d92ae9633a9f06d67f7a`, diff SHA-256 `dd474586b2e0d8189fd58007aabf7e05d581d64503ffa37a430d97f2bb4a6f96`.\n\nThe event-wide hook override closes the discovery race. Retention uses expected-old ref deletion and create-only restoration, avoiding overwrites during concurrent ref changes. The new wrapper regression changes the record between validation and ref deletion, then verifies the record is preserved and the ref restored. Ref-deletion failures also leave the record available for retry and are reported. Diff check is clean; I did not run tests.\n\nSeparate scope note: manual pruning in [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:376) retains its earlier record-first deletion and swallowed-error behavior; this diff changes the shared hook suppression there but does not make that path failure-atomic."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793124347.5842752}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":20412}}
