{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:06:04.699Z","ordinal":421131,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","item":{"type":"Extension","kind":"web.search","id":"exec-5b867bec-6ce9-4283-8229-181acfcff95b","query":"site:github.com/git/git \"hook.<event>.enabled\" ...","action":{"type":"search","query":null,"queries":["site:github.com/git/git \"hook.<event>.enabled\"","Git hook.<event>.enabled introduced version event-level hook setting"]},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"git-scm.com","ref_id":"turn111search0","snippet":"See git-hook[1]. ... Switch to enable or disable all hooks for the <event> hook event. ... Since using a known event name as a friendly-name","title":"Git - git-config Documentation","url":"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"kernel.org","ref_id":"turn111search1","snippet":"See git-hook(1). ... Since using a known event name as a friendly-name is disallowed (see `hook.`<friendly-name>`.event` above), there is no ambiguity between event-level and per-hook","title":"git-config(1)","url":"https://kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/docs/git-config.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn111search2","snippet":"\"`git config set advice.ignoredHook false`.\"), ... * friendly-names are event-level switches (hook.<event>.enabled = false). ... /* to enable oneliners, let config-specified hooks run in shell.","title":"git/hook.c at master · git/git · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/git/git/blob/master/hook.c"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.kernel.org","ref_id":"turn111search3","snippet":"See git-hook(1). ... Since using a known event name as a friendly-name is disallowed (see `hook.`<friendly-name>`.event` above), there is no ambiguity between event-level and per-hook","title":"git-config(1)","url":"https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/docs/git-config.html"},{"type":"text_result","d