{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:14:22.062Z","ordinal":421623,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0e9fb9c5081a0a4bef6a75b759103","usage":{"input_tokens":134583,"cached_input_tokens":134144,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":153,"reasoning_output_tokens":23,"total_tokens":134736},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":34527734,"cached_input_tokens":34253952,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":105978,"reasoning_output_tokens":59729,"total_tokens":34633712},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7760387626,"cached_input_tokens":7677707008,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":22179383,"reasoning_output_tokens":12837224,"total_tokens":7782567009}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:14:23.847Z","ordinal":421624,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-642e75d5-3913-492d-9fe4-445f246649a8","process_id":"17649","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,160p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-READONLY-MODE-ESCALATION-20261024/README.md && sed -n '1,100p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_POST_REVIEW_TRANSACTION_FIXES/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,160p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-READONLY-MODE-ESCALATION-20261024/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-READONLY-MODE-ESCALATION-20261024/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,100p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_POST_REVIEW_TRANSACTION_FIXES/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_POST_REVIEW_TRANSACTION_FIXES/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# DEFECT: `/mode auto` lowers an explicit `--read-only` launch and unlocks mutating slash commands\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Base revision | `29eab4cd58051a8210b5ef66e0c9e248b2046a13` (`origin/main`) |\n| Branch | `v1/defect-readonly-mode-escalation` |\n| Affected behavior | With an explicit `--read-only` launch, `Agent.getApprovalMode()` returned `config.approvalMode` before checking `config.readOnly`. The TUI `/mode auto` slash command calls `setApprovalMode(\"auto\")`, so the reported mode became `auto`; the sidecar's read-only slash gate keys on `getApprovalMode() === \"read-only\"`, so after `/mode auto` mutating slash commands were allowed. In the reproduction, `/skill init leaked` then wrote `.nexus/skills/leaked/SKILL.md` and returned success, despite the session being launched read-only. |\n| Severity | Medium: a read-only session is meant to be a safe inspection posture for untrusted workspaces; this lets the operator (or a misleading UI) unlock writes, MCP server startup, theme/knowledge/skill scaffolding without leaving the session. |\n\n## Reproduction (pre-fix)\n\nSidecar probe with `ApplicationCore({ readOnly: true, approvalMode: \"read-only\" })`:\n\n```\nMODE_AFTER= auto\nMODE_OUTPUT= Mode: auto. Edits and commands run without asking.\nSKILL_RESULT= {\"type\":\"slash.result\",\"id\":\"skill-1\",\"command\":\"skill\",\"success\":true,\n              \"output\":\"Scaffolded leaked at /tmp/.../.nexus/skills/leaked/SKILL.md\"}\nSKILL_WROTE= true\n```\n\nThe new regression test fails on the base source at the read-only assertion (actual `auto`, expected\n`read-only`).\n\n## Fix\n\n`getApprovalMode()` now checks the immutable restrictions first:\n\n```ts\nif (this.checkpointReadOnlyFallback || this.config.readOnly) return \"read-only\";\nif (this.config.approvalMode) return this.config.approvalMode;\n```\n\nThe checkpoint read-only fallback was already authoritative; an explicit `--read-only` launch now is too, so a later\nmode change cannot lower it. The sidecar's existing slash gate and session-state reporting therefore stay read-only,\nand `/mode auto` reports the queued behaviour instead of claiming auto.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New `cli/test/readonly_mode_escalation.test.ts`: fails on the pre-fix source (`actual: auto`, expected\n  `read-only`); passes after. It also drives `/skill init leaked`, `/mode review`, `models.list` and\n  `provider.connect`, asserting the slash command is refused with no `SKILL.md`, provider discovery stays `BUSY`,\n  provider connection fails, and the reported session mode stays `read-only`.\n- `approval_policy.test.ts` 13/13 and `readonly_home.test.ts` 5/5 in isolated HOME.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` clean; `git diff --check` clean.\n- The full sidecar suite is timing-sensitive in this environment: it has unrelated failures on the base source as\n  well (approval-timing/evidence tests), so it is not cited as a gate for this slice.\n\n## Residual risk\n\n- The REPL keeps a separate `approvalMode` field; `/mode auto` there still prints auto, although the agent-level\n  read-only mode now remains authoritative and the tool/authority layers still reject mutations. A follow-up can\n  align the REPL's displayed mode and queued-checkpoint wording.\n- `checkpointReadOnlyFallback` intentionally lifts after a safe checkpoint; the test documents that behaviour and\n  this change preserves it.\n# PLAN-12 post-review transaction fixes — PR #51\n\nImplementation source: `b590be268b37790bfe4568694a9378f2016749b0` on `v1/plan-12-post-review-transaction-fixes`. This follow-up preserves rejected PR #48 and its branch/history. It incorporates the explicitly handed-off component-coherence and bounded legacy-policy commits from the release coordinator. No independent verdict is authored here.\n\n## Fresh validation\n\n- Local WSL, Node 20.18.1, isolated test-runner HOME: TypeScript `--noEmit` succeeded. Five focused test files passed **107/107**, 13 suites, no skips (retained TAP). This is a source snapshot extracted from the exact committed tree, not the live editing worktree.\n- Fault coverage includes six crash filesystem/journal windows, five actual upgrade exception boundaries, an actual SIGKILL after replacing the package, post-install wrong-version rejection, missing runtime rejection, hung descendant cleanup, redirected recovery paths, failed link restoration with retained artifacts, read-only checks over pending journals, invalid-recovery exit code, exact previous-package binary rollback, and complete session/config backup restoration.\n- Official public alpha.2 archive SHA-256 `56227e58366d21f67bfb46fde4d0e916cadf4c5eed1fdc65d39e01b1d57c60c7` matched the independently fetched public SHA256SUMS. Its core reported `harness-core 1.2.1` on WSL; the complete bounded runtime helper returned `healthy: true`. These are runtime observations, not an end-to-end upgrade or RC acceptance result.\n- The release coordinator independently observed both public alpha core binaries reporting 1.2.1 on mike-dev. Its retained observation record is included unchanged. Historical component exceptions are bound to exact official component hashes, platform, target identities, and schemas, rather than arbitrary version mismatch.\n- No inference, private held-out data, canonical dirty checkout edits, shared-host test overlap, merges, tags, deployment, or publication occurred in this slice.\n\n## Acceptance mapping and limits\n\n| Criterion | Evidence supplied here | Still required |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-UPG-01/02 | Existing release comparison fixtures plus pending-journal check-only purity regression | Installed-RC checks against published releases |\n| ACC-UPG-03/04 | Existing command/upgrade/downgrade fixtures | Installed interactive/noninteractive acceptance |\n| ACC-UPG-05 | Startup integration preserves CLI/TUI entry path; deliberate approval implementation unchanged | Real installed TUI approval/queued-input acceptance |\n| ACC-UPG-06 | Live package exception and actual-kill rollback regressions; canonical-root/path checks | Installed package upgrade acceptance |\n| ACC-UPG-07 | Component coherence, requested-target binding, bounded legacy/config/state policy fixtures | Workflow-produced metadata and installed legacy upgrade |\n| ACC-UPG-08 | Existing tar/download safety fixtures rerun | Required RC artifact gates |\n| ACC-UPG-09 | Complete private state/config snapshot restoration and distinct binary rollback tests | Installed migration/rollback matrix |\n| ACC-UPG-10 | Existing provenance fixtures; journal identity/rename boundary regressions | Installed provenance acceptance |\n| ACC-UPG-11 | Same-version durable backup recovery, actual process kill, nonzero invalid/manual recovery, startup integration | Installed startup/crash matrix and independent review |\n| ACC-UPG-12 | Exact version/core/TUI probes, bounded process-group cleanup, missing/wrong runtime tests | Real package/Rust build and installed verification |\n| ACC-UPG-13 | Official historical alpha.2 runtime health only | Full real prior-public-release → RC upgrade with state, doctor, CLI, TUI, restart |\n| ACC-UPG-14 | Existing trust-boundary document preserved and runtime/legacy caveats clarified | Required workflow provenance and publication checks |\n\nFull `make test`, Rust build/tests, exact-head CI, independent review, installed-RC qualification, terminal/operator evidence, and release acceptance are **pending**. The focused suite and historical runtime observation do not qualify the product. Requirement statuses and frozen thresholds are unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":722916140}},"started_at_ms":1793124863119,"completed_at_ms":1793124863843}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:14:24.921Z","ordinal":421625,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17e92-1398-7a62-a382-05852d7a36e1","call_id":"call_e554b64bb2a248e687d838b311daedbe","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1866)\nTotal output lines: 85\n\n# DEFECT: `/mode auto` lowers an explicit `--read-only` launch and unlocks mutating slash commands\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Base revision | `29eab4cd58051a8210b5ef66e0c9e248b2046a13` (`origin/main`) |\n| Branch | `v1/defect-readonly-mode-escalation` |\n| Affected behavior | With an explicit `--read-only` launch, `Agent.getApprovalMode()` returned `config.approvalMode` before checking `config.readOnly`. The TUI `/mode auto` slash command calls `setApprovalMode(\"auto\")`, so the reported mode became `auto`; the sidecar's read-only slash gate keys on `getApprovalMode() === \"read-only\"`, so after `/mode auto` mutating slash commands were allowed. In the reproduction, `/skill init leaked` then wrote `.nexus/skills/leaked/SKILL.md` and returned success, despite the session being launched read-only. |\n| Severity | Medium: a read-only session is meant to be a safe inspection posture for untrusted workspaces; this lets the operator (or a misleading UI) unlock writes, MCP server startup, theme/knowledge/skill scaffolding without leaving the session. |\n\n## Reproduction (pre-fix)\n\nSidecar probe with `ApplicationCore({ readOnly: true, approvalMode: \"read-only\" })`:\n\n```\nMODE_AFTER= auto\nMODE_OUTPUT= Mode: auto. Edits and commands run without asking.\nSKILL_RESULT= {\"type\":\"slash.result\",\"id\":\"skill-1\",\"command\":\"skill\",\"success\":true,\n              \"output\":\"Scaffolded leaked at /tmp/.../.nexus/skills/leaked/SKILL.md\"}\nSKILL_WROTE= true\n```\n\nThe new regression test fails on the base source at the read-only assertion (actual `auto`, expected\n`read-only`).\n\n## Fix\n\n`getApprovalMode()` now checks the immutable restrictions first:\n\n```ts\nif (this.checkpointReadOnlyFallback || this.config.readOnly) return \"read-only\";\nif (this.config.approvalMode) return this.config.approvalMode;\n```\n\nThe checkpoint read-only fallback was already authoritative; an explicit `--read-only` launch now is too, so a later\nmode change cannot lower it. The sidecar's existing slash gate and session-state reporting therefore stay read-only,\nand `/mode auto` reports the queued behaviour instead of claiming auto.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New `cli/test/readonly_mode_escalation.test.ts`: fails on the pre-fix source (`actual: auto`, expected\n  `read-only`); passes after. It also drives `/skill init leaked`, `/mode review`, `models.list` and\n  `provider.connect`, asserting the slash command is refused with no `SKILL.md`, provider discovery stays `BUSY`,\n  provider connection fails, and the reported session mode stays `read-only`.\n- `approval_policy.test.ts` 13/13 and `readonly_home.test.ts` 5/5 in isolated HOME.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` clean; `git diff --check` clean.\n- The full sidecar suite is timing-sensitive in this environment: it has unrelated failures on the base source as\n  well (approval-timing/evidence tests), so it is not cited as a gate for this slice.\n\n## Residual risk\n\n- The REPL keeps a separate `approvalMode` field; `/mode auto` there still prints auto, although the agent-level\n  read-only mode now…366 tokens truncated…fficial public alpha.2 archive SHA-256 `56227e58366d21f67bfb46fde4d0e916cadf4c5eed1fdc65d39e01b1d57c60c7` matched the independently fetched public SHA256SUMS. Its core reported `harness-core 1.2.1` on WSL; the complete bounded runtime helper returned `healthy: true`. These are runtime observations, not an end-to-end upgrade or RC acceptance result.\n- The release coordinator independently observed both public alpha core binaries reporting 1.2.1 on mike-dev. Its retained observation record is included unchanged. Historical component exceptions are bound to exact official component hashes, platform, target identities, and schemas, rather than arbitrary version mismatch.\n- No inference, private held-out data, canonical dirty checkout edits, shared-host test overlap, merges, tags, deployment, or publication occurred in this slice.\n\n## Acceptance mapping and limits\n\n| Criterion | Evidence supplied here | Still required |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-UPG-01/02 | Existing release comparison fixtures plus pending-journal check-only purity regression | Installed-RC checks against published releases |\n| ACC-UPG-03/04 | Existing command/upgrade/downgrade fixtures | Installed interactive/noninteractive acceptance |\n| ACC-UPG-05 | Startup integration preserves CLI/TUI entry path; deliberate approval implementation unchanged | Real installed TUI approval/queued-input acceptance |\n| ACC-UPG-06 | Live package exception and actual-kill rollback regressions; canonical-root/path checks | Installed package upgrade acceptance |\n| ACC-UPG-07 | Component coherence, requested-target binding, bounded legacy/config/state policy fixtures | Workflow-produced metadata and installed legacy upgrade |\n| ACC-UPG-08 | Existing tar/download safety fixtures rerun | Required RC artifact gates |\n| ACC-UPG-09 | Complete private state/config snapshot restoration and distinct binary rollback tests | Installed migration/rollback matrix |\n| ACC-UPG-10 | Existing provenance fixtures; journal identity/rename boundary regressions | Installed provenance acceptance |\n| ACC-UPG-11 | Same-version durable backup recovery, actual process kill, nonzero invalid/manual recovery, startup integration | Installed startup/crash matrix and independent review |\n| ACC-UPG-12 | Exact version/core/TUI probes, bounded process-group cleanup, missing/wrong runtime tests | Real package/Rust build and installed verification |\n| ACC-UPG-13 | Official historical alpha.2 runtime health only | Full real prior-public-release → RC upgrade with state, doctor, CLI, TUI, restart |\n| ACC-UPG-14 | Existing trust-boundary document preserved and runtime/legacy caveats clarified | Required workflow provenance and publication checks |\n\nFull `make test`, Rust build/tests, exact-head CI, independent review, installed-RC qualification, terminal/operator evidence, and release acceptance are **pending**. The focused suite and historical runtime observation do not qualify the product. Requirement statuses and frozen thresholds are unchanged.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793124864.9209664}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
