{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:15:04.191Z","ordinal":421666,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0ea22bce081a0a64dd3271de79dd9","status":"completed","call_id":"call_098d2a6cb9ba453592461e72db06ca7c","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-RACE-RETENTION-ERRORS-20261027/README.md\\n+# Configured Git Hook Suppression and Checkpoint Retention Failure Handling\\n+\\n+| | |\\n+|---|---|\\n+| Base revision | `7a860c091297abc13371d92ae9633a9f06d67f7a` |\\n+| Branch | `v1/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027` |\\n+| Scope | Close the configured-hook discovery race and preserve checkpoint metadata/ref consistency when retention cleanup fails. |\\n+\\n+## Changes\\n+\\n+- Protected Git operations now disable all configured hooks for each relevant event with the event-wide `hook.<event>.enabled=false` setting. They do not enumerate friendly names before the operation, which would permit a newly added hook to escape suppression.\\n+- Git 2.54 is rejected for protected operations. That release supports named configured hooks but does not implement the event-wide disable switch; continuing would silently leave them executable. Git versions before 2.54 do not implement named configured hooks, and Git 2.55 or later supports the event-wide switch.\\n+- Retention validates checkpoint record and directory identities before ref deletion, deletes refs with an expected old object ID, and restores a deleted ref with a create-only update if final record cleanup rejects the item. Ref deletion errors are reported and leave the record available for retry.\\n+\\n+## Verification\\n+\\n+- `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/retention_git_hook.test.ts test/checkpoint_git_hook.test.ts` using system Git 2.43.0: **11 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed**. The skip is the repository-configured late-hook race test, which requires Git 2.55 or later.\\n+- The same focused suite using an official source build of Git 2.55.0: **12 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed**. The archive was `https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/git-2.55.0.tar.xz`, SHA-256 `457fdb04dc8728e007d4688695e6912e6f680727920f2a40bf11eacc17505357`; the source-built `git` executable reported version 2.55.0. `GIT_TEMPLATE_DIR=/usr/share/git-core/templates` was set because the temporary build was not installed with templates.\\n+- The suite includes an inherited-enable override check, a late-added configured-hook fixture, a Git 2.54 fail-closed fixture, stale-record protection, rollback after a record replacement during ref deletion, and explicit ref-deletion failure handling.\\n+- `npx tsc --noEmit`: passed.\\n+- `git diff --check`: passed.\\n+\\n+## Review and limits\\n+\\n+- Independent review of the exact initial race/retention changes accepted the expected-old ref deletion, create-only restoration, and injected record-replacement regression. The revised Git 2.54 fail-closed guard is awaiting a fresh independent review.\\n+- The review identified manual pruning in `cli/src/checkpoint.ts` as a separate pre-existing record-first deletion path; this slice does not change its failure atomicity.\\n+- The full repository suite, current-main CI, and release qualification were not run for this slice. This evidence does not qualify an RC or change acceptance status.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793124898.74834}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:15:04.221Z","ordinal":421667,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-e765778f-f887-4b7c-bdfa-f2ba8a044fcf","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-RACE-RETENTION-ERRORS-20261027/README.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Configured Git Hook Suppression and Checkpoint Retention Failure Handling\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Base revision | `7a860c091297abc13371d92ae9633a9f06d67f7a` |\n| Branch | `v1/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027` |\n| Scope | Close the configured-hook discovery race and preserve checkpoint metadata/ref consistency when retention cleanup fails. |\n\n## Changes\n\n- Protected Git operations now disable all configured hooks for each relevant event with the event-wide `hook.<event>.enabled=false` setting. They do not enumerate friendly names before the operation, which would permit a newly added hook to escape suppression.\n- Git 2.54 is rejected for protected operations. That release supports named configured hooks but does not implement the event-wide disable switch; continuing would silently leave them executable. Git versions before 2.54 do not implement named configured hooks, and Git 2.55 or later supports the event-wide switch.\n- Retention validates checkpoint record and directory identities before ref deletion, deletes refs with an expected old object ID, and restores a deleted ref with a create-only update if final record cleanup rejects the item. Ref deletion errors are reported and leave the record available for retry.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/retention_git_hook.test.ts test/checkpoint_git_hook.test.ts` using system Git 2.43.0: **11 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed**. The skip is the repository-configured late-hook race test, which requires Git 2.55 or later.\n- The same focused suite using an official source build of Git 2.55.0: **12 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed**. The archive was `https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/git-2.55.0.tar.xz`, SHA-256 `457fdb04dc8728e007d4688695e6912e6f680727920f2a40bf11eacc17505357`; the source-built `git` executable reported version 2.55.0. `GIT_TEMPLATE_DIR=/usr/share/git-core/templates` was set because the temporary build was not installed with templates.\n- The suite includes an inherited-enable override check, a late-added configured-hook fixture, a Git 2.54 fail-closed fixture, stale-record protection, rollback after a record replacement during ref deletion, and explicit ref-deletion failure handling.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\n## Review and limits\n\n- Independent review of the exact initial race/retention changes accepted the expected-old ref deletion, create-only restoration, and injected record-replacement regression. The revised Git 2.54 fail-closed guard is awaiting a fresh independent review.\n- The review identified manual pruning in `cli/src/checkpoint.ts` as a separate pre-existing record-first deletion path; this slice does not change its failure atomicity.\n- The full repository suite, current-main CI, and release qualification were not run for this slice. This evidence does not qualify an RC or change acceptance status.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-RACE-RETENTION-ERRORS-20261027/README.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793124904219,"completed_at_ms":1793124904221}}
