{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:17:36.377Z","ordinal":421830,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4f69db4f-e3a2-4347-a2ff-cc5ca2889aa9","process_id":"28362","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","xerj feedback --submit --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" --used-for \"traced checkpoint pruning integration and protected ref cleanup\" --verdict \"Definition lookup found CheckpointManager.pruneCheckpoints at checkpoint.ts:367. Useful for navigation; current behavior was confirmed in the exact worktree source.\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"xerj feedback --submit --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" --used-for \"traced checkpoint pruning integration and protected ref cleanup\" --verdict \"Definition lookup found CheckpointManager.pruneCheckpoints at checkpoint.ts:367. Useful for navigation; current behavior was confirmed in the exact worktree source.\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"the `--remote` flag is unsupported when a repository argument is provided\n\nCreate a fork of a repository.\n\nWith no argument, creates a fork of the current repository. Otherwise, forks\nthe specified repository.\n\nBy default, the new fork is set to be your `origin` remote and any existing\norigin remote is renamed to `upstream`. To alter this behavior, you can set\na name for the new fork's remote with `--remote-name`.\n\nThe `upstream` remote will be set as the default remote repository.\n\nAdditional `git clone` flags can be passed after `--`.\n\n\nUSAGE\n  gh repo fork [<repository>] [-- <gitflags>...] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n  --clone                 Clone the fork\n  --default-branch-only   Only include the default branch in the fork\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \"origin\")\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n  --help   Show help for command\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Fork a repository\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\n  \n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\n  \n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\ncd xerj\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\nxerj feedback \\\n --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" \\\n  --used-for \"traced checkpoint pruning integration and protected ref cleanup\" --pointed-at \"1051 records across 1 dataset(s) under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261027T181548Z-7e7c-0000)\" \\\n  --verdict \"Definition lookup found CheckpointManager.pruneCheckpoints at checkpoint.ts:367. Useful for navigation; current behavior was confirmed in the exact worktree source.\" --numbers \"not measured\" \\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-27-traced-checkpoint-pruning-integration-and.md\ngit checkout -b field-report/traced-checkpoint-pruning-integration-and\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-27-traced-checkpoint-pruning-integration-and.md\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-27-traced-checkpoint-pruning-integration-and.md -m \"docs(field-report): traced-checkpoint-pruning-integration-and\"\ngit push -u xerj-fork field-report/traced-checkpoint-pruning-integration-and\ngh pr create --repo xerj-org/xerj --base main --head YOUR_LOGIN:field-report/traced-checkpoint-pruning-integration-and \\\n  --title \"Agent field report: traced checkpoint pruning integration and protected ref cleanup\" \\\n  --body \"Field report only; see user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-27-traced-checkpoint-pruning-integration-and.md.\"\nerror: this account cannot push to xerj-org/xerj, and forking failed: `gh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork` failed\nNothing was branched.\n\nGitHub is unavailable (the pull request could not be opened (see above)); sending the field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report instead.\nsent field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report (HTTP 200)\n{\"ok\":true,\"stored\":true,\"note\":\"Thanks. The canonical path is a GitHub PR: https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/tree/main/user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":16,"nanos":358151290}},"started_at_ms":1793125040018,"completed_at_ms":1793125056377}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:17:37.138Z","ordinal":421831,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0eabbb51c81a0965d1da69f0f680d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_d0a9b2e4e5534eb881d8f879483c5665","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CONFIGURED-HOOKS-RACE-RETENTION-ERRORS-20261027/README.md\\n@@\\n - Retention validates checkpoint record and directory identities before ref deletion, deletes refs with an expected old object ID, and restores a deleted ref with a create-only update if final record cleanup rejects the item. Ref deletion errors are reported and leave the record available for retry.\\n+- Manual checkpoint pruning resolves the hook-suppression guard before changing metadata, uses expected-old ref deletion, restores the ref if metadata removal fails, and includes per-checkpoint failures in its returned message instead of swallowing them.\\n@@\\n-- `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/retention_git_hook.test.ts test/checkpoint_git_hook.test.ts` using system Git 2.43.0: **11 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed**. The skip is the repository-configured late-hook race test, which requires Git 2.55 or later.\\n-- The same focused suite using an official source build of Git 2.55.0: **12 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed**. The archive was `https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/git-2.55.0.tar.xz`, SHA-256 `457fdb04dc8728e007d4688695e6912e6f680727920f2a40bf11eacc17505357`; the source-built `git` executable reported version 2.55.0. `GIT_TEMPLATE_DIR=/usr/share/git-core/templates` was set because the temporary build was not installed with templates.\\n-- The suite includes an inherited-enable override check, a late-added configured-hook fixture, a Git 2.54 fail-closed fixture, stale-record protection, rollback after a record replacement during ref deletion, and explicit ref-deletion failure handling.\\n+- `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/retention_git_hook.test.ts test/checkpoint_git_hook.test.ts` using system Git 2.43.0: **12 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed**. The skip is the repository-configured late-hook race test, which requires Git 2.55 or later.\\n+- The same focused suite using an official source build of Git 2.55.0: **13 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed**. The archive was `https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/git-2.55.0.tar.xz`, SHA-256 `457fdb04dc8728e007d4688695e6912e6f680727920f2a40bf11eacc17505357`; the source-built `git` executable reported version 2.55.0. `GIT_TEMPLATE_DIR=/usr/share/git-core/templates` was set because the temporary build was not installed with templates.\\n+- The suite includes inherited-enable override, late-added configured-hook, Git 2.54 fail-closed (including manual-prune preservation), stale-record protection, rollback after record replacement during ref deletion, and explicit ref-deletion failure cases.\\n@@\\n-- Independent review of the exact initial race/retention changes accepted the expected-old ref deletion, create-only restoration, and injected record-replacement regression. The revised Git 2.54 fail-closed guard is awaiting a fresh independent review.\\n-- The review identified manual pruning in `cli/src/checkpoint.ts` as a separate pre-existing record-first deletion path; this slice does not change its failure atomicity.\\n+- Independent review accepted the initial expected-old ref deletion, create-only restoration, and injected record-replacement regression. Review of the Git 2.54 guard and manual-prune correction is pending on the revised diff.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793125051.7099395}}}
