e are source-gate results; the CI package is validation output, not a new published RC.\n295:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n297:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\n299:**Release disposition and next actions:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is published but unaccepted; no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL now pass on `1f3c655`; the pinned-builder documentation claim still needs a safe owner handoff and reconciliation. Continue the installed-candidate qualification lanes, resolve held-out corpus compatibility with the independent custodian, and prepare a new versioned RC only through the accepted process after its prerequisites pass. Exact-RC qualification, independent acceptance, and final publication remain gated by their evidence. Publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n303:**Exact source gates:** `origin/main` and the signed `v1.0.0-rc.3` tag resolve to source commit `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. Exact-main CI [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) completed successfully on that commit. CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux CLI tests, security gates, requirements checks, two-build package reproducibility, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.3` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed at the same source; the latter reports 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is source-gate evidence, not product acceptance.\n307:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\n309:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n311:**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is a published candidate, not an accepted RC. No stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. The installed command now uses RC3; RC1 remains available by its versioned path. The next critical dependency is accepted held-out custody and runner compatibility; other exact-RC gates can proceed independently where their required providers and environments are available.\n317:**Source gates:** PR #159 (`a81f79df35a76207751ffd8a86640baafca98eeb`) merged as `1b9791f`. Its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux package/reproducibility/install-smoke, and CodeQL checks passed; independent source review accepted the change. The focused Doctor schema-2 empty-history regression passed 1/1 with isolated HOME. At exact post-merge source `1b9791f`, `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes with all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`; `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passes with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. Post-merge CI run [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL run [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) are running on the exact merge commit; do not claim post-merge CI complete until both terminate successfully.\n321:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\n323:**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Next source action is to finish exact post-merge CI on `1b9791f`; after it passes, proceed through the accepted RC3 workflow and exact-artifact qualification. Held-out qualification remains dependent on the independent custodian and cannot start before custody and runner compatibility are accepted.\n327:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed successfully on exact `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`: Node 24 at 03:56:55Z, Node 22 at 03:57:48Z, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/package-smoke/installer-smoke at 04:11:34Z. Its Linux job validated identical package archives, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer across two builds. Current-main CodeQL run [39896372726](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372726) completed successfully at 03:43:55Z on that same SHA. CI’s Linux package used existing `1.0.0-rc.2` version metadata; it is source CI evidence, not an immutable RC3 artifact or qualification.\n329:**Source requirements gate:** At exact main `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in the isolated readiness worktree with isolated HOME/XDG. It reported 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open; 12 rows remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. This is the pre-RC source gate only; it does not qualify an installed RC or change any acceptance threshold.\n331:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\n337:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags remain `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor and checkpoint-choice fix. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at exact main and reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.2`. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. A new candidate must use the next RC identity after source CI and release prerequisites pass, then undergo installed-artifact qualification.\n339:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n343:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` was `fa16045a6351ce61763bc3fcc93b562c50849285`, the merge of PR #152. PR #152 carried the readiness checkpoint refresh and terminal worksheet wording separating the §5.3 disposition gate from `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`; its exact head `deaf56fdb074df3f5cd3b62d50f811a2f14ca101` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/repro/install-smoke CI in run `39881805268`; CodeQL `39881805274` passed. The independent reviewer accepted that exact head. Post-merge CI run `39885102002` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/smoke/install; post-merge CodeQL `39885101945` passed. These checks are bound to exact main `fa16045`. Retained post-merge check summary: [CI and CodeQL result](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/post-merge-ci-main-fa16045.txt).\n345:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\n347:**Source requirements gate:** At exact main `fa16045`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in a clean detached Git worktree with isolated HOME/XDG. Retained stdout is in the [exact-main enforcement record](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/requirements-enforce-main-fa16045.txt). It reported 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open; 12 rows are explicitly mapped to exact-RC qualification. This is the pre-RC source gate only. It does not qualify an installed RC or change any requirement's acceptance threshold.\n353:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n357:The authoritative source is `origin/main@269d611ca0a0c8a55244bf70d89fa4a918b9d218`. The Node 22 convergence branch was refreshed without rewriting history and its current candidate head is `v1/node22-floor-converged@658ace9d4ab67901b5b2db1c090f6b01537be27a`; the Node `>=22` source implementation was validated at `fb798a1bd517ac85fd3c99f76d3fda1709540a8d`, and the candidate adds reviewed ruleset and acceptance-stage reconciliations. It is not yet integrated. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at version `1.0.0-rc.2`. The source requirements check currently fails because REQ-REL-111 remains partial pending exact-candidate checks; REQ-REL-003 remains partial for installed-RC platform qualification and is now explicitly mapped to ACC-PLAT in the exact-RC stage. No threshold or qualification evidence was changed.\n363:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n371:**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, PR #140's merge commit. Exact-main CI [39747222866](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39747222866) passed all four jobs on that exact SHA: Node 20, 22, 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging, including the CLI suite and package smoke check. Exact-main CodeQL [39747222840](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39747222840) passed. PR #140's host report is synthetic-only: 10/10 infrastructure checks passed and independent review accepted it; it does not establish held-out qualification.\n373:**Requirements and acceptance:** I reran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` at 09:34 UTC from a clean detached worktree at exact source `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, with isolated HOME/XDG; it exited 0 and reported 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 requirements explicitly mapped to exact-RC qualification in `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1. The checker output is reproducible from that source revision. This is a source-stage gate only; it does not establish RC qualification or acceptance. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`.\n375:**Evaluator containment and Git isolation:** Source tests cover CPU, memory, process-count, storage limits, process cleanup, solution-bearing Git refs/reflogs/dangling objects, and external canary stores in `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts`. PR #140 records a separate exact-source synthetic host preflight with 10/10 checks; its merge and CI do not establish held-out qualification. The public held-out manifest records 40 T2 tasks, ten each across four task classes and four languages; this metadata does not prove private digest re-derivation, author-session independence, effective access controls, custody acceptance, or qualification readiness. No private payloads or validators were accessed for this checkpoint.\n377:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n381:**Contest status:** The contest is over. No contest freeze applies to any files or dependency maintenance. The retired contest-contract check is not a release gate; this does not convert historical contest artifacts into product qualification evidence.\n388:- The source requirements gate remains a clean-worktree pass on exact integration `7d6673f`; eleven requirements remain deferred to exact-RC qualification as listed in the checkpoint below. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; this CI progression does not establish RC readiness or acceptance.\n396:**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n401:- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\n403:- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\n411:**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n413:Exact-source CI and requirements enforcement pass on `8f4504e`, but held-out custody and corpus compatibility, installed-RC qualification, independent RC acceptance, and final publication remain incomplete. No v1.0.0 RC or stable release exists. Publication authorization is granted and remains gated on acceptance.\n420:- **PR and contest state:** PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-`main` candidate. Its CI and CodeQL checks are green, but it is not a release acceptance or publication. PR #102 is open at `3756afe05dbd75c4e6929d87cd50facbb8ab1748`, based on `8f4504e`, to record a synthetic qualification-host preflight; its CodeQL and TypeScript checks passed and its Node matrix was still running at this checkpoint. The preflight report records 10/10 checks using only an empty synthetic marker store; it does not establish private corpus custody or qualification acceptance. The contest has concluded; no contest freeze applies. Historical contest artifacts remain historical evidence only.\n422:- **Evaluator and qualification-host boundary:** Source fixtures for cgroup resource limits, process-tree cleanup, workspace storage, and staged Git-history isolation are in the integration source suite and passed its exact-source CI. A synthetic host preflight at source `8f4504e` recorded 10/10 checks and is being documented in PR #102. Neither source fixtures nor the synthetic-host report establish access separation against the custodian's real store or permit held-out execution before custody acceptance.\n423:- **Held-out corpus and custody:** Public T2 manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` remains the 40-task identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`; T3 public manifest identity remains `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4bfa0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response since 2026-10-21 12:21 UTC. Current evaluator qualification rejects the sealed T2 corpus's legacy `hidden.command` format; the documented path requires a custodian-owned compatible immutable successor and repeated custody checks. Private digest re-derivation, exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective access separation, and current custody acceptance remain unverified here. No payload, validator, reference solution, or hidden answer was accessed, and no held-out run has started.\n424:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\n425:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Root and CLI package versions remain `0.1.0-alpha.2`. GitHub currently lists only alpha pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound RC gates, installed-RC qualification and independent G6 acceptance, then stable promotion/publication and post-publication verification.\n436:- **PR and evaluator state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, #44, and #45 are integrated. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c` on stale base `faf95803714a3c543f5c59bc0610ca6291a6184d`. Its exact CI run `39141771002` passed on that old head, but independent review found qualification preflight does not account for host-source mounts created unconditionally by `agentSandboxArgv`. The finding is recorded in comment `6252102243`; a read-only source inventory and shared-mount-plan remediation target are in comment `6252621855`. Owner handoff request `6252543078` has no response as of this checkpoint. The evaluator claim remains protected. Do not execute held-out tasks until this boundary is fixed, exact-head validated, and independently accepted.\n438:- **Held-out custody and qualification:** The custodian previously accepted the sealed 40-task manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b` and its private digest/reference validation. This does not establish evaluator acceptance or T2 qualification. The implementing agent has not accessed private payloads. No held-out run has started because evaluator confidentiality preflight remains unaccepted and corpus/evaluator schema compatibility is unresolved.\n439:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":683065809}},"started_at_ms":1793125275485,"completed_at_ms":1793125276168}}
