{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:23:18.953Z","ordinal":422161,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0ec1524bc81a08ee9b4b4da41f614","usage":{"input_tokens":81007,"cached_input_tokens":75008,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":93,"reasoning_output_tokens":76,"total_tokens":81100},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":45387962,"cached_input_tokens":45031680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":131858,"reasoning_output_tokens":72257,"total_tokens":45519820},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7771247854,"cached_input_tokens":7688484736,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":22205263,"reasoning_output_tokens":12849752,"total_tokens":7793453117}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:23:19.941Z","ordinal":422162,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17e9a-3d85-7661-b09a-49ac00cba1e7","call_id":"call_38f9eefc1c624717b69916ab3f3ac05a","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for evidence file SHA-256 `8fa49c2369f42f2f09707bc1f21a60f515501d30222939925731afc80bfec7cc`.\\n\\nThe three archived receipts match the check IDs and usage summaries, identify the RC10 ChatGPT provider calls, and contain no credential values or workspace content. The evidence satisfies the ChatGPT verify-on-RC row while keeping its claim limited to that provider gate. No provider tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since `2026-10-26T12:18:17Z`, Issue #1 gained coordinator comments #6415806863 and #6423073471. The issue was last updated at `2026-10-26T17:37:53Z`; all 22 comments are from the coordinator, with no custodian response or handoff. The claims search also shows no active custodian/author claim.\\n\\nAt current `origin/main@303ea322a7148b4a9d1a8231d7ce1c8f824bbae4`, the evaluator still rejects legacy `hidden.command` for qualification (`eval/validate.mjs:49`); the README still requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeat custody checks, and a new manifest identity. The `2026-10-27T05:30:30Z` release-loop record reports RC10 published but still lists `blackbox_v1_custodian_sealing` as a blocker.\\n\\nNo private material was accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed the exact working diff, SHA-256 `24505962c5d887efe49b9499ef686f5fa2a0f7e29fd3aa0cd1c69de23f592073`, against base `7a860c091297abc13371d92ae9633a9f06d67f7a`.\\n\\nThe Git 2.54 guard fails before mutation; manual pruning now preflights it, deletes refs with an expected-old value, restores the ref if record deletion fails, and reports errors ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:377), [git_hook_guard.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/cli/src/core/git_hook_guard.ts:24)). Retention performs confined identity validation before ref deletion and restores refs without overwriting concurrent refs if cleanup fails ([retention.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/cli/src/core/retention.ts:1058), [retention.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027/cli/src/core/retention.ts:1116)).\\n\\nThe added regressions cover unsupported Git 2.54 pruning, record replacement during ref deletion, ref-deletion failure, and rollback. `git diff --check` is clean. I did not run tests.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793125399.9412966}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
