{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:24:44.798Z","ordinal":422240,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-03258bc9-11a7-4b7f-9619-70e460480aa8","process_id":"66830","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short && git diff --check && git diff --stat && git diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | head -100 && rg -n 'claim|handoff|release|push|review' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md | head -70 && tail -80 .git/nexus-claims.log"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-readiness-20261027","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short && git diff --check && git diff --stat && git diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | head -100 && rg -n 'claim|handoff|release|push|review' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md | head -70 && tail -80 .git/nexus-claims.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":" M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | 12 ++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex a425a39c..e79bc2cb 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,17 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 18:24 UTC)\n+\n+**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `7a860c091297abc13371d92ae9633a9f06d67f7a`, integrating PR #277. Post-merge CI run [40554202482](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40554202482) is still in progress; CodeQL run [40554202502](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40554202502) passed on the exact same SHA. A clean detached worktree at `7a860c0` passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-gate results, not installed-RC acceptance.\n+\n+**Readiness PR #268:** The remote PR remains open at head `2cf9e9949dc6ff8068099d07d765919e59e538d3`, based on `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. Its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed on that older base. GitHub reports no independent review on the current PR head and blocks merging. This readiness branch has been brought forward to include `origin/main@7a860c0`; this checkpoint records the exact old PR evidence and the current base separately. The refreshed change still requires independent review and exact-head CI.\n+\n+**Other open source PRs:** PR [#279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/279) fixes configured-hook race and retention error handling. Its exact diff was independently accepted; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript pass, while Node 22 and Node 24 are pending. PR [#278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/278) records RC10 ChatGPT verification; CodeQL, JavaScript/TypeScript, Node 22, and Node 24 pass, while Linux packaging remains pending. Neither PR is merged.\n+\n+**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; the operator cannot run the requested xterm 80×24 cell now, and no result or screenshot is inferred. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication is authorized but gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\n+\n+The 17:31 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, CI, and requirements status by this checkpoint.\n+\n ## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 17:31 UTC)\n \n **Authoritative source and post-merge checks:** `origin/main` is `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`, integrating PR #275 after PR #273. Exact-main CI [40537474824](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40537474824) passed the Node 22, Node 24, and `linux-x86_64` jobs on `ceabfcc`; CodeQL [40537475057](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40537475057) also passed on that SHA. Earlier post-merge CI [40536704465](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40536704465) and CodeQL [40536704530](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40536704530) passed on `e94208d`. These establish source CI for those exact commits; they do not establish RC acceptance or release qualification.\n12:## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n15:- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n18:## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n20:Claims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n23:CLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\n24:mkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\n26:if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\n30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\n34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n35:- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n37:- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n51:| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n56:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n60:| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n61:| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n62:| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n63:| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n64:| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n65:| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n66:| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n67:| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n71:| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n72:| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n76:| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n86:3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n95:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n97:| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n98:| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n102:The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n110:| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n111:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n116:- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\ntail: cannot open '.git/nexus-claims.log' for reading: Not a directory\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":698626964}},"started_at_ms":1793125484099,"completed_at_ms":1793125484798}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:24:46.009Z","ordinal":422241,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17e9b-8db8-7430-8b24-c964ee60879e","call_id":"call_17b0aeb6197d4f5eaf69bbb70759fd14","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":" M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | 12 ++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex a425a39c..e79bc2cb 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,17 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 18:24 UTC)\n+\n+**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `7a860c091297abc13371d92ae9633a9f06d67f7a`, integrating PR #277. Post-merge CI run [40554202482](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40554202482) is still in progress; CodeQL run [40554202502](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40554202502) passed on the exact same SHA. A clean detached worktree at `7a860c0` passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-gate results, not installed-RC acceptance.\n+\n+**Readiness PR #268:** The remote PR remains open at head `2cf9e9949dc6ff8068099d07d765919e59e538d3`, based on `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. Its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed on that older base. GitHub reports no independent review on the current PR head and blocks merging. This readiness branch has been brought forward to include `origin/main@7a860c0`; this checkpoint records the exact old PR evidence and the current base separately. The refreshed change still requires independent review and exact-head CI.\n+\n+**Other open source PRs:** PR [#279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/279) fixes configured-hook race and retention error handling. Its exact diff was independently accepted; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript pass, while Node 22 and Node 24 are pending. PR [#278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/278) records RC10 ChatGPT verification; CodeQL, JavaScript/TypeScript, Node 22, and Node 24 pass, while Linux packaging remains pending. Neither PR is merged.\n+\n+**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; the operator cannot run the requested xterm 80×24 cell now, and no result or screenshot is inferred. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication is authorized but gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\n+\n+The 17:31 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, CI, and requirements status by this checkpoint.\n+\n ## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 17:31 UTC)\n \n **Authoritative source and post-merge checks:** `origin/main` is `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`, integrating PR #275 after PR #273. Exact-main CI [40537474824](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40537474824) passed the Node 22, Node 24, and `linux-x86_64` jobs on `ceabfcc`; CodeQL [40537475057](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40537475057) also passed on that SHA. Earlier post-merge CI [40536704465](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40536704465) and CodeQL [40536704530](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40536704530) passed on `e94208d`. These establish source CI for those exact commits; they do not establish RC acceptance or release qualification.\n12:## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n15:- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n18:## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n20:Claims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n23:CLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\n24:mkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\n26:if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\n30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\n34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n35:- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n37:- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n51:| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n56:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n60:| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n61:| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n62:| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n63:| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n64:| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n65:| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n66:| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n67:| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n71:| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n72:| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n76:| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n86:3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n95:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n97:| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n98:| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n102:The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n110:| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n111:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n116:- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\ntail: cannot open '.git/nexus-claims.log' for reading: Not a directory\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793125486.008955}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
