{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:33:25.396Z","ordinal":422612,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0ee6ffba881a09413169300f32f75","status":"completed","call_id":"call_aa911160d6ef4e58bac1ae2555bab9a6","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-readiness-20261027/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\\n@@\\n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 18:32 UTC)\\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 18:33 UTC)\\n@@\\n-**Readiness PR #268:** At the 18:32 UTC observation, the PR was at head `e17a4519c5eb7834cf1dc58f73bfeac9f0985a0c` on current base `main@7a860c091297abc13371d92ae9633a9f06d67f7a`. Node 22 and Node 24 were still running; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL had passed. No independent review was recorded for that head. Its prior head `2cf9e99` passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks against the older `ceabfcc` base; those results do not qualify the refreshed head. This checkpoint update advances the PR again, so its resulting head requires its own exact-head CI and independent review before merge.\\n+**Readiness PR #268:** The first refresh commit `e17a451` was on current base `main@7a860c0`; its observation recorded Node 22/24 in progress and JavaScript/TypeScript plus CodeQL passed. The current remote PR head is `9b9c1813207b228e695e91f727af1fae3b9cc5fa` on that same base. At 18:33 UTC, CodeQL passed while JavaScript/TypeScript and Node 22/24 were pending; no independent review was recorded on `9b9c181`. The older `2cf9e99` checks passed against `ceabfcc`, but do not qualify the refreshed branch. The next checkpoint commit will advance the PR head again and require its own exact-head checks and independent review before merge.\\n@@\\n-**Other open source PRs:** PR [#279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/279) addresses the configured-hook race and retention error-accounting findings left by merged PR #277. Owner read-only review accepted exact head `a27b0d7c6d2195fb805eb88540a0f4a130b7a888` (diff SHA-256 `8e3eb6ea729c8c06f11d9915c1668a288a455802b0dc161c701787039d72853b`); Node 22/24 are running, while CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript pass. Until this corrective PR merges, the findings remain present on main. PR [#278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/278) records RC10 ChatGPT verification; CodeQL, JavaScript/TypeScript, Node 22, and Node 24 pass, while Linux packaging remains in progress. Neither PR is merged.\\n+**Other open source PRs:** PR [#279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/279) addresses the configured-hook race and retention error-accounting findings left by merged PR #277. An independent read-only review accepted exact head `a27b0d7c6d2195fb805eb88540a0f4a130b7a888`; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript pass, while Node 22 and Node 24 are pending. Until this corrective PR merges, the findings remain present on main. PR [#278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/278) records RC10 ChatGPT verification; CodeQL, JavaScript/TypeScript, Linux, Node 22, and Node 24 pass. Neither PR is merged.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793125999.996616}}}
