{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:36:17.568Z","ordinal":422736,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17ea6-1b20-7850-9b52-7c6636a44937","call_id":"call_6dbd5a1c3bf642ac8611922eeb58d3ad","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8897)\nTotal output lines: 176\n\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:20:The source tests cover the applicable source acceptance criteria. They do not claim installed-RC qualification, held-out qualification, cross-runner qualification, or human terminal acceptance. Those release gates remain pending.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:33:This revalidation confirms source-level evidence on the rebased candidate only. It does not satisfy exact-RC, held-out, cross-runner, or human terminal qualification.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:41:This is a local source-test result on commit `93d0fa460517bf60fe5817cf4b51278498ec8d0e`; fresh exact-head hosted CI is still required. Exact-RC, held-out, cross-runner, and human terminal qualification remain pending.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md:29:This evidence establishes one synthetic OpenRouter live task on the installed RC10 artifact. It does not establish held-out, standalone long-task, provider recovery, T3/T4, cross-runner, manual terminal, exact-RC acceptance, or stable-release completion. OpenRouter's separate provider verification receipts and result are in [`../providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl`](../providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl) and [`../providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json`](../providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json).\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc10-chatgpt-verification-20261027T174805Z.json:76:    \"It does not establish standalone engineering-task correctness, held-out qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, terminal acceptance, or independent RC acceptance.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/resource-limits-20261021T0500Z-synthetic.md:15:This is host infrastructure evidence, not held-out qualification or custody acceptance. The path-canary test exercises the production candidate Bubblewrap sandbox but does not exercise end-to-end `eval/run.mjs` task staging with Git object canaries. Those custody and runner-path gates remain open.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/platform-e2/attempts-incomplete.md:6:- A first matrix invocation requested a prepared image named `nexus-e2/ubuntu-22-04-node24`, which was not present. The final matrix uses the prepared Node 22 OS image and a read-only mount of the local Node v24.11.1 runtime. The runtime major is asserted in the runner.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/platform-e2/attempts-incomplete.md:7:- A second Node 22 invocation failed before installer execution because shell quoting changed the Node major-version assertion into invalid JavaScript `process.versions.node.split(.)`. The corrected runner uses `node --version | cut -d. -f1` and passed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/cross-runner/README.md:1:# RC10 cross-runner reproducibility\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/cross-runner/README.md:10:- The comparison job passed and matched both runner outputs to each other and to all six published artifacts.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/cross-runner/README.md:13:The retained `repro-evidence.json` records tag, tree, lockfiles, toolchain, builder images, package script identity, and the SHA-256 for `SHA256SUMS`, notices, compatibility metadata, installer, archive, and SBOM. This is one passed exact-RC reproducibility gate; it does not establish overall product acceptance or stable-release readiness.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/cross-runner/repro-evidence.json:43:      \"runner\": {\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/cross-runner/repro-evidence.json:56:      \"runner\": {\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/README.md:27:Runner exit codes were zero for the 12 original scripts, but the original scripts do not assert every acceptance limit. Manual review found the s5 timing outlier above; therefore this evidence does not claim a clean pass of the entire scripted E3 gate. The source artifact and installed package identities are exact.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md:22:The two failed full-matrix attempts, the successful isolated retry, their runner scripts, synthetic gateway logs, PTY streams, and screen snapshots are retained here without replacing earlier attempts.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md:13:These records cover the provider verification path only. The synthetic task and its failed attempts are separately documented, and all held-out, long-task, fault-injection, terminal, cross-runner, independent acceptance, and stable-release gates remain outside this result.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc10-chatgpt-verification-20261027T174805Z.json\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/repro_false_verified.test.ts\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_infer_repro.test.ts\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/repro_steering.repro.ts\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/repro_findings_crash.repro.ts\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/repro_notice.repro.ts\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_parser_probe.test.ts\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/repro_overhead.test.ts\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RUNNER-BACKGROUND-STARTUP-EXIT-20261023/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v