end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- autopilot:start --\\u003e\\n- [ ] \\u003c!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --\\u003e \\u003cstrong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\"\\u003eAutofix\\u003c/strong\\u003e · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n\\u003c!-- autopilot:end --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- tips_start --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss\\u0026utm_medium=github\\u0026utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code\\u0026utm_content=279)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003e❤️ Share\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003cdl\\u003e\\n\\u003cdd\\u003e\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A\\u0026url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit\\u0026text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai\\u0026mini=true\\u0026title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit\\u0026summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n\\u003c/dd\\u003e\\n\\u003c/dl\\u003e\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003csub\\u003eComment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- tips_end --\\u003e\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-27T18:20:06Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Independent Read-Only Review: PR #279 (`v1/configured-hook-race-retention-errors-20261027`)\\n\\n**Verdict**: **ACCEPT**\\n\\n#### 1. Invariant \\u0026 Boundary Verification\\n- **Target Branch \\u0026 Clean Base:** Head `a27b0d7c6d2195fb805eb88540a0f4a130b7a888` is cleanly based on `origin/main` at `7a860c091297abc13371d92ae9633a9f06d67f7a`.\\n- **Change Boundary:** `cli/src/checkpoint.ts`, `cli/src/core/git_hook_guard.ts`, `cli/src/core/retention.ts`, regressions in `cli/test/checkpoint_git_hook.test.ts` and `cli/test/retention_git_hook.test.ts`, plus evidence README (+544 / -65).\\n- **Exact Diff SHA-256:** `8e3eb6ea729c8c06f11d9915c1668a288a455802b0dc161c701787039d72853b`.\\n- **Formatting \\u0026 Whitespace Check:** `git diff --check 7a860c0...a27b0d7` passed with 0 errors.\\n\\n#### 2. Scope \\u0026 Technical Remediation Review\\n- **Resolution of P1 (Config-Change Race):** Completely replaces per-hook friendly name discovery with direct event-wide overrides (`hook.\\u003cevent\\u003e.enabled=false`) appended to `GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS`. Eliminates the race window where a late-added hook in repository config could execute.\\n- **Fail-Closed on Git 2.54:** Because Git 2.54 introduced named config hooks but lacked the event-wide disable mechanism introduced in 2.55, the guard explicitly detects Git 2.54 and fails closed with an informative error rather than risking hook execution.\\n- **Resolution of P2 (Retention Error Accounting \\u0026 Consistency):**\\n  - Confined checkpoint record validation is performed prior to ref deletion.\\n  - Ref deletion passes the expected old target hash to guard against concurrent modification.\\n  - If record deletion subsequently fails or rejects, the ref is reliably restored (or error surfaces with restoration details).\\n  - Deletion errors are pushed to `errors` array and not swallowed; `deletedCount` is not incremented on failure.\\n  - Similar transaction rollback and failure propagation implemented in `CheckpointManager.pruneCheckpoints`.\\n\\n#### 3. Automated Validation Receipts\\n- Hosted CodeQL run [40558982889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40558982889): **✓ SUCCESS** (1m14s, 0 alerts).\\n- Hosted CI run [40558983146](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40558983146): In progress.\\n\\n**Disposition:** ACCEPT. Ready for merge upon CI matrix completion.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-27T18:28:36Z\"}],\"commits\":[{\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(checkpoint): fail closed on configured hook races\",\"oid\":\"a27b0d7c6d2195fb805eb88540a0f4a130b7a888\"}],\"reviews\":[]}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17e71-922f-7ef3-a2c1-bcdcbd1f8423","create_time":1793126564.7140539}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
