{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:49:03.299Z","ordinal":423277,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17eb1-62db-7543-bdeb-97095e0e59b7","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17eb1-62db-7543-bdeb-97095e0e59b7","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0f21d533c81a0a07c38bc5283f523","usage":{"input_tokens":143991,"cached_input_tokens":139136,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":165,"reasoning_output_tokens":94,"total_tokens":144156},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":698044,"cached_input_tokens":689152,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":989,"reasoning_output_tokens":459,"total_tokens":699033},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7790824217,"cached_input_tokens":7707853568,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":22259793,"reasoning_output_tokens":12877274,"total_tokens":7813084010}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:49:04.275Z","ordinal":423278,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17eb1-62db-7543-bdeb-97095e0e59b7","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6d93cf3d-684d-4da9-b1ed-35658b4633b0","process_id":"14188","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | head -110"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | head -110"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 02:11 UTC)\n\n**Terminal recheck:** Installed RC10 synthetic tool cancellation at `TERM=dumb`, 100×30 passed five targeted trials with Esc delays from 0 to 1 second; idle return measured 0.405–0.507 seconds. The two earlier full-matrix timeouts remain valid and unresolved; this recheck does not promote ACC-TUI-A11Y or E3. Evidence and raw PTY streams are in [the cancellation timing recheck](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/cancel-timing-recheck-20261027/README.md). The separate supplemental probes now observed all nine overlay variants at `TERM=dumb` 40×14. The Detail panel opened and closed; its final idle-prompt predicate was too specific after focus moved to transcript. Human matrix is still 0/15.\n\n**Release state:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains a prerelease on source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; `origin/main` still resolves to that commit. Stable `v1.0.0` is not published. Issues #1 and #2 remain open. Exact-RC T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, live provider/standalone, independent acceptance, and human terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Keep publication gated.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 02:01 UTC)\n\n**RC10 terminal evidence update:** PR #264 carries the scripted terminal evidence update on the current main base. No product source changes are included in this evidence slice. Earlier interrupted Detail-overlay probes are classified as harness-incomplete. Across the original and corrected supplemental PTY probes, all nine source `Overlay` variants were observed at `TERM=dumb`, 40×14, including a separately retained Detail capture; the Detail capture’s post-Esc idle predicate remained harness-limited. Follow-up synthetic command approval attempts did not complete and are not product failures. See [supplemental overlay evidence](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/README.md). The ACC-TUI-A11Y disposition remains `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`: the earlier intermittent `TERM=dumb` 100×30 cancellation timeouts remain, other terminal configurations are not covered by this supplemental run, and human acceptance remains separate.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 01:42 UTC)\n\n**Source and published candidate:** `origin/main` is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` (PR #262). Public tag and prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.10` resolve to that exact source. Its Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`; installer SHA-256 is `5620d56ef6f8d637fc102ae2c8ea3b055effbc4069243a2df68b67520b1e2302`. Strict GitHub attestation verification passed for the archive and checksum index; the release workflow [40424225668](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40424225668), exact-main CI [40419408166](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40419408166), and exact-main CodeQL [40419408185](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40419408185) succeeded on the RC10 source. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n\n**RC10 qualification evidence:** E2 lifecycle and identity-bound positive install evidence is recorded separately; the cross-platform positive identity matrix passed 8/8 on Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12, and Fedora 40 with Node 22/24. Application process-death recovery passed and is explicitly not power-loss evidence. Strict artifact and install checks passed. Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 in workflow [40433818126](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40433818126); the comparison matched both runner outputs to each other and all six published artifact digests. The archived evidence is [here](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/cross-runner/README.md), with `repro-evidence.json` SHA-256 `f393db75f06cc9675b34941c8d5e42cb7de0f01892cc2f8e64a48c9998d4fcc7`.\n\nInstalled terminal evidence is not fully accepted. Scripted E3 remains `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`: one late-stream Ctrl-C case returned idle after 27.89 seconds against the five-second criterion; passing retries remain recorded but do not erase that observation. The expanded ACC-TUI-A11Y probe sampled ten readable states with zero color-setting SGR codes and a complete 40-column approval hint, but two full runs timed out waiting for Esc tool cancellation at `TERM=dumb` 100×30, one isolated retry passed, and the supplemental probes later observed all nine overlay variants in one configuration, including the separately retained Detail capture. The supplemental run does not clear the timeout anomaly or qualify other configurations. Evidence and failed attempts are preserved under [RC10 scripted terminal evidence](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/README.md). The required human real-terminal matrix remains `0/15`; its exact-RC10 blank worksheet is [here](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual/README.md). Neither scripted evidence nor worksheet is human acceptance.\n\n**Outstanding external and exact-RC gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN. Its last update is 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC; no compatible immutable T2 successor or independent custody acceptance has been recorded, and this implementation lane has not accessed held-out payloads. Issue [#2](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/2) remains OPEN; no T4 qualification run is recorded. Standalone profiles requiring held-out tasks, exact-RC live provider qualification, independent X5 acceptance, and the human terminal matrix are not established. The E5 OpenRouter task lane is separately claimed; do not duplicate it without handoff.\n\n**Disposition:** RC10 is a published prerelease and has passed its source/release pipeline, but is not an accepted release candidate. Keep stable promotion gated on all remaining exact-RC, independent, human, T2/T3/T4, standalone/provider, and terminal gates. This checkpoint supersedes the 2026-10-26 21:10 UTC RC9 checkpoint below; earlier entries remain historical records.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 21:10 UTC)\n\n**Current source and post-merge gates:** `origin/main` is `30f1b89a88bac81d8ab2d4f1e6800e1978a61f38`, the merge commit for PR #261. Its post-merge CI [40401857374](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40401857374) and CodeQL [40401857568](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40401857568) were still running at this checkpoint; do not call the new main source gate complete yet. PR #261's exact-head CI [40396216500](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40396216500) and CodeQL [40396216414](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40396216414) passed before merge. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed exact head `20170c51ef483319aadb56b6b3f60943d227816b`, diff SHA-256 `26a6761810c00cbd3c05b9e05bdbcb36c3e1e97c78693fa4cfed7293ae88fce3`. The PR's first attempt exposed a CI-only TTY-size assumption in its regression test; this was corrected by rendering a buffer directly through Crossterm and the corrected exact-head checks passed.\n\n**RC9 installed accessibility result and source fix:** Published tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` still points to source `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`; its archive SHA-256 is `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`. PR [#260](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/260) merged the exact installed-RC PTY evidence as `9def2658e9269f6468ff7c5562839999cc7352a8`; captures and verifier are in [the RC9 accessibility evidence](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md). On installed RC9, `NO_COLOR=1` under xterm at 40x14 and 100x30 emitted no color SGR codes (2/2 subcases passed); `TERM=dumb` with `NO_COLOR` unset emitted reset SGR `39m`, `49m`, and `59m` at both sizes (2/2 subcases failed). The complete all-state accessibility gate remains partial. PR [#261](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/261) now disables Crossterm color output when the TUI resolves `Depth::Mono` and adds a real-backend regression test. This fix is on `main`, not in the immutable RC9 artifact; RC9 remains failed for the `TERM=dumb` subcase. A new immutable RC and affected-gate requalification are required before any stable release.\n\n**RC9 artifact and installation record:** Tag object `d211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6` targets the source above. Local `git verify-tag` reports a good signature; GitHub reports source-commit verification `verified: true, reason: valid` and tag-object verification `verified: false, reason: bad_email`. Release workflow [40370485753](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40370485753) succeeded and published RC9 as a prerelease. All nine downloaded assets matched GitHub Release API digests. `SHA256SUMS` covers the archive and `compatibility.json` (both entries verified), and `gh attestation verify` passed for the archive and checksum index. The archive was installed in an isolated prefix and reports `1.0.0-rc.9 (4cae11cbc3b0)`. Full artifact details remain in [RC9 artifact verification](evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md). This is artifact/install evidence, not product acceptance.\n\n**Custody and remaining acceptance:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN and its latest update is 17:37:53 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded. No private held-out payload was accessed, and held-out qualification has not started. The repository's latest human terminal matrix status is 0/15; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute for those operator cells. Current-source provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC9 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; the existing publication authorization remains gated on every required release acceptance.\n\n**Next:** Finish exact post-merge CI and CodeQL on `30f1b89`; then prepare a new immutable RC candidate from the validated current source and requalify all affected and still-open gates. Do not promote RC9 to stable.\n\n---\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 15:16 UTC)\n\n**PR #256 exact-head update:** Following independent source-review acceptance of candidate `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, the reviewed branch was pushed as a normal fast-forward from `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a`. PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) now targets exact `origin/main` `ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4`; its hosted CI run [40347686120](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40347686120) and CodeQL [40347686125](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40347686125) are in progress. Do not merge until every required exact-head check completes successfully and branch protection/review requirements are satisfied. The 15:15 checkpoint immediately below remains accurate as a pre-push snapshot and is superseded for PR head and CI status by this update.\n\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 15:15 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source gates:** `origin/main` is `ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4`. Exact-main post-merge CI [40340228722](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228722) completed SUCCESS on that commit across Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging, including the reproducibility build. Post-merge CodeQL [40340228417](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228417) passed. Requirements enforcement and `sync-version --check` passed on exact `ff349383`; 123 requirement rows remain with 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. Components remain `1.0.0-rc.8`.\n\n**PR #256 local-provider candidate:** Public PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) still points to stale head `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a` on base `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421`. The refreshed local candidate is `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, based on current main `ff349383` through normal merge commit `9d898eb9bb77a87490d6fcf47b11260193b1e315`; it is not yet pushed and has no hosted exact-head checks. Independent source review ACCEPTed the full candidate diff (SHA-256 `7dc76f1d5d9ee3dd6ebd982eaefc250cd9862043de1f901bf73f58a26d43e376`) and confirmed prior findings are addressed. The implementer reports focused provider-connect tests 33/33, TUI Rust tests 6/6, TypeScript build, and `git diff --check` pass; no local full suite was run. Run exact PR checks after updating the public branch before integration.\n\n**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN; its latest metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Independent private custody, evaluator-compatible corpus sealing, and held-out acceptance remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. Current-candidate provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The human terminal matrix remains