aling are not established. Held-out qualification has not started. Exact-RC provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3 and nine-class T4 qualification, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. The human terminal matrix remains 0/15; automated PTY checks do not satisfy it. Stable `v1.0.0` is not published. Campaign status remains `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted but gated on acceptance.\n\nThe 06:24 checkpoint immediately below is retained as a historical snapshot; this update supersedes its CI conclusion, RC publication state, cross-runner status, and current blocker summary.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 06:24 UTC at `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, incorporating PR #249 (`8e562b0f3406e94003806746cb69a5258f72a59f`) and PR #250. PR #249 merged at 05:57 UTC and PR #250 merged at 06:20 UTC. On this exact source, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` confirms all components are `1.0.0-rc.8`. CodeQL run [40279197561](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197561) passed. Exact-main CI [40279197785](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197785) is still running; its Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed Rust tests and release builds and were running the CLI test suite at 06:24 UTC. The current checkpoint does not claim full CI success.\n\n**RC and publication state:** The latest public prerelease remains `v1.0.0-rc.7`; `v1.0.0-rc.8` is not yet tagged or published. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The `rc.8` source version is not itself evidence of an accepted or installed RC. No release artifact should be published until every required acceptance gate passes.\n\n**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1), for held-out T2/T3 corpus custody, remains OPEN (last observed update 02:33:48 UTC); the required custodian sealing and independent private-custody acceptance are not established. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone coverage, T3/T4 qualification, installed exact-RC qualification, independent RC acceptance, and the human terminal matrix (0/15 at last evidence) remain incomplete. Treat the older entries below as historical snapshots; they do not supersede these current observations.\n\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 02:27 UTC at `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` remains `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`. CI run [40255529634](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529634) and CodeQL run [40255529667](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529667) both completed successfully on that exact commit. CI passed the Node 22/24 and Linux test matrices, requirements enforcement, security gates, package build and reproducibility, SBOM checks, and package/install smoke checks.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":26173}},"started_at_ms":1793126944275,"completed_at_ms":1793126944275}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:49:05.674Z","ordinal":423279,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17eb1-d38a-7f33-9a14-62da92d63dfa","call_id":"call_80c133288b3c4e5d901c45eb8b3656af","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7136)\nTotal output lines: 110\n\n# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 02:11 UTC)\n\n**Terminal recheck:** Installed RC10 synthetic tool cancellation at `TERM=dumb`, 100×30 passed five targeted trials with Esc delays from 0 to 1 second; idle return measured 0.405–0.507 seconds. The two earlier full-matrix timeouts remain valid and unresolved; this recheck does not promote ACC-TUI-A11Y or E3. Evidence and raw PTY streams are in [the cancellation timing recheck](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/cancel-timing-recheck-20261027/README.md). The separate supplemental probes now observed all nine overlay variants at `TERM=dumb` 40×14. The Detail panel opened and closed; its final idle-prompt predicate was too specific after focus moved to transcript. Human matrix is still 0/15.\n\n**Release state:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains a prerelease on source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; `origin/main` still resolves to that commit. Stable `v1.0.0` is not published. Issues #1 and #2 remain open. Exact-RC T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, live provider/standalone, independent acceptance, and human terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Keep publication gated.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 02:01 UTC)\n\n**RC10 terminal evidence update:** PR #264 carries the scripted terminal evidence update on the current main base. No product source changes are included in this evidence slice. Earlier interrupted Detail-overlay probes are classified as harness-incomplete. Across the original and corrected supplemental PTY probes, all nine source `Overlay` variants were observed at `TERM=dumb`, 40×14, including a separately retained Detail capture; the Detail capture’s post-Esc idle predicate remained harness-limited. Follow-up synthetic command approval attempts did not complete and are not product failures. See [supplemental overlay evidence](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/README.md). The ACC-TUI-A11Y disposition remains `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`: the earlier intermittent `TERM=dumb` 100×30 cancellation timeouts remain, other terminal configurations are not covered by this supplemental run, and human acceptance remains separate.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 01:42 UTC)\n\n**Source and published candidate:** `origin/main` is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` (PR #262). Public tag and prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.10` resolve to that exact source. Its Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`; installer SHA-256 is `5620d56ef6f8d637fc102ae2c8ea3b055effbc4069243a2df68b67520b1e2302`. Strict GitHub attestation verification passed for the archive and checksum index; the release workflow [40424225668](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40424225668), exact-main CI [40419408166](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40419408166), and exact-main CodeQL [40419408185](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40419408185) succeeded on the RC10 source. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n\n**RC10 qualification evidence:** E2 lifecycle and identity-bound positive install evidence is recorded separately; the cross-platform positive identity matrix passed 8/8 on Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12, and Fedora 40 with Node 22/24. Application process-death recovery passed and is explicitly not power-loss evidence. Strict artifact and install checks passed. Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 in workflow [40433818126](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40433818126); the comparison matched both runner outputs to each other and all six published artifact digests. The archived evidence is [here](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/cross-runner/README.md), with `repro-evidence.json` SHA-256 `f393db75f06cc9675b34941c8d5e42cb7de0f01892cc2f8e64a48c9998d4fcc7`.\n\nInstalled terminal evidence is not fully accepted. Scripted E3 remains `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`: one late-stream Ctrl-C case returned idle after 27.89 seconds against the five-second criterion; passing retries remain recorded but do not erase that observation. The expanded ACC-TUI-A11Y probe sampled ten readable states with zero color-setting SGR codes and a complete 40-column approval hint, but two full runs timed out waiting for Esc tool cancellation at `TERM=dumb` 100×30, one isolated retry passed, and the supplemental probes later observed all nine overlay variants in one configuration, including the separately retained Detail capture. The supplemental run does not clear the timeout anomaly or qualify other configurations. Evidence and failed attempts are preserved under [RC10 scripted terminal evidence](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/README.md). The required human real-terminal matrix remains `0/15`; its exact-RC10 blank worksheet is [here](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual/README.md). Neither scripted evidence nor worksheet is human acceptance.\n\n**Outstanding external and exact-RC gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN. Its last update is 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC; no compatible immutable T2 successor or independent custody acceptance has been recorded, and this implementation lane has not accessed held-out payloads. Issue [#2](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/2) remains OPEN; no T4 qualification run is recorded. Standalone profiles requiring held-out tasks, exact-RC live provider qualification, independent X5 acceptance, and the human terminal matrix are not established. The E5 OpenRouter task lane is separately claimed; do not duplicate it without handoff.\n\n**Disposition:** RC10 is a published prerelease and has passed its source/release pipeline, but is not an accepted release candidate. Keep stable promotion gated on all remaining exact-RC, independent, human, T2/T3/T4, standalone/provider, and terminal gates. This checkpoint supersedes the 2026-10-26 21:10 UTC RC9 checkpoint below; earlier entries remain historical records.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 21:10 UTC)\n\n**Current source and post-merge gates:** `origin/main` is `30f1b89a88bac81d8ab2d4f1e6800e1978a61f38`, the merge commit for PR #261. Its post-merge CI [40401857374](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40401857374) and CodeQL [40401857568](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40401857568) were still running at this checkpoint; do not call the new main source gate complete yet. PR #261's exact-head CI [40396216500](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40396216500) and CodeQL [40396216414](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40396216414) passed before merge. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed exact head `20170c51…3636 tokens truncated…ownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) remains the latest release, but its tag resolves to `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, before PR #252 and PR #254. Its Linux archive digest remains `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. RC8 reproducibility and isolated-prefix provenance checks apply only to that earlier artifact. It is not an accepted RC for current `main`; a candidate from the current source must be rebuilt and qualified. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The RC8 signing identity remains reported by GitHub as unverified (`bad_email`); stable signing must use a GitHub-verified identity.\n\n**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open. The latest public metadata-only custody request (12:18 UTC) has no custodian response; do not access held-out payloads or begin the held-out run before independent custody acceptance. The last recorded human terminal matrix is 0/15, with real-terminal operator evidence still required. Exact-current-RC installed qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, T2/T3/T4 qualification and independent exact-RC acceptance are not established. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted but gated on all required acceptance and stable-artifact checks.\n\nThe 08:05 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence; this update supersedes its source, CI, candidate and current blocker status.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 08:05 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`. Exact-main CI run [40279197785](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197785) completed successfully on this commit; all three required jobs (`test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`) passed. CodeQL run [40279197561](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197561) passed. The requirements enforcement and version synchronization checks passed on the same source: 123 requirements (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), with package components at `1.0.0-rc.8`.\n\n**RC8 construction and reproducibility:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) was published at 07:26 UTC and resolves to the exact source commit above. Its Linux archive has GitHub asset digest `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. Cross-runner RC reproducibility workflow [40286712425](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40286712425) completed successfully against that exact tag, including Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builds and artifact comparison. An installed RC8 copy was also provenance-verified on the Ubuntu desktop in an isolated qualification prefix ([setup record](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6411066559)); this was not the user's normal Nexus installation and is not full installed-RC acceptance. The tag's local GPG signature verifies, but GitHub reports it as unverified (`bad_email`); the stable tag must use a signer identity that GitHub verifies against the signing key. The earlier RC6-to-RC7 upgrade attempt failed because RC6 rejected GitHub's signed release-asset redirect. The redirect allowlist and URL-secret redaction are present in RC8; the RC6 installation was not changed by the isolated RC8 check.\n\n**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN; the custodian has not responded to the metadata-only request, and private custody acceptance, evaluator compatibility and sealing are not established. Held-out qualification has not started. Exact-RC provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3 and nine-class T4 qualification, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. The human terminal matrix remains 0/15; automated PTY checks do not satisfy it. Stable `v1.0.0` is not published. Campaign status remains `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted but gated on acceptance.\n\nThe 06:24 checkpoint immediately below is retained as a historical snapshot; this update supersedes its CI conclusion, RC publication state, cross-runner status, and current blocker summary.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 06:24 UTC at `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, incorporating PR #249 (`8e562b0f3406e94003806746cb69a5258f72a59f`) and PR #250. PR #249 merged at 05:57 UTC and PR #250 merged at 06:20 UTC. On this exact source, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` confirms all components are `1.0.0-rc.8`. CodeQL run [40279197561](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197561) passed. Exact-main CI [40279197785](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197785) is still running; its Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed Rust tests and release builds and were running the CLI test suite at 06:24 UTC. The current checkpoint does not claim full CI success.\n\n**RC and publication state:** The latest public prerelease remains `v1.0.0-rc.7`; `v1.0.0-rc.8` is not yet tagged or published. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The `rc.8` source version is not itself evidence of an accepted or installed RC. No release artifact should be published until every required acceptance gate passes.\n\n**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1), for held-out T2/T3 corpus custody, remains OPEN (last observed update 02:33:48 UTC); the required custodian sealing and independent private-custody acceptance are not established. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone coverage, T3/T4 qualification, installed exact-RC qualification, independent RC acceptance, and the human terminal matrix (0/15 at last evidence) remain incomplete. Treat the older entries below as historical snapshots; they do not supersede these current observations.\n\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 02:27 UTC at `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` remains `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`. CI run [40255529634](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529634) and CodeQL run [40255529667](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529667) both completed successfully on that exact commit. CI passed the Node 22/24 and Linux test matrices, requirements enforcement, security gates, package build and reproducibility, SBOM checks, and package/install smoke checks.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17eb1-62db-7543-bdeb-97095e0e59b7","create_time":1793126945.6740093}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
