{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:56:33.932Z","ordinal":423566,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17eb8-aa8c-74b1-b84a-33db3f46b6a7","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed PR #280 at head `c1bb5573acdb3fa89d1735f37999482c22b9fb39` against base `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`. Diff SHA-256 matches the supplied `b87c4994afc29d37165355428353877cda9432f5730a322e043e9dc414ba6f38`.\n\n**Finding:** [upgrade_journal.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/state-home-alias-backup/cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:534) checks whether the launcher is a symlink, then creates a temporary symlink and renames it over the launcher at lines 540–541. A regular file created or swapped into `linkPath` after the check can therefore be overwritten by `renameSync`. The new tests cover a regular launcher already present before recovery, but not this check-to-rename race ([upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/state-home-alias-backup/cli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:86)). The preservation guard needs to make replacement safe against that race.\n\nThe `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` backup/restore routing, symlinked-HOME override matching, and pending-restore replay before the REPL are otherwise consistently routed in the reviewed changes. I did not run tests, per instruction.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17eb3-a9cd-72c2-8903-33ec16779f56","create_time":1793127393.9321213}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":20507}}
