{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T19:02:38.856Z","ordinal":423924,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17ebe-3c08-78e1-9595-0098ce76e425","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed exact HEAD `78b425bffadc894ba746693ee8d9952423666e23` against base `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`; diff SHA-256 `e3ba9bb0b81843819e1ad734bd8a3ce442c144cda6ecfec840f14fadce3b6cdf`.\n\nThe check-to-replacement race is handled on the normal error path: the code moves the entry aside, checks its type and inode, then restores a changed entry using an exclusive hard link. The regression at [upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/state-home-alias-backup/cli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:100) injects a regular file after inspection and before the real rename, and verifies its contents and the recovery-required journal.\n\nOne crash window remains. If the process terminates after `renameSync(linkPath, displacedLink)` at [upgrade_journal.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/state-home-alias-backup/cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:548) but before restoration or installation, the prior entry remains under a random hidden filename. Recovery does not record or scan that filename, so the launcher is absent at its expected path; the regression covers the catch path, not process termination. Add recovery handling for displaced entries or otherwise make this transition recoverable after a crash."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17eb3-a9cd-72c2-8903-33ec16779f56","create_time":1793127758.8560936}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":20519}}
