{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T19:04:11.310Z","ordinal":424015,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17ebf-a52e-7001-a2b3-1cd733258a33","call_id":"call_98386977ec0b4894bdc1f8559e1836e9","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for evidence file SHA-256 `8fa49c2369f42f2f09707bc1f21a60f515501d30222939925731afc80bfec7cc`.\\n\\nThe three archived receipts match the check IDs and usage summaries, identify the RC10 ChatGPT provider calls, and contain no credential values or workspace content. The evidence satisfies the ChatGPT verify-on-RC row while keeping its claim limited to that provider gate. No provider tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since `2026-10-26T12:18:17Z`, Issue #1 gained coordinator comments #6415806863 and #6423073471. The issue was last updated at `2026-10-26T17:37:53Z`; all 22 comments are from the coordinator, with no custodian response or handoff. The claims search also shows no active custodian/author claim.\\n\\nAt current `origin/main@303ea322a7148b4a9d1a8231d7ce1c8f824bbae4`, the evaluator still rejects legacy `hidden.command` for qualification (`eval/validate.mjs:49`); the README still requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeat custody checks, and a new manifest identity. The `2026-10-27T05:30:30Z` release-loop record reports RC10 published but still lists `blackbox_v1_custodian_sealing` as a blocker.\\n\\nNo private material was accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed exact HEAD `78b425bffadc894ba746693ee8d9952423666e23` against base `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`; diff SHA-256 `e3ba9bb0b81843819e1ad734bd8a3ce442c144cda6ecfec840f14fadce3b6cdf`.\\n\\nThe check-to-replacement race is handled on the normal error path: the code moves the entry aside, checks its type and inode, then restores a changed entry using an exclusive hard link. The regression at [upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/state-home-alias-backup/cli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:100) injects a regular file after inspection and before the real rename, and verifies its contents and the recovery-required journal.\\n\\nOne crash window remains. If the process terminates after `renameSync(linkPath, displacedLink)` at [upgrade_journal.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/state-home-alias-backup/cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:548) but before restoration or installation, the prior entry remains under a random hidden filename. Recovery does not record or scan that filename, so the launcher is absent at its expected path; the regression covers the catch path, not process termination. Add recovery handling for displaced entries or otherwise make this transition recoverable after a crash.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17eb3-a9cd-72c2-8903-33ec16779f56","create_time":1793127851.3103843}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
