{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T19:06:51.066Z","ordinal":424186,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17ec2-153a-7703-9a86-95a514deaaf1","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed exact HEAD `fd13a8ee7269bebd2d3d6b4f6a3ac77daa4e60a4` against base `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`; diff SHA-256 `84cef644a224f16e9330577644d4d55d78ee452d53c9e612ffdd82dbff071635`.\n\nThe same-inode check now recognizes an interrupted restore, removes the duplicate backup entry, and continues. The tests cover both a restored symlink and a regular launcher: the symlink case proceeds to the intended source link, while the regular file remains intact and recovery stays fail-closed. The earlier race test still verifies that a regular launcher substituted after inspection is preserved. No remaining blocker found in the reviewed recovery paths."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17eb3-a9cd-72c2-8903-33ec16779f56","create_time":1793128011.0663834}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":20534}}
