ipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:5:- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:6:- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:10:They also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:14:- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:46:| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n40565654437 sha=a2832c01a1bb552c7d9a0ef324424a80ecb48ee3 status=in_progress conclusion=\n40566060161 sha=fd13a8ee7269bebd2d3d6b4f6a3ac77daa4e60a4 status=in_progress conclusion=\n40562094616 sha=398a0babadb51ac01dd475a1697125ab716ee4c8 status=in_progress conclusion=\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":886703240}},"started_at_ms":1793128430556,"completed_at_ms":17931284334