{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T19:16:10.647Z","ordinal":424613,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17ec5-069e-7660-98c6-af7c51147c1b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8cae4a69-4e46-4bef-83c9-9bd3f38c158f","process_id":"13543","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'identity|Claude|273|RC10' /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-readiness-20261027/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -25; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-readiness-20261027 status --short; gh pr view 268 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json headRefOid,baseRefOid,statusCheckRollup --jq '\"head=\\(.headRefOid) base=\\(.baseRefOid)\" , (.statusCheckRollup[] | \"\\(.name // .context): \\(.status // .state)/\\(.conclusion // \"\")\")'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i 'identity|Claude|273|RC10' /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-readiness-20261027/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -25; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-readiness-20261027 status --short; gh pr view 268 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json headRefOid,baseRefOid,statusCheckRollup --jq '\"head=\\(.headRefOid) base=\\(.baseRefOid)\" , (.statusCheckRollup[] | \"\\(.name // .context): \\(.status // .state)/\\(.conclusion // \"\")\")'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"78:**Current release PRs:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264) is open at `97e3f72e4a5fe8676a0a30ea9f6e023147ad73a5` on current base `d2442b0`; CodeQL [40499839711](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499839711) passed and exact-head CI [40499840211](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499840211) is still running. PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) remains remotely at `bda6714ff885f2fd4fef736b84ca7005a9cddbdf`, based on the previous `303ea32` source. Its earlier CI and CodeQL passed on that older head. A local readiness candidate has been refreshed to `d2442b0`; requirement enforcement (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), RC10 version synchronization, and diff hygiene pass on the refreshed candidate. Independent review asked that the old 05:54 snapshot be clearly superseded; this checkpoint does so. The refreshed candidate still needs final-base review, owner push, and exact-head hosted checks.\n82:**Disposition:** Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC10 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Existing publication authorization remains gated on all required qualification and independent acceptance. The 05:54 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence and is superseded for source, PR #266 integration, current PR checks, and release-gate status by this checkpoint.\n90:**RC10 installation and terminal preparation:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The linked [RC10 desktop preflight record](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual-preflight/README.md) documents successful provenance-verified installation to an isolated qualification prefix on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`), with CLI identity `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)`. xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are present. This prepares the host only: the human matrix remains **0/15**. The operator must perform each of the five terminal environments at all three sizes and provide two genuine screenshots and a verdict per cell; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute.\n92:**Remaining exact-RC and release gates:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264) archives RC10 scripted observations and keeps the manual matrix separate; its remote head is `73bdc7d91b1b8925b522b052d89228d99bad4893` on a stale base, with all reported exact-head checks successful. Its manual worksheet is blank. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) still lacks custodian acceptance; the sealed public manifest alone is not private custody acceptance, and no held-out payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, standalone qualification, full installed-RC provider coverage, exact-RC cross-runner checks, the manual matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release is published; publication authorization remains granted but gated by acceptance.\n102:**Terminal observation and acceptance:** The user reports that the client rendered at the sizes they tried except in tmux inside GNOME Terminal; the smallest observed tmux window was 43×13. They said the remaining observations may take several days. No screenshots, exact installed-package identity, or cell-by-cell results were supplied. The 15-cell worksheet therefore remains 0/15 and unaccepted; the report is retained as provisional operator context only. Do not prompt while other gates can progress.\n116:**RC10 artifact boundary:** The latest published prerelease is [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, not current main. Its Linux archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. Previously completed RC10 artifact, installation, provenance and cross-runner checks apply only to that immutable artifact. Scripted terminal coverage remains partial; the required manual real-terminal matrix is 0/15. No exact-RC acceptance is established. Further source changes require constructing and qualifying a new candidate.\n118:**Held-out and human gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian acceptance recorded; no held-out payload was accessed and T2/T3/T4 acceptance is not established. The manual terminal matrix still requires operator evidence across five environments and three sizes. At 2026-10-27 03:49 UTC, I verified over SSH to `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`) that `/home/mike/nexus-rc10-manual-evidence/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md` exists and contains an unfilled 15-cell template with directories for every environment/size pair. No cell evidence is present; the installed candidate identity is blank. Any matrix run must use the eventual installed RC. Scripted PTY output is not a substitute.\n120:**RC8 dogfood export:** `/home/mike/nexus-code/nexus-session-session_20261026_162439_34f2cnrn.json` records an exploratory codebase-review objective, 28 model-written findings, no candidate identity, zero validation receipts, `unverifiedChangesPending=true`, and a `VERIFIER_FAILED` incomplete outcome. Treat the findings as hypotheses requiring reproduction; they are not verified defects or RC acceptance evidence.\n122:**Disposition:** Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; RC10 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated on all mandatory qualification and independent acceptance. The user-selected distribution target is the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n186:**Candidate and publication state:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) remains the latest release, but its tag resolves to `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, before PR #252 and PR #254. Its Linux archive digest remains `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. RC8 reproducibility and isolated-prefix provenance checks apply only to that earlier artifact. It is not an accepted RC for current `main`; a candidate from the current source must be rebuilt and qualified. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The RC8 signing identity remains reported by GitHub as unverified (`bad_email`); stable signing must use a GitHub-verified identity.\n196:**RC8 construction and reproducibility:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) was published at 07:26 UTC and resolves to the exact source commit above. Its Linux archive has GitHub asset digest `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. Cross-runner RC reproducibility workflow [40286712425](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40286712425) completed successfully against that exact tag, including Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builds and artifact comparison. An installed RC8 copy was also provenance-verified on the Ubuntu desktop in an isolated qualification prefix ([setup record](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6411066559)); this was not the user's normal Nexus installation and is not full installed-RC acceptance. The tag's local GPG signature verifies, but GitHub reports it as unverified (`bad_email`); the stable tag must use a signer identity that GitHub verifies against the signing key. The earlier RC6-to-RC7 upgrade attempt failed because RC6 rejected GitHub's signed release-asset redirect. The redirect allowlist and URL-secret redaction are present in RC8; the RC6 installation was not changed by the isolated RC8 check.\n297:**Next evidence:** Finish the RC7 Release workflow and verify its exact artifact identity and provenance. Finish exact-head CI for PRs #243–245, integrate only after required review and checks, and requalify resulting main before constructing a subsequent candidate. The `cli/src/agent.ts` defect-remediation handoff is recorded for KimiCode-defect-scan; its implementation is not yet present in that branch. Resolve independent held-out custody and evaluator compatibility before beginning protected qualification; then qualify an eligible installed RC and complete the manual terminal matrix. Keep source gates, RC construction, installed-RC qualification, and stable-release checks distinct.\n331:**Checkpoint failure:** `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus` resolves to the installed `v1.0.0-rc.1` package and reports `1.0.0-rc.1 (cb364c386c42)`. That immutable package lacks checkpoint choices, so the reported failure before turn start is reproducible by version identity and will persist on RC1. The fix is integrated in PR #147 (TUI/sidecar) and PR #153 (legacy REPL): before starting a turn, Nexus asks the operator whether to use read-only mode, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitive-content risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Both PRs passed exact-head checks, and the subsequent exact-main CI on `dac465d` passed. No replacement package has been installed. The public release page still has RC1 only; RC2 has a tag but no published release, and RC3 has neither tag nor release.\n333:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\n349:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags remain `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor and checkpoint-choice fix. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at exact main and reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.2`. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. A new candidate must use the next RC identity after source CI and release prerequisites pass, then undergo installed-artifact qualification.\n363:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags are `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor. GitHub currently publishes RC1 as a prerelease; RC2 has a tag but no published release. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. The next candidate needs a fresh RC3 identity after its source/version checks; it must be installed and qualified before acceptance.\n389:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n435:- **Held-out corpus and custody:** Public T2 manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` remains the 40-task identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`; T3 public manifest identity remains `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4bfa0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response since 2026-10-21 12:21 UTC. Current evaluator qualification rejects the sealed T2 corpus's legacy `hidden.command` format; the documented path requires a custodian-owned compatible immutable successor and repeated custody checks. Private digest re-derivation, exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective access separation, and current custody acceptance remain unverified here. No payload, validator, reference solution, or hidden answer was accessed, and no held-out run has started.\n450:- **Held-out custody and qualification:** The custodian previously accepted the sealed 40-task manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b` and its private digest/reference validation. This does not establish evaluator acceptance or T2 qualification. The implementing agent has not accessed private payloads. No held-out run has started because evaluator confidentiality preflight remains unaccepted and corpus/evaluator schema compatibility is unresolved.\n460:- **Evaluator boundary and T2 custody:** PR #33's exact source CI passes resource-bound and Git-history canary fixtures, but the independent unconditional-system-mount finding remains open. Separately, the custodian report accepts the sealed manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, its custody, author-session provenance, private digest validation, and reference validation; private payloads were not inspected for this checkpoint. The sealed tasks use legacy `hidden: { dir, into, command }` checks, while evaluator qualification requires `blackbox-v1`. Custody acceptance does not resolve this format mismatch or evaluator-boundary acceptance. No T2 qualification has started.\n472:- **Held-out T2 custody:** The custodian reported re-derived manifest, 40 task, and 40 private-payload digest matches; isolated author-session audits; and 40/40 reference validation. The public manifest identity is `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`. At 10:38:44 UTC the custodian recorded moving the store and quarantine to `root:root` mode `0700` (task/reference subdirectories `0500`) without changing contents or manifest identity, and explicitly accepted sealed-manifest custody under this boundary. Coordinator verification was limited to metadata (`stat`, `namei`, and a denied `ls` as uid `mike`); private payloads were not inspected. This is custody evidence, not T2 qualification: held-out execution remains blocked on host provisioning, frozen resources, and an installed RC.\n494:  - `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (`86bdbe6`, PR #20) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/version identity across independent Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders.\n562:| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\n596:### Release identity and source gates\n614:- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nhead=9c153d984ff92eaafa413564ec2401a2a22ecb13 base=fc582c66bf70e00938eedc0ce3cafc635f582540\ntest-matrix (22): IN_PROGRESS/\njavascript-typescript: COMPLETED/SUCCESS\ntest-matrix (24): IN_PROGRESS/\nCodeQL: COMPLETED/SUCCESS\nCodeRabbit: SUCCESS/\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":718746049}},"started_at_ms":1793128569927,"completed_at_ms":1793128570647}}
