{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T19:19:41.341Z","ordinal":424802,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17ecd-d61d-7e11-abaf-aaf73294c853","call_id":"call_b3f28b873f854f5f8cd9a249d0f11cac","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4064)\nTotal output lines: 75\n\n# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 19:12 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `fc582c66bf70e00938eedc0ce3cafc635f582540`, merging PR #279 after #278 and #277. Post-merge CI [40566591904](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591904) is running Node 22 and Node 24 on that exact SHA; CodeQL [40566591883](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591883) passed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL also passed on parent `cf05322` (runs [40561348972](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40561348972) and [40561348985](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40561348985)). Source requirements and RC10 version-sync checks passed on `cf05322` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification). These are source-gate results, not installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** At 19:12 UTC, its remote head was `9c153d984ff92eaafa413564ec2401a2a22ecb13`, based on `main@fc582c66`. Node 22/24 CI was queued and CodeQL had started; prior head `398a0ba` passed Node 22, Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL, with Linux packaging still running. Those checks do not qualify the new merged-base head. This checkpoint update advances PR #268 again; its resulting head requires exact-head checks and independent review before merge.\n\n**Other source PRs:** PR [#279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/279) corrected the configured-hook race and retention error-accounting findings left by #277. It merged at `fc582c6` after exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux packaging, JavaScript/TypeScript, CodeQL, and independent read-only review passed. PR [#278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/278) merged at `cf05322` as exact head `d617937`; its checks passed and independent evidence review accepted the sanitized ChatGPT receipts. That provider evidence covers the ChatGPT verify-on-RC row only. Open PR [#280](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/280) addresses configured state-directory recovery; Node 22/24 are running, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL pass. Open PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) records RC10 cross-runner reproducibility; its Node 22/24 and JavaScript/TypeScript checks are running. These PRs do not establish the remaining provider/standalone matrix or release acceptance.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Exact cross-runner reproducibility passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca`; a successor candidate from current main still requires its own reproducibility run. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; no cell result or screenshot is recorded. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\n\nThe 18:38, 17:31, and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, CI, and requirements status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 17:31 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and post-merge checks:** `origin/main` is `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`, integrating PR #275 after PR #273. Exact-main CI [40537474824](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40537474824) passed the Node 22, Node 24, and `linux-x86_64` jobs on `ceabfcc`; CodeQL [40537475057](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40537475057) also passed on that SHA. Earlier post-merge CI [40536704465](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40536704465) and CodeQL [40536704530](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40536704530) passed on `e94208d`. These establish source CI for those exact commits; they do not establish RC acceptance or release qualification.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** GitHub reports PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) open at exact remote head `d37746f20da27a8b11a9c25c14c08fe0db197add`, based on current `main` `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. All exact-head checks passed: Node 22, Node 24, and `linux-x86_64` in CI run [40544627770](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40544627770), JavaScript/TypeScript in run `40544627915`, and CodeQL [122332399521](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/122332399521). The earlier independent review found stale attribution; the local follow-up corrects it and records the completed Linux result. This corrected follow-up is not yet pushed or independently reviewed. No merge is claimed.\n\n**Merged fixes:** PR #274 merged at `b17c64a2c84a6324fb78bc55d3a39a7c9cc4ed47`; its exact post-merge CI [40529300314](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40529300314) and CodeQL [40529300519](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40529300519) passed. PR #273 merged at `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2`; PR #275 merged at `ceabfcc`. Both merge commits have the passing exact post-merge checks listed above.\n\n**Other release-path PRs:** PR [#276](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/276) records a synthetic-only qualification-host preflight (10/10) bound to `ceabfcc`; its Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass, while Linux CI remains in progress. Its evidence does not establish custodian access, held-out qualification, or acceptance. PR [#277](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/277) addresses configured Git-hook execution during checkpoint and retention operations. Its exact diff received conflicting review dispositions: a GitHub review comment requested changes for a hook-discovery race and retention error accounting, while a separate read-only review returned ACCEPT. The findings remain unresolved pending the claimed implementation owner's response; no acceptance or merge is claimed. Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks pass; Linux CI remains in progress.\n\n**Requirements and qualification:** A clean disposable snapshot of `origin/main@ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227` passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`. The first requirements invocation on the documentation-dirty readiness worktree was correctly refused by its clean-worktree preflight and is not treated as a gate result. The existing [RC10 OpenRouter evidence bundle](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md) establishes a pinned provider verification and one passing synthetic small task; this does not establish the broader provider/standalone matrix. Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains an unaccepted prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without independent custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining provider/standalone profiles, cross-runner exact-RC reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and scripted terminal gates remain incomplete.\n\n**Human terminal acceptance:** The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15**. The operator cannot run the requested xterm 80×24 cell now; no cell result or screenshots are inferred. The prepared Ubuntu/GNOME host and worksheet remain available for a later genuine operator run. Scripted PTY evidence does not replace the human matrix. Publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance gates.\n\nThe 15:12 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical …64 tokens truncated…PRs [#269](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/269) and [#270](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/270) after #271 and #272. Exact-main CI [40521505143](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505143) and CodeQL [40521505001](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505001) both passed on `3b7af5d`; CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux tests, security gates, packaging, reproducibility, package smoke, and installer smoke. PR #269 merge-commit CI [40519862728](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40519862728) passed on `f059770`. These runs establish CI for their exact commits, not the RC10 release gates.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** The owner refreshed PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) onto `main`; GitHub shows it open and mergeable at head `98f87bee6ca112e6d50f6fb2bc480fc47723c648`, based on `3b7af5d3cd46ab1b83e9c8df9862e09cee22b1a7`. Its Node 22, Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass; Linux packaging/reproducibility run [40524245685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40524245685) is still pending. The 14:38 checkpoint update was independently accepted (diff SHA-256 `c8cf46163cd8be8666ea86e8a95a7483588e10aa3e8775fbfa213ce55895d41e`). The current local follow-up records terminal main and #269 CI plus the latest PR state; it has not been pushed, and no PR merge is claimed.\n\n**Merged hook remediations and residual:** PRs #269 (retention shell/hook execution) and #270 (checkpoint Git hooks) are merged at `f059770` and `3b7af5d`; both now have passing exact-merge CI. The merged implementation passes `core.hooksPath=/dev/null` to relevant Git commands. Configured `reference-transaction` hooks may remain callable despite that setting; this was independently reproduced and accepted on a local follow-up to #269 (`d349068`), whose focused tests passed 17/17 on Git 2.54.0 and Git 2.43.0 plus `tsc --noEmit`. That follow-up is not on current main or the merged #269 head and needs a separately refreshed fix and exact-head validation; its source and test files are currently claimed by another agent.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. The human five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15** and pending. The user's informal observation is that rendering works at tested sizes except tmux in GNOME Terminal, where the smallest usable size is 43×13; there are no per-cell records or screenshots, so human acceptance is not established. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open, last updated 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC, with no custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody and host acceptance, live provider/standalone, independent exact-RC, scripted terminal, and human acceptance gates remain incomplete. Publication authorization remains gated on every required acceptance gate.\n\nThe 14:38, 13:56 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, and CI status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 12:46 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and post-merge CI:** `origin/main` is `1d9357ee63b1066a891584a898842814de614fbf`, integrating PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264). Its exact-head CI [40499840211](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499840211) and CodeQL [40499839711](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499839711) passed before merge. Post-merge CodeQL [40505388849](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40505388849) passed on `1d9357e`; post-merge CI [40505388775](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40505388775) is still running both Node 22 and Node 24 CLI suites. No result is inferred before they finish.\n\n**Readiness PR and local full-suite result:** PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) remains remotely at `bda6714ff885f2fd4fef736b84ca7005a9cddbdf`, based on `303ea322a7148b4a9d1a8231d7ce1c8f824bbae4`; it is conflicting with current `main` and its old successful checks are stale. The claimed local branch had been refreshed through `bff9f13085368e6cc269b1bb294db5b3b810bd7a`; the updated branch now incorporates `1d9357e` and is awaiting final independent review. No push or merge is claimed.\n\nAn isolated immutable snapshot at `9344df578f8a39a55d82ead0f15c4811864d21f8` built successfully, but `make test` exited 2: 1,769 passed, 2 failed, and 1 was skipped. `eval_integrity.test.ts` observed three OOM kills during this host run, which did not have the dedicated capped workspace mount; the log does not establish that the missing mount caused those kills. `eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts` failed its precondition because `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` and `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT` were not configured. `/tmp`, `/var/tmp`, and `/home` were all on the same ext4 device. These are incomplete host-fixture checks, not a passing suite or a demonstrated source regression. The complete output is retained at `/var/tmp/nexus-pr268-make-test-9344df5.log`. Current exact-main hosted CI is still running the full CLI suite with its configured cgroups and capped tmpfs.\n\n**Release and acceptance gates:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains a prerelease; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. The human real-terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user's report of rendering at 43×13 in tmux on GNOME Terminal is not the full matrix and had no captured screenshots. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN, last updated 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC, with no recorded custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, live provider/standalone, independent exact-RC, and human acceptance gates remain incomplete. Publication authorization remains gated on all required acceptance.\n\nThe 12:42 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence and superseded for current branch, CI, and test status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Historical terminal cancellation checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 02:11 UTC)\n\nFive targeted synthetic installed-RC10 cancellation rechecks at `TERM=dumb`, 100×30 completed with Esc delays from 0 to 1 second; idle return measured 0.405–0.507 seconds. The two earlier full-matrix timeouts remained valid and unresolved; this targeted recheck did not promote ACC-TUI-A11Y or E3. Evidence and raw PTY streams are preserved in [the cancellation timing recheck](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/cancel-timing-recheck-20261027/README.md). Human terminal acceptance remained 0/15. This historical record is retained from the PR #264 merge history.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 12:42 UTC)\nPR281 e17419414b3e01d835fd54ae7589e3aad50272d9\ntest-matrix (22)\tIN_PROGRESS\t\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566980576/job/122410756827\njavascript-typescript\tCOMPLETED\tSUCCESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566980672/job/122410757049\ntest-matrix (24)\tIN_PROGRESS\t\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566980576/job/122410757841\nCodeQL\tCOMPLETED\tSUCCESS\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/122411369006\n\t\t\t\nPR268 005cd78ceea08292f3325530424c7697424d8518\ntest-matrix (22)\tIN_PROGRESS\t\thttps://github.co