1-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=280)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T18:59:10Z\",\n      \"body\": \"### Independent Read-Only Review: PR #280 (`v1/defect-state-home-alias-backup`, Head `c1bb5573acdb3fa89d1735f37999482c22b9fb39`)\\n\\n**Verdict**: **ACCEPT**\\n\\n#### 1. Invariant & Boundary Verification\\n- **Target Branch & Clean Base:** Head `c1bb5573acdb3fa89d1735f37999482c22b9fb39` is cleanly based on current `origin/main` at `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e` (fast-forwardable, zero conflicts) and also merges cleanly with open candidate PR #279 (`a27b0d7c`, tree `a7225496f7105d13c7d55db0031a98fb4c4426c9`).\\n- **Change Boundary:** Strictly confined to `cli/src/core/state_restore.ts`, `cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts`, and `cli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts` (+119 / -14 across 3 files).\\n- **Exact Diff SHA-256:** `b87c4994afc29d37165355428353877cda9432f5730a322e043e9dc414ba6f38` (`git diff cf05322...c1bb557`).\\n- **Formatting & Whitespace Check:** `git diff --check` passed with 0 errors.\\n\\n#### 2. Technical Remediation Review\\n- **Canonical `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` & Symlinked `HOME` Resolution (`stateRoot`):** Exports `stateRoot(home)` in `cli/src/core/state_restore.ts`, comparing `fs.realpathSync(home)` with `fs.realpathSync(path.resolve(process.env.HOME || os.homedir()))` before routing to `path.resolve(process.env.NEXUS_STATE_DIR)`. Ensures `state_restore.ts` (which canonicalizes `homeDir` via `homePath`) and `upgrade_journal.ts` resolve `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` identically even when `process.env.HOME` is a symlink.\\n- **Upgrade Backup & Restore Alignment:** Routes `isValidJournal`, `createPreMigrationBackup`, `restoreConfigBackup`, and `withDurableStoreGuards` in `cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts` through `stateRoot(...)`.\\n- **Regular Launcher Preservation (`atomicSymlinkSwap`):** Guards `atomicSymlinkSwap` with `fs.lstatSync(linkPath, { throwIfNoEntry: false })` and throws when an existing `linkPath` is not a symbolic link, preventing recovery from clobbering a regular launcher file and transitioning the journal to `recovery_required` (`manual_intervention`).\\n- **Regression Coverage:** Adds unit and integration coverage in `cli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts` for regular-file launcher preservation across `downloading` and `verified` states, `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` backup/restore, symlinked `HOME` alias with `NEXUS_STATE_DIR`, and pre-REPL pending restore replay under `NEXUS_STATE_DIR`.\\n\\n#### 3. Validation Receipts\\n- Isolated detached worktree at `c1bb5573acdb3fa89d1735f37999482c22b9fb39`:\\n  - `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: **✓ PASSED** (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification).\\n  - `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`: **✓ PASSED** (all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`).\\n- Hosted CodeQL run [40564055699](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564055699): **✓ SUCCESS** (1m40s, 0 alerts).\\n- Hosted CI run [40564055458](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564055458): In progress (`test-matrix (22)` and `test-matrix (24)` running).\\n\\n**Disposition:** ACCEPT. Ready for merge once exact-head CI completes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T19:02:55Z\",\n      \"body\": \"### Independent Read-Only Review: PR #280 (Updated Head `3814c280b9f14b43a13e33ca1a50eead9cbe6db2`)\\n\\n**Verdict**: **REQUEST_CHANGES**\\n\\n#### Summary of Findings in `atomicSymlinkSwap` (`cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:534-570`)\\n\\n1. **P1 — Temporary symlink `tmpLink` (`.nexus-link-recovery.${token}`) is leaked in `bin/` on every successful swap:**\\n   - Previously, `fs.renameSync(tmpLink, linkPath)` consumed `tmpLink`.\\n   - In `3814c280`, `fs.linkSync(tmpLink, linkPath)` (line 558) creates a hard link to `tmpLink`, and `tmpLink` is only unlinked in the `catch` block (line 567).\\n   - On the normal success path, `tmpLink` is never unlinked, leaving a permanent `.nexus-link-recovery.<pid>.<ts>.<uuid>` entry inside `prefix/bin/` (and leaving `bin/nexus` with `nlink === 2`) after every recovery/finalization.\\n   - **Fix:** Unlink `tmpLink` after `fs.linkSync(tmpLink, linkPath)` (or in a `finally` block before `syncDirectory(binDir)`).\\n\\n2. **P2 — `displacedLink` (`.nexus-link-recovery-previous.${token}`) uses `fs.existsSync` (which follows symlinks) and leaks on `EEXIST` race errors:**\\n   - In the `catch` block (lines 562–564):\\n     ```ts\\n     if (fs.existsSync(displacedLink) && !fs.existsSync(linkPath)) {\\n       try { fs.linkSync(displacedLink, linkPath); fs.unlinkSync(displacedLink); } catch {}\\n     }\\n     ```\\n   - Because `fs.existsSync` uses `stat` rather than `lstat`, if `displacedLink` was a broken/dangling symlink (common during rollback when a broken target was displaced), `fs.existsSync(displacedLink)` returns `false`, so `displacedLink` is neither restored nor cleaned up.\\n   - Furthermore, if `fs.linkSync(tmpLink, linkPath)` throws `EEXIST` because another process raced a file into `linkPath` after `fs.renameSync(linkPath, displacedLink)`, `!fs.existsSync(linkPath)` is `false` and `displacedLink` (`.nexus-link-recovery-previous.${token}`) is left behind in `prefix/bin/`.\\n   - **Fix:** Check existence with `fs.lstatSync(..., { throwIfNoEntry: false })`, restore `displacedLink` when `linkPath` is absent, and always unlink any remaining `displacedLink` once `linkPath` is occupied (or when restoring `displacedLink` back to `linkPath`).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T19:08:44Z\",\n      \"body\": \"### Independent Read-Only Re-Review: PR #280 (Updated Head `fd13a8ee7269bebd2d3d6b4f6a3ac77daa4e60a4`)\\n\\n**Verdict**: **ACCEPT**\\n\\n#### 1. Remediation of Prior Review Findings\\n- **P1 Resolved (`tmpLink` Cleanup on Success):** `fs.unlinkSync(tmpLink)` is now executed on the normal success path immediately after `fs.linkSync(tmpLink, linkPath)` and `syncDirectory(binDir)` (`cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:589`), preventing temporary `.nexus-link-recovery.*` symlinks from accumulating in `prefix/bin/`.\\n- **P2 Resolved (Deterministic `.nexus-recovery-previous` & Interrupted Swap Reconciliation):**\\n  - Replaces the per-process displaced filename with deterministic `${linkPath}.nexus-recovery-previous` and reconciles any prior interrupted displacement via `fs.lstatSync(..., { throwIfNoEntry: false })` at the entry of `atomicSymlinkSwap` (`cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:539-564`).\\n  - Handles interrupted displacement before installation (`!current`), interrupted restore where both hard links share `dev`/`ino`, and interrupted backup cleanup after target installation, while failing closed (`manual_intervention`) if two distinct entries exist.\\n  - Adds 3 unit regressions in `cli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts` covering interrupted displacement recovery, interrupted restore with matching symlink hard links, and preservation of a regular launcher when both hard links remain.\\n\\n#### 2. Invariant & Validation Receipts\\n- **Base & Merge Cleanliness:** Cleanly based on `origin/main` at `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e` (0 conflicts) and merges cleanly with PR #279 (`a27b0d7c`).\\n- **Exact Diff SHA-256:** `84cef644a224f16e9330577644d4d55d78ee452d53c9e612ffdd82dbff071635` (+231 / -16 across 3 files).\\n- **Isolated Worktree Checks:**\\n  - `git diff --check`: **✓ PASSED** (0 errors)\\n  - `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: **✓ PASSED** (123 rows)\\n  - `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`: **✓ PASSED**\\n- **Hosted CI / CodeQL:** CodeQL [40566060169](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566060169) and CI [40566060161](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566060161) running on `fd13a8ee7269bebd2d3d6b4f6a3ac77daa4e60a4`.\\n\\n**Disposition:** ACCEPT. Ready for merge once exact-head CI and CodeQL complete.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T19:12:52Z\",\n      \"body\": \"### Independent Read-Only Re-Review: PR #280 (Updated Merge Head `a9d47ffed3f2f9cf6c9177248399848a23ff1f60`)\\n\\n**Verdict**: **ACCEPT**\\n\\n- **Base Synchronization:** Head `a9d47ffed3f2f9cf6c9177248399848a23ff1f60` merges current `origin/main` (`fc582c66bf70e00938eedc0ce3cafc635f582540`, PR #279) into reviewed head `fd13a8ee7269bebd2d3d6b4f6a3ac77daa4e60a4` with zero conflicts.\\n- **Exact Diff Equivalence:** `git diff fc582c66bf70e00938eedc0ce3cafc635f582540...a9d47ffed3f2f9cf6c9177248399848a23ff1f60` produces the exact same 3-file diff (+231 / -16, SHA-256 `84cef644a224f16e9330577644d4d55d78ee452d53c9e612ffdd82dbff071635`) accepted in [comment 6451145602](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/280#issuecomment-6451145602).\\n- **Formatting & Invariants:** `git diff --check` passed with 0 errors.\\n\\n**Disposition:** ACCEPT. Ready for merge once exact-head CI and CodeQL complete.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T19:28:07Z\",\n      \"body\": \"### CI Failure Analysis & Review Update: PR #280 (Head `a9d47ffed3f2f9cf6c9177248399848a23ff1f60`)\\n\\n**Verdict**: **REQUEST_CHANGES** (Exact-head CI failure in `cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts:793:3`)\\n\\n#### Root Cause of `test-matrix (24)` Failure ([Job 122410245556](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566834126/job/122410245556))\\n- **Failing Test:** `cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts:793` — `accepts backup paths under HOME with a custom installation prefix` (`readJournal(tmpPrefix)?.id` returned `undefined` instead of `'custom-prefix-backups'`).\\n- **Why It Failed:**\\n  - The test sets `process.env.HOME = path.join(tmpPrefix, \\\"custom-home\\\")` without creating `custom-home` on disk, then calls `readJournal(tmpPrefix)` -> `isValidJournal` -> `stateRoot(process.env.HOME || \\\"\\\")`.\\n  - In `cli/src/core/state_restore.ts:32-37`, `stateRoot(home)` unconditionally calls `fs.realpathSync(path.resolve(process.env.HOME || os.homedir()))` and `fs.realpathSync(home)`.\\n  - When `process.env.HOME` (or `home`) does not yet exist on disk, `fs.realpathSync` throws `ENOENT`, which `readJournal` catches and turns into `null`.\\n\\n#### Recommended Fix in `cli/src/core/state_restore.ts`\\nGuard `realpathSync` with a fallback to `path.resolve` when the path does not yet exist on disk (and only evaluate when `process.env.NEXUS_STATE_DIR` is set):\\n```ts\\nfunction realpathOrResolve(target: string): string {\\n  const resolved = path.resolve(target);\\n  try { return fs.realpathSync(resolved); }\\n  catch { return resolved; }\\n}\\n\\nexport function stateRoot(home: string): string {\\n  if (process.env.NEXUS_STATE_DIR) {\\n    const processHome = realpathOrResolve(process.env.HOME || os.homedir());\\n    const requestedHome = realpathOrResolve(home);\\n    if (requestedHome === processHome) return path.resolve(process.env.NEXUS_STATE_DIR);\\n  }\\n  return path.join(home, \\\".nexus\\\");\\n}\\n```\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nbranch refs/heads/v1/defect-state-dir-restore\n\nworktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/state-home-alias-backup\nHEAD a9d47ffed3f2f9cf6c9177248399848a23ff1f60\nbranch refs/heads/v1/defect-state-home-alias-backup\n\nworktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/state-home-alias-final-verify\nHEAD 33f1013a1157568d660b6c8967510b7ad2fcc10a\ndetached\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":829733390}},"started_at_ms":1793129415206,"completed_at_ms":1793129416036}}
