{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T19:36:00.647Z","ordinal":425266,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17ec5-069e-7660-98c6-af7c51147c1b","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0fd1fd4c881a0bdecda709f353c46","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"PR #280’s failure is confirmed on both Node 22 and Node 24: its journal validator calls `realpathSync` even when no custom state directory is configured, so a legitimate not-yet-created HOME makes the journal unreadable. I’ve changed the alias check to resolve paths only when needed and to fall back safely for a missing HOME. I’m validating the fix before updating the PR; merge is withheld."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793129759865,"completed_at_ms":1793129760647}}
