nting (11.242906ms)\n  ✔ rejects malicious tar archive with escaping symlink (6.833517ms)\n  ✔ rejects archive containing disallowed entry types (FIFOs, devices, hardlinks) (6.510252ms)\n  ✔ rejects archive with duplicate entries (7.334876ms)\n  ✔ safely extracts valid archive and validates containment walk (24.275034ms)\n✔ Tar Archive Structural Safety Engine (REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-08) (97.887838ms)\n▶ Pre-Migration Backups & Migration/Downgrade Safety (REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-09)\n  ✔ creates protected config and state backups with 0600 file and 0700 dir permissions (120.886221ms)\n  ✔ restores configuration cleanly from backup with strict 0600 permissions (189.272306ms)\n✔ Pre-Migration Backups & Migration/Downgrade Safety (REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-09) (310.60936ms)\n▶ Machine-Readable Compatibility & Downgrade State Rejection (REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-07)\n  ✔ validates and generates valid compatibility metadata (2.057818ms)\n  ✔ package validator rejects unsupported compatibility schemas (71.148316ms)\n  ✔ rejects malformed compatibility metadata (0.589775ms)\n  ✔ refuses downgrade when target release state schema is older than current state schema (1.110318ms)\n  ✔ enforces minimum supported config and state schema versions (0.8154ms)\n  ✔ compares minimum updater versions using full SemVer prerelease ordering (0.658774ms)\n  ✔ rejects a target config schema older than the current config schema (0.512782ms)\n  ✔ applies legacy policy for releases lacking compatibility metadata (0.369159ms)\n✔ Machine-Readable Compatibility & Downgrade State Rejection (REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-07) (78.062498ms)\n▶ Durable Provenance & Package-Manager Protection (REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-10)\n  ✔ writes and reads durable installation provenance record (20.099882ms)\n  ✔ detects package-manager installations and blocks self-upgrade (16.069059ms)\n✔ Durable Provenance & Package-Manager Protection (REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-10) (36.515406ms)\n▶ Upgrade Journal, Crash Recovery & PATH Shadowing (REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-11, ACC-UPG-12)\n  ✔ resolves the state root when HOME has not been created yet (1.327525ms)\n  ✔ recovers an interrupted upgrade that crashed during downloading or staging (580.948768ms)\n  ✔ fails closed without deleting paths named by a malicious journal (85.194991ms)\n  ✔ rejects a staging path whose apparent parent is redirected by a symlink (48.9302ms)\n  ✔ accepts backup paths under HOME with a custom installation prefix (17.847078ms)\n  ✔ never executes a target binary redirected outside its version directory (457.431427ms)\n  ✔ does not repoint the launcher to an external source symlink during early recovery (40.843812ms)\n  ✔ rolls back when a contained target launcher exits unsuccessfully (420.133337ms)\n  ✔ recovers a crash during switching by reverting symlink to source installation (437.452288ms)\n  ✔ reverts launcher symlink to previous release with rollbackBinary (367.484813ms)\n  ✔ detects PATH shadowing when another nexus executable precedes prefix bin in PATH (2.034194ms)\n  ✔ retries an idempotent download once after a connection reset (73.495701ms)\n✔ Upgrade Journal, Crash Recovery & PATH Shadowing (REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-11, ACC-UPG-12) (2534.98412ms)\n▶ managed client invocation classification\n  ✔ keeps ambiguous maintenance options on the normal client path (1.792805ms)\n  ✔ releases the normal client lease only for recognized metadata and restore commands (0.51564ms)\n✔ managed client invocation classification (4.623189ms)\n▶ durable same-version transaction recovery\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash before-old-move (845.826488ms)\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash after-old-move (1259.184123ms)\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash after-new-move (1263.152846ms)\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash after-provenance (1199.803762ms)\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash after-link (1250.27982ms)\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash after-failed-displacement (1193.28853ms)\n  ✔ retains backups and truthful journal when restoring the link fails (821.846863ms)\n  ✔ preserves a regular launcher file and refuses downloading recovery (411.676741ms)\n  ✔ preserves a regular launcher file and refuses verified recovery (408.155313ms)\n  ✔ preserves a regular launcher substituted after inspection (418.712319ms)\n  ✔ restores an entry displaced by a process interrupted before launcher installation (792.164221ms)\n  ✔ continues after a process is interrupted while restoring the original symlink (472.50417ms)\n  ✔ preserves a regular launcher after an interrupted restore left both hard links (420.929068ms)\n  ✔ admits only one recovery when two contenders both observe the same stale lock (1206.507847ms)\n  ✔ reclaims a stale lock through the kernel guard without contention (462.847548ms)\n  ✔ reports the guard path and stays back while a live reclaimer holds the kernel guard (448.485886ms)\n  ✔ acquires the kernel guard after its holder is killed (646.850854ms)\n  ✔ does not leak descriptors across repeated guard contention (230.375331ms)\n  ✔ fails closed when the flock utility is unavailable (11.14261ms)\n  ✔ rejects a symlinked reclaim guard (7.748376ms)\n  ✔ rejects a FIFO reclaim guard (15.238558ms)\n  ✔ rejects a reclaim guard with unsafe permissions (8.248839ms)\n  ✔ does not touch the lock for a completed journal in a read-only package directory (742.393684ms)\n  ✔ does not finalize a launcher that reports the wrong release (887.140075ms)\n  ✔ refuses missing runtime components despite a successful version shim (57.808254ms)\n  ✔ uses the actual previous same-version package for explicit binary rollback (827.386025ms)\n  ✔ rejects a redirected backup without touching outside data (30.873316ms)\n  ✔ check-only leaves a pending transaction byte-for-byte unchanged (824.052132ms)\n  ✔ explicit recovery rejects invalid journals with an operational exit (863.398595ms)\n  ✔ bounds hung probes and kills their process group (283.576989ms)\n✔ durable same-version transaction recovery (18317.060881ms)\n▶ complete private state/config backup restore\n  ✔ reports byte progress while a single large file is still being copied (87.754973ms)\n  ✔ reports only aggregate backup progress and syncs each copied directory once (424.126859ms)\n  ✔ restores session payloads and config rather than copying an archive into config.env (833.635078ms)\n  ✔ captures and restores task and session state rooted at NEXUS_STATE_DIR (331.976075ms)\n  ✔ honors NEXUS_STATE_DIR when HOME is a symlink (268.89786ms)\n  ✔ flushes every automatic backup payload and containing directory before returning (109.888032ms)\n  ✔ preserves an existing backup when exclusive creation reports EEXIST (8.044978ms)\n  ✔ does not merge into an existing timestamped state backup directory (9.282202ms)\n  ✔ keeps committed restore barriers until staged payload cleanup succeeds (223.40917ms)\n  ✔ replays a prepared restore after interruption and blocks state access until recovery (242.050241ms)\n  ✔ fails closed when a per-store marker survives without its global journal (3.638154ms)\n  ✔ fails closed on dangling active and per-store restore markers (4.079304ms)\n  ✔ replays a pending restore rooted at NEXUS_STATE_DIR before starting the REPL (987.039462ms)\n  ✔ refuses upgrade --check before loading config when restore is pending (723.528943ms)\n  ✔ routes launches before legacy-client census and resumes after the legacy client exits (583.546614ms)\n  ✔ keeps a restore pending while a detached legacy client outlives its launcher (457.873831ms)\n✔ complete private state/config backup restore (5301.62992ms)\n▶ live transaction exceptions after each destructive boundary\n  ✔ restores the real previous same-version package after package_preserved (1887.826606ms)\n  ✔ restores the real previous same-version package after package_moved (1737.40234ms)\n  ✔ restores the real previous same-version package after provenance_written (1696.293