s repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nList changed filenames for a PR across all paginated file-list pages. \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_list_recent_issues\",\"description\":\"Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nReturn the most recent GitHub issues the user can access. `top_k` is t\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_list_user_org_memberships\",\"description\":\"Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nList the authenticated user's organization memberships. This tool is p\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_list_user_orgs\",\"description\":\"Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nList organizations the authenticated user is a member of. This tool is\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_merge_pull_request\",\"description\":\"Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nMerge a pull request immediately. Returns GitHub's merge result payloa\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_remove_reaction_from_pr\",\"description\":\"Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nRemove a reaction from a GitHub pull request. This tool is part of plu\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_remove_reaction_from_pr_review_comment\",\"description\":\"Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nRemove a reaction from a pull request review comment. This tool is par\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_search\",\"description\":\"Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nSearch GitHub files and return matching excerpts when available. Provi\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_search_prs\",\"description\":\"Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nSearch GitHub pull requests globally, by organization, or optionally b\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__faultline__faultline_get_pr_advisory\",\"description\":\"Risk advisory for a PR based on changed Go package paths.\\n\\nArgs: org_id, changed_packages (string[]), base_ref (optional), head_ref (optional), api_token\\nReturn\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__dumb_search\",\"description\":\"Dumb search (optional): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. This one-call lookup picks records by title word ove\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__get_observations\",\"description\":\"Step 3: Fetch selected useful details for the IDs chosen after reviewing the index and timeline. Any shortening is marked. Params: ids (required), orderBy, limi\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__get_tool_uses\",\"description\":\"Exceptional follow-up (raw tool I/O, rarely needed): fetch the ORIGINAL tool_input/tool_response for tool calls you already identified. Requires ids — run searc\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__important_workflow\",\"description\":\"SMART SEARCH (DEFAULT): Use the mem-search skill in three steps; no auto or guided modes. In server runtime, search, timeline, and get_observations use the conf\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__observation_search\",\"description\":\"Search generated observations by keyword (Postgres full-text) and, when the server has search by meaning (pgvector, CLAUDE_MEM_SERVER_VECTOR_SEARCH), by meaning\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__save_memory\",\"description\":\"Save an explicit durable note, decision, correction or handoff into worker-mode claude-mem. Use this for your own note taking after searching memory for duplica\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__search\",\"description\":\"Smart search (default), step 1: search memory for an index with IDs. Review it, use timeline for context, then get_observations only for selected IDs. Params: q\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__timeline\",\"description\":\"Step 2: Get context around results. Params: anchor (observation ID) OR query (finds anchor automatically), depth_before, depth_after, project. This tool is part\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read\",\"description\":\"Read this project's to-do lists and working state written with work_state_write: every open item, or one list, with done and dropped items when includeClosed is\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__work_state_write\",\"description\":\"Your canonical to-do list and working state for this project, kept across sessions: whatever is still open is shown at the start of every session. Each call app\"}]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17ec5-069e-7660-98c6-af7c51147c1b","create_time":1793130217.9555619}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
