{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T20:00:50.368Z","ordinal":426076,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ca2e60ba-cf48-4b20-8f58-5329817a45a4","process_id":"62509","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show FETCH_HEAD:docs/reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md | sed -n '1,160p'; printf '\\nCLAIM DIRS\\n'; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 1 -type d -printf '%f\\n' | rg -i '114|repro|evidence' | tail -40"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show FETCH_HEAD:docs/reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md | sed -n '1,160p'; printf '\\nCLAIM DIRS\\n'; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 1 -type d -printf '%f\\n' | rg -i '114|repro|evidence' | tail -40"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08: cross-runner reproducibility on `v1.0.0-rc.10`\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Requirement | `REQ-REL-114` (ACC-SUP-08) |\n| Result | **PASS** |\n| Tag | `v1.0.0-rc.10` |\n| Tag commit | `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` |\n| Tree | `4e76eadcb44f419001f67960241517000a8b682a` |\n| Workflow run | [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) (`refs/heads/main`, `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`, attempt 1) |\n| Jobs | `resolve-tag`, `build (ubuntu-22.04)`, `build (ubuntu-24.04)`, `compare` — all `success` |\n| Evidence artifact | `nexus-repro-evidence-v1.0.0-rc.10`, artifact id `12762288932`, zip SHA-256 `bb4bb289a75ef553805d825d681881f699f2a81302c024065700ee92d6e41e76` |\n\n## What was proven\n\nThe published RC10 tag resolved to the immutable commit above, passed version/tag/lockfile checks, and was rebuilt independently on two runners:\n\n- Ubuntu 22.04, image `20261023.322.3`\n- Ubuntu 24.04, image `20261023.334.3`\n- Both with Node `v22.22.1`, npm `10.9.4`, rustc/cargo `1.95.0` and the pinned `rust:1.95.0-bookworm` container.\n\nThe `compare` job succeeded, confirming the two rebuilds are byte-identical:\n\n| Artifact | SHA-256 |\n|---|---|\n| `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.10.tar.gz` | `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7` |\n| `SHA256SUMS` | `760199fcb7e079b356ddbae4f739c74bc356a7b0a7a2edd956b554736651d8fe` |\n| `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` | `512d808a937aedb6ba84d99b0988502af04c1ea3964f9c0c45114d4ce00053b9` |\n| `sbom.cdx.json` | `1a082a2ed29950a9cff828fd00db33de8e182dcb2758846a4e1276849a4a2c3a` |\n| `compatibility.json` | `500f4f05d089a3bad911becfd17e26c702747f5a0c9a26b6aac84497e88c1f94` |\n| `install.sh` | `5620d56ef6f8d637fc102ae2c8ea3b055effbc4069243a2df68b67520b1e2302` |\n\nThe full machine-readable record is [repro-evidence.json](repro-evidence.json): source lockfile hashes, empty untracked list, packaging-script hash, both builder manifests and every artifact digest.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\ngh workflow run repro.yml --ref main -f tag=v1.0.0-rc.10\ngh run download 40564959805 -n nexus-repro-evidence-v1.0.0-rc.10\n```\n\nThe workflow checks out the tag, but the packaging tool is the reviewed `main` workflow commit recorded above. This evidence closes the exact-tag execution gap for REQ-REL-114; promoting the ledger row remains the ledger owner's action.\n\nCLAIM DIRS\nFILE_scripts_repro-identity.mjs\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.3_terminal_installed-identity-20261024T0133Z\nREDACTED.md\nREDACTED.md\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_e5-openrouter-live-task-20261023.json\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl\nREDACTED\nREDACTED.md\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.7\nFILE_cli_test_repro_identity.test.ts\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc10_terminal_scripted\nNEXUS_PACKAGE_TAR_REPRO_20261024\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_plan-10-host-preflight-current\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.7_terminal-matrix\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":29389}},"started_at_ms":1793131250367,"completed_at_ms":1793131250368}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T20:00:51.448Z","ordinal":426077,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17ef3-86f8-7260-b20e-b4126d009b40","call_id":"call_5eefb30f929b4b35959dcfa53cf04ee7","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"e86811\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000029389,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":859,\"output\":\"# REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08: cross-runner reproducibility on `v1.0.0-rc.10`\\n\\n| | |\\n|---|---|\\n| Requirement | `REQ-REL-114` (ACC-SUP-08) |\\n| Result | **PASS** |\\n| Tag | `v1.0.0-rc.10` |\\n| Tag commit | `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` |\\n| Tree | `4e76eadcb44f419001f67960241517000a8b682a` |\\n| Workflow run | [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) (`refs/heads/main`, `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`, attempt 1) |\\n| Jobs | `resolve-tag`, `build (ubuntu-22.04)`, `build (ubuntu-24.04)`, `compare` — all `success` |\\n| Evidence artifact | `nexus-repro-evidence-v1.0.0-rc.10`, artifact id `12762288932`, zip SHA-256 `bb4bb289a75ef553805d825d681881f699f2a81302c024065700ee92d6e41e76` |\\n\\n## What was proven\\n\\nThe published RC10 tag resolved to the immutable commit above, passed version/tag/lockfile checks, and was rebuilt independently on two runners:\\n\\n- Ubuntu 22.04, image `20261023.322.3`\\n- Ubuntu 24.04, image `20261023.334.3`\\n- Both with Node `v22.22.1`, npm `10.9.4`, rustc/cargo `1.95.0` and the pinned `rust:1.95.0-bookworm` container.\\n\\nThe `compare` job succeeded, confirming the two rebuilds are byte-identical:\\n\\n| Artifact | SHA-256 |\\n|---|---|\\n| `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.10.tar.gz` | `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7` |\\n| `SHA256SUMS` | `760199fcb7e079b356ddbae4f739c74bc356a7b0a7a2edd956b554736651d8fe` |\\n| `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` | `512d808a937aedb6ba84d99b0988502af04c1ea3964f9c0c45114d4ce00053b9` |\\n| `sbom.cdx.json` | `1a082a2ed29950a9cff828fd00db33de8e182dcb2758846a4e1276849a4a2c3a` |\\n| `compatibility.json` | `500f4f05d089a3bad911becfd17e26c702747f5a0c9a26b6aac84497e88c1f94` |\\n| `install.sh` | `5620d56ef6f8d637fc102ae2c8ea3b055effbc4069243a2df68b67520b1e2302` |\\n\\nThe full machine-readable record is [repro-evidence.json](repro-evidence.json): source lockfile hashes, empty untracked list, packaging-script hash, both builder manifests and every artifact digest.\\n\\n## Reproduce\\n\\n```sh\\ngh workflow run repro.yml --ref main -f tag=v1.0.0-rc.10\\ngh run download 40564959805 -n nexus-repro-evidence-v1.0.0-rc.10\\n```\\n\\nThe workflow checks out the tag, but the packaging tool is the reviewed `main` workflow commit recorded above. This evidence closes the exact-tag execution gap for REQ-REL-114; promoting the ledger row remains the ledger owner's action.\\n\\nCLAIM DIRS\\nFILE_scripts_repro-identity.mjs\\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.3_terminal_installed-identity-20261024T0133Z\\nREDACTED.md\\nREDACTED.md\\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_e5-openrouter-live-task-20261023.json\\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl\\nREDACTED\\nREDACTED.md\\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.7\\nFILE_cli_test_repro_identity.test.ts\\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc10_terminal_scripted\\nNEXUS_PACKAGE_TAR_REPRO_20261024\\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json\\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_plan-10-host-preflight-current\\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.7_terminal-matrix\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26","create_time":1793131251.448369}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
