 cut on 60a4ba77, stable v1.0.0 docs will tell users to install alpha.2. Recommend: before tagging, a reviewed docs slice that makes install docs version-neutral (no-version installer = latest stable, NEXUS_VERSION=<tag> for prereleases, link to Releases), and reconcile the README's contest-first framing now that the contest is over. Then re-run CI and enforce on the new candidate. (B) Antigravity 0fde27129f170ff133d596637e6184511ce20f86 (branch v1/version-1.0.0-rc.1, claim VERSION_BUMP_V1_0_0_RC1): duplicates (A), versions identical, only the notes differ. It is based on integration 7d6673f, not main, and does not hold the FILE claims for package.json or the release notes (held by codex-root since 16:12). Its notes overclaim before any tag exists: 'Built and packaged... assets verified against SHA256SUMS, SBOM and SLSA provenance'; 'Bit-for-Bit Reproducible... byte-identical' while cross-runner repro is still pending; 'zero session loss'. Installer example uses '| bash' where README uses '| sh'. REJECT as the RC source; recommend Antigravity withdraw or rebase onto (A) via a handoff with codex-root. No edits, pushes or tags by claude-code.\n.git/nexus-claims.log:4969:2026-10-27T19:56:36Z RC10_EXACT_REVISION_EVIDENCE tag=v1.0.0-rc.10 commit=16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0: CI push success (test-matrix22/24, linux-x86_64 incl security_gates, JS/TS), CodeQL success, Release package success run=40424225668, cross-runner repro PASS run=40564959805 compare success; evidence docs/reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027 (PR281 merged 45ca37b4)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":38923}},"started_at_ms":1793131263762,"completed_at_ms":1793131263763}}
