-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a17ded-e7ae-7300-8479-0fca92a43367","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_user_login"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26","turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae1016b39e881a0b58f0a68ba97ed0c","order":20597,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17eed-8d29-7e92-8cd2-5ea54a35ce13","text":"PR #280 is still executing its full Node 22/24 suites; both jobs remain active rather than failed. The post-merge source CI on `fc582c6` is fully green. The other two open convergence PRs (#268 and #281) each still need their Linux package lane, so none is merge-ready yet.","turn_id":"01a17ec5-069e-7660-98c6-af7c51147c1b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae101a1d85081a0a44f88e82aba20dd","order":20599,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17eee-62c3-72b2-8fc2-c5d8d3af75bd","text":"PR #281’s exact-head Node 22/24 and Linux packaging/repro checks have now all passed, and its independent evidence review is ACCEPT. It records RC10’s exact-tag cross-runner reproducibility result without claiming the remaining acceptance gates. I’m integrating this completed evidence PR through GitHub; the requirements ledger promotion remains a separate owner action.","turn_id":"01a17ec5-069e-7660-98c6-af7c51147c1b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae101beead081a08a0ace3ce1f36168","order":20600,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17eee-d522-7b13-b016-f1f666c21931","text":"PR #281 is merged at **`45ca37b467b5e6a7b42be733be61e6964c73b4fd`** after all five required checks passed and its evidence review accepted. GitHub has started fresh post-merge CI and CodeQL on that exact commit. PR #280 is unchanged while its Node suites continue; I’ll integrate it only after those checks finish and GitHub confirms the updated base is mergeable.","turn_id":"01a17ec5-069e-7660-98c6-af7c51147c1b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae102167d7c81a0ae6af05168aa8747","order":20602,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17ef0-2a18-7e33-ab09-18a25fe09c2f","text":"PR #280’s Node 22 and Node 24 matrices have both passed. Its Linux package lane has started; once that finishes, I’ll recheck the base and mergeability before deciding whether it can be integrated directly or needs a refreshed run.","turn_id":"01a17ec5-069e-7660-98c6-af7c51147c1b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae10289f07481a0a2f893dc86b4f6eb","order":20605,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a17ef1-f357-7632-acd4-22457ccae881","text":"Understood. I recorded the terminal cell as **not run**; the matrix remains **0/15**. The worksheet is ready for when you can continue.\n\nMeanwhile, PR #281 merged at `45ca37b467b5e6a7b42be733be61e6964c73b4fd` after its exact checks and independent review passed. On that revision, requirements enforcement and RC10 version sync also pass. Post-merge CI is still running.\n\nPR #280’s independent review is ACCEPT, its focused regression suite passed **93/93**, and Node 22/24 passed. Its Linux package check is still running, so it is not ready to merge. Held-out custody is still unresolved; acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**.","turn_id":"01a17ec5-069e-7660-98c6-af7c51147c1b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae102cba3b081a0b34ded7289dbdea6","order":20606,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17ef2-ed79-7f73-baa5-4108121d31e8","text":"The previous turn advanced the release path: PR #281 merged, current-main requirements/version checks passed, and PR #280’s Node matrices passed. I’m refreshing the live Linux check, post-merge CI, PR #268, and claims before choosing the next integration step.","turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae102dbdaf881a08a04ceaccfbc92d6","order":20607,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17ef3-2d43-7892-aca6-a8eb4a74b749","text":"I found a review conflict in the just-merged PR #281: a later independent review flagged that its wording could imply more artifacts were byte-identical than the six actually compared. I’m correcting the evidence wording in a follow-up PR and will record PR #281’s evidence as needing this clarification until that correction is independently reviewed and checked.","turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae1032b318c81a0bcd92d95eeac6a2c","order":20609,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17ef4-632c-7053-b827-36ec5a8ebf14","text":"The follow-up correction is now PR #282 (`e4db23eb`), limited to that one sentence. It states the comparison covers the six listed release files and explicitly excludes the uploaded runner identity manifests. I checked the workflow’s `cmp` loop; exact PR checks and independent review are now pending.","turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":20612,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant me