{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T20:51:40.524Z","ordinal":427197,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-689b64f7-ebdd-4b64-ad74-ae161b6eb7b0","process_id":"29313","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/283/comments --jq '.[]|{user:.user.login,created_at,body}' | tail -c 2200"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/283/comments --jq '.[]|{user:.user.login,created_at,body}' | tail -c 2200"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"ve and lifecycle container runs pass `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` (since the isolated containers do not carry a trusted `gh` CLI and host-side attestation is verified separately).\\n   - `README.md:52`: `prepared-images.json` records `cell`, `image`, and `id` (digest), not the base distro and `node --version` strings directly; adjust the wording in `README.md` (or include those fields in `prepared-images.json`).\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-27T20:33:48Z\",\"user\":\"mikeholownych\"}\n{\"body\":\"claude-code re-review: still **CHANGES REQUIRED** at exact head `71a4218a232246d389f5439ec9e47a97c0c6fe14`.\\n\\nThis head adds a lifecycle cell, but none of my three findings from `7b3f464` is resolved:\\n\\n1. **Logs are still missing.** `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` on a `git archive` of this head reports `WARNING: 21 listed files could not be read`: the 20 matrix logs plus the new `ubuntu-22-04-node22-lifecycle.log`. The README now links to that lifecycle log as the evidence for \\\"Result: **PASS**\\\", but it isn't in the commit, so the link is dead.\\n2. **`README.md:52` still says** `prepared-images.json` records \\\"base distro and Node versions\\\". The file still holds only `cell`, `image` and `id`.\\n3. **Attestation is still unstated.** `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` is set in the matrix positive cells and in every lifecycle `install()` call (`run-rc10-lifecycle.sh:19`), and the README still doesn't say so.\\n\\n**New finding on the lifecycle cell:** it overstates what was tested. Every \\\"upgrade\\\", \\\"rollback\\\" and \\\"repair\\\" step is `sh /tmp/nexus-install.sh` re-run with a different `NEXUS_VERSION` (`run-rc10-lifecycle.sh:19,29,37,50`). The product's own `nexus upgrade` path is never exercised: its staging, upgrade journal, restart notice and the recovery from #280. The README should say these are installer-driven version switches, or the cell should also run `nexus upgrade` for the alpha.2 → RC step.\\n\\nWhat passes at this head: the script and README digests, the doctor JSONs, and the checks the lifecycle script actually runs for state, config and adjacent-file preservation and for byte-identical restore of the provenance file.\\n\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-27T20:50:49Z\",\"user\":\"mikeholownych\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":386704079}},"started_at_ms":1793134300134,"completed_at_ms":1793134300522}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T20:51:41.974Z","ordinal":427198,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17f22-1316-7891-bb80-cc9bd856f11d","call_id":"call_e30b3c2053984a9b830da29d805d7b72","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ve and lifecycle container runs pass `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` (since the isolated containers do not carry a trusted `gh` CLI and host-side attestation is verified separately).\\n   - `README.md:52`: `prepared-images.json` records `cell`, `image`, and `id` (digest), not the base distro and `node --version` strings directly; adjust the wording in `README.md` (or include those fields in `prepared-images.json`).\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-27T20:33:48Z\",\"user\":\"mikeholownych\"}\n{\"body\":\"claude-code re-review: still **CHANGES REQUIRED** at exact head `71a4218a232246d389f5439ec9e47a97c0c6fe14`.\\n\\nThis head adds a lifecycle cell, but none of my three findings from `7b3f464` is resolved:\\n\\n1. **Logs are still missing.** `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` on a `git archive` of this head reports `WARNING: 21 listed files could not be read`: the 20 matrix logs plus the new `ubuntu-22-04-node22-lifecycle.log`. The README now links to that lifecycle log as the evidence for \\\"Result: **PASS**\\\", but it isn't in the commit, so the link is dead.\\n2. **`README.md:52` still says** `prepared-images.json` records \\\"base distro and Node versions\\\". The file still holds only `cell`, `image` and `id`.\\n3. **Attestation is still unstated.** `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` is set in the matrix positive cells and in every lifecycle `install()` call (`run-rc10-lifecycle.sh:19`), and the README still doesn't say so.\\n\\n**New finding on the lifecycle cell:** it overstates what was tested. Every \\\"upgrade\\\", \\\"rollback\\\" and \\\"repair\\\" step is `sh /tmp/nexus-install.sh` re-run with a different `NEXUS_VERSION` (`run-rc10-lifecycle.sh:19,29,37,50`). The product's own `nexus upgrade` path is never exercised: its staging, upgrade journal, restart notice and the recovery from #280. The README should say these are installer-driven version switches, or the cell should also run `nexus upgrade` for the alpha.2 → RC step.\\n\\nWhat passes at this head: the script and README digests, the doctor JSONs, and the checks the lifecycle script actually runs for state, config and adjacent-file preservation and for byte-identical restore of the provenance file.\\n\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-27T20:50:49Z\",\"user\":\"mikeholownych\"}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26","create_time":1793134301.9741597}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
