\nFILE_cli_test_discovered_verifier_premutation.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_doctor.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_flight_exclude.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_helpers_startup_permission_driver.py\nFILE_cli_test_html_text.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_inference_transport.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_mcp.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_process_lifecycle.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_provider_connect.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_readonly_command_paths.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_readonly_home.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_repl_approval_e2e.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_repl_checkpoint_choice.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_repro_identity.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_search_web.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_session_export_escaping.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_tui_surface_e2e.test.ts\nFILE_cli_test_verifier_gating.test.ts\nFILE_demo_test_substrate-adapter.test.mjs\nFILE_docs_CLIENT_GUIDE.md\nFILE_docs_REPOSITORY_QUALITY.md\nFILE_docs_releases_v1_0_0-rc_6_md\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.3_terminal_installed-identity-20261024T0133Z\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.7\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.7_terminal-matrix\nREDACTED.md\nREDACTED.md\nREDACTED.md\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_plan-10-host-preflight-current\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_e5-openrouter-live-task-20261023.json\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc10_terminal_scripted\nREDACTED\nFILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md\nFILE_docs_v1.0.0_REQUIREMENTS.md\nFILE_docs_v1.0.0_ROADMAP.md\nFILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\nFILE_docs_v1.0.0_plans_PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md\nFILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md\nFILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_agent-collab-worker_package.json\nFILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_fork-worker_package.json\nFILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_package-lock.json\nFILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_package.json\nFILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_trusted-broker-bundle_package-lock.json\nFILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_trusted-broker-bundle_package.json\nFILE_scripts_generate_sbom.sh\nFILE_scripts_package-linux.sh\nFILE_scripts_release-tools_package-lock.json\nFILE_scripts_release-tools_package.json\nFILE_scripts_repro-identity.mjs\nNEXUS_PACKAGE_TAR_REPRO_20261024\nPLAN-01_SEC101_119_PTY_REBASE_VALIDATION_20261025\nPLAN-05_PR-5B_CODEQL_CLIENT_NORMALIZE\nPLAN-08_TASK1_HOME_ISOLATION_TEST\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\n\nThis package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n\n**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** There are 31 blocker requirements, none of them met. Task-quality, standalone and real-terminal qualification are **unverified**: no qualifying evidence exists yet. The contest entry was submitted, is frozen, and is tracked separately.\n\n## How to read it\n\n| If you want to… | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\n\n## Workstreams\n\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; frozen until judging ends) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\n\n## How to execute\n\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06 PR-6a (version sync) and PLAN-09 PR-9a (ledger checker, historical banners, cheap doc fixes).\n2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\n3. **For every PR:**\n   - update the matching REQUIREMENTS rows (status, test reference, commit);\n   - keep `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` green;\n   - run `make test` on a snapshot copy, never while editing (tasks/lessons.md).\n4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\n5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Requirement IDs.** `REQ-<AREA>-0xx` marks a commitment carried over from history. `REQ-<AREA>-1xx` marks a new v1 requirement.\n- **Finding IDs.** These are owned by the scoped evidence files: AGT, VER, PRV, SEC, PER, TUI, REL, DX, MNT, HIST, EVL, CON, PERF, DOC.\n- **Acceptance IDs.** `ACC-<AREA>-NN`. Each is defined in its spec, or in ACCEPTANCE §3.1.\n- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\n- **Status ladder.** open → partial → implemented → tested → visually-accepted → product-qualified. Independent acceptance is recorded separately.\n\nThis package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\neval/README.md:3:`run.mjs` runs tasks against one agent configuration and appends a JSON line per run; `score.mjs` reports the scores\neval/README.md:4:separately (never combined), per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals.\neval/README.md:7:node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/gateway-engineering-deep.json --out eval/out/<label> [--only id,id] [--runs N]\neval/README.md:8:node eval/score.mjs eval/out/<label>/results.jsonl          # markdown table; --json for machine output\neval/README.md:11:Each run: a fresh workspace (the task's `fixture`, or its `repo.url` at `repo.commit`, cached in `eval/.cache`), a fresh\neval/README.md:14:the configuration (secrets in `env` masked), host and Node version; per-run logs go to `logs/<task>-<run>/`.\neval/README.md:16:## Task format (`eval/tasks/<id>/task.json`)\neval/README.md:24:| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\neval/README.md:37:- T2 hidden-test pass rate (pooled over all T2 runs of a configuration, point estimate, 95 % intervals reported) ≥ the\neval/README.md:40:  configuration the 95 % interval half-width near 50 % is ~13 points, so a tighter margin is not distinguishable from\neval/README.md:45:- ≥ 5 runs per task-configuration, per-task results with 95 % intervals.\neval/README.md:62:Configurations `configs/pilot-*.json`: Nexus, Aider 0.86.2, OpenCode 1.18.35, Goose 1.27.2, all on\neval/README.md:70:one `--message` exchange with `--yes-always` (its non-interactive mode); no cloud configuration (operator decision);\neval/infra.mjs:5:// usage: eval/infra.mjs <out-dir-of-one-config>   → prints \"task run\" per infrastructure failure\neval/score.mjs:2:// Scores eval results (results.jsonl from eval/run.mjs). Scores are reported separately and never combined\neval/score.mjs:4:// bounded failure, wall time, steps, tokens — per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals for rates.\neval/score.mjs:7:// Several files may be given: a later record for the same configuration, task and run replaces an earlier one (a rerun\neval/score.mjs:8:// of a run that failed on infrastructure, see eval/infra.mjs). The replaced records stay in their files.\neval/score.mjs:11:  console.error(\"usage: eval/score.mjs <results.jsonl>... [--json]\");\neval/score.mjs:18:    const key = `${r.config}\\t${r.task}\\t${r.run}`;\neval/score.mjs:43:  const key = `${r.config}\\t${r.task}`;\neval/score.mjs:49:  const [config, task] = key.split(\"\\t\");\neval/score.mjs:54:    config,\neval/score.mjs:80:const pooled = [...new Set(records.map((r) => r.config))].map((config) => {\neval/score.mjs:81:  const rs = records.filter((r) => r.config === config);\neval/score.mjs:83:  return { config, n: rs.length, correct: k, rate: k / rs.length, ci: wilson(k, rs.length), falseVerified: rs.filter((r) => r.falseVerified).length };\neval/score.mjs:91:  console.log(\"| config | runs | correct | pass rate (95% CI) | false VERIFIED |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\");\neval/score.mjs:92:  for (const p of pooled) console.log(`| ${p.config} | ${p.n} | ${p.correct} | ${pct(p.rate)} (${pct(p.ci[0])}–${pct(p.ci[1])}) | ${p.falseVerified} |`);\neval/score.mjs:94:  console.log(\"| config | task | tier | n | claimed | correct (95% CI) | false VERIFIED | regressions | timed out | contaminated | median wall s | median steps | median tokens |\");\neval/score.mjs:97:    console.log(`| ${r.config} | ${r.task} | ${r.tier} | ${r.n} | ${r.claimed} | ${r.correct} (${pct(r.correctCI[0])}–${pct(r.correctCI[1])}) | ${r.falseVerified} | ${r.regressions} | ${r.timedOut} | ${r.contaminated} | ${r.medianWallS?.toFixed(0) ?? \"–\"} | ${r.medianSteps ?? \"–\"} | ${r.medianTokens ?? \"–\"} |`);\ncore/Cargo.lock:594: \"pkg-config\",\ncore/Cargo.lock:611: \"pkg-config\",\ncore/Cargo.lock:792:name = \"pkg-config\"\neval/run.mjs:2:// Runs evaluation tasks against an agent configuration and appends one JSON line per run (see eval/README.md).\neval/run.mjs:5:// regression command are run in that workspace. Nothing is scored here: eval/score.mjs reads the JSON lines.\neval/run.mjs:16:if (!args.config || !args.out) {\neval/run.mjs:17:  console.error(\"usage: eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/<name>.json --out <dir> [--tasks eval/tasks] [--only id,id] [--runs N]\");\neval/run.mjs:20:const config = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(args.config, \"utf8\"));\neval/run.mjs:21:const tasksDir = path.resolve(args.tasks ?? path.join(ROOT, \"eval/tasks\"));\neval/run.mjs:22:const runs = Number(args.runs ?? config.runs ?? 1);\neval/run.mjs:24:// --pairs \"task run,task run\": rerun exactly these (runs that failed on infrastructure; see eval/infra.mjs).\neval/run.mjs:31:fs.writeFileSync(path.join(args.out, \"manifest.json\"), JSON.stringify({ createdAt: new Date().toISOString(), harness: identity, config: redactConfig(config), runs, tasks, host: os.hostname(), node: process.version }, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\neval/run.mjs:34:const apiKey = readApiKey(config.apiKey);\neval/run.mjs:35:const caFile = config.caFile ? expandHome(config.caFile) : null;\neval/run.mjs:43:    console.log(`${new Date().toISOString()} ${config.name} ${id} run ${run}: ${record.turn?.outcome ?? record.error ?? `exit ${record.exitCode}`} hidden=${record.hiddenPass} regression=${record.regressionPass} ${Math.round(record.wallMs / 1000)}s`);\neval/run.mjs:50:  const base = { task: task.id, tier: task.tier, config: config.name, agent: config.agent ?? \"nexus\", run, harness: identity.string, model: config.model, startedAt: new Date().toISOString() };\neval/run.mjs:97:    const cache = path.join(ROOT, \"eval/.cache\", createHash(\"sha256\").update(task.repo.url).digest(\"hex\").slice(0, 16));\neval/run.mjs:110:  const ep = config.endpoint;\neval/run.mjs:114:  const env = { ...process.env, ...(config.env ?? {}), ...keyEnv, ...caEnv, HOME: home, PWD: ws, XDG_CONFIG_HOME: path.join(home, \".config\"), XDG_DATA_HOME: path.join(home, \".local/share\"), XDG_STATE_HOME: path.join(home, \".local/state\") };\neval/run.mjs:115:  const agent = config.agent ?? \"nexus\";\neval/run.mjs:118:    return { cmd: process.execPath, argv: [path.join(ROOT, \"cli/dist/index.js\"), \"run\", \"--json\", \"-w\", ws, \"-e\", ep, \"-m\", config.model, \"-s\", \"30\", \"--max-total-steps\", String(budget.steps), \"--max-turn-minutes\", String(budget.minutes), ...(config.args ?? []), task.objective], env };\neval/run.mjs:121:    return { cmd: \"aider\", argv: [\"--model\", `openai/${config.model}`, \"--openai-api-base\", ep, \"--yes-always\", \"--no-auto-commits\", \"--no-dirty-commits\", \"--no-gitignore\", \"--no-show-model-warnings\", \"--no-check-update\", \"--analytics-disable\", \"--no-pretty\", \"--no-fancy-input\", ...(config.args ?? []), \"--message\", task.objective], env };\neval/run.mjs:124:    const dir = path.join(home, \".config/opencode\");\neval/run.mjs:126:    const limits = config.limits ?? { context: 65536, output: 8192 };\neval/run.mjs:128:      $schema: \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\neval/run.mjs:132:      provider: { gw: { npm: \"@ai-sdk/openai-compatible\", name: \"gateway\", options: { baseURL: ep, apiKey: \"{env:GW_KEY}\" }, models: { [config.model]: { name: config.model, limit: limits } } } },\neval/run.mjs:133:      model: `gw/${config.model}`,\neval/run.mjs:136:    env.XDG_CACHE_HOME = path.join(ROOT, \"eval/.cache/xdg-cache\");\neval/run.mjs:137:    return { cmd: \"opencode\", argv: [\"run\", \"--model\", `gw/${config.model}`, ...(config.args ?? []), task.objective], env };\neval/run.mjs:141:    Object.assign(env, { GOOSE_PROVIDER: \"openai\", GOOSE_MODEL: config.model, OPENAI_HOST: u.origin, OPENAI_BASE_PATH: `${u.pathname.replace(/^\\/|\\/$/g, \"\")}/chat/completions`, GOOSE_MODE: \"auto\", GOOSE_DISABLE_KEYRING: \"1\", GOOSE_CONTEXT_LIMIT: String(config.limits?.context ?? 65536) });\neval/run.mjs:142:    return { cmd: \"goose\", argv: [\"run\", \"--no-session\", \"--with-builtin\", \"developer\", ...(config.args ?? []), \"-t\", task.objective], env };\neval/run.mjs:148:  const budget = { steps: task.steps ?? config.steps ?? 300, minutes: task.minutes ?? config.minutes ?? 120 };\neval/run.mjs:224:/** `{ file, var }`: the key is read from a KEY=value file (e.g. ~/.config/nexus/config.env); never logged. */\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:23:| Runtime services | The local inference gateway is configured in `~/.config/nexus/config.env`: endpoint `https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1`, model `engineering/b0`, key redacted, `LOCAL_HARNESS_SHELL=bash`. The repo-tracked `cli/.env` holds LM Studio defaults (`localhost:1234`, key \"local\"). **The audit sent no requests to the gateway.** With owner authorization (2026-10-14, small spend), it made live cloud calls through the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections: two `providers verify` runs and one `nexus run` bug-fix task. See EVIDENCE §3. | RT (values redacted) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:59:1. **Safe by default on untrusted input.** Content from a repository, a web page, a skill or a tool output cannot cause unapproved host execution, egress, or configuration changes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:105:| Workspace → configuration | Only allowlisted project settings | `.env` overrides any env, including TLS (PRV-01) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:134:| Agent loop and core (`cli/src/agent.ts`, `core/{turn,app,execution_tracking,objective,provider_recovery,operation_runner}.ts`, `team.ts`) | 9 | Full read | A_core_agent | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:137:| Providers: `client.ts`, `protocols/*`, `providers, provider_cli, provider_connect, model_catalog, credentials, oauth, config, usage, search_web, onboard, embeddings`, `core/{provider_capabilities, egress}` | 17 | Full read (embeddings, egress: targeted) + mock probes | B_providers; this file (provider_connect, read by lead) | `evaluateEgress` deep logic reviewed only for classification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:145:| Eval harness `eval/` (43) | 43 | Full read of run/score/infra/configs. 2 of 7 tasks read. | G | Hidden tests of the other 5 tasks not read (by design) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:173:| HIST-05 | S2 | B | Review mode | `capabilities.ts` (`mutating:false` network tools); `agent.ts:3946` | SRC | Egress never needs approval | REQ-SEC-102 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:201:| PRV-01 | S2 | B | Opening any repo | `config.ts:36-39` | RT (TLS repro) | A repo `.env` disables TLS; keys can be intercepted | REQ-SEC-110 (SPEC-03) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:204:| HIST-04 | S2 | B | Startup | `plugins.ts:47-54` | SRC | Imports `~/.config/opencode/plugins` | REQ-SEC-115 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:209:| PRV-06 | S2 | B | Standalone LM Studio and llama.cpp | `provider_capabilities.ts:29,72` | SRC + INF | 65536 default; overflow ends the turn | REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-102 (SPEC-05) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:252:| AGT-11 | S3 | RR | Team outcome | `operation_runner.ts:651-663` | SRC | COMPLETE without a change | REQ-AGT-107 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:253:| AGT-12 | S4 | RR | Operation bound | `operation_runner.ts:95-137` | SRC | Dead-end decision | REQ-AGT-107 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:297:| PRV-06b | S3 | B (via REQ-PRV-101) | Cloud context sizing | `provider_capabilities.ts` | RT (live): ChatGPT run reported `context_limit=65536 (client_default)` | Large-window cloud models are under-used, and small-window ones overflow | Covered by REQ-PRV-101, extended to provider catalog limits |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:308:| EVL-001 | S1 | B | v1 quality claim | `eval/` | DOC + SRC | No qualifying evidence | REQ-QUAL-101..105 (SPEC-10) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:313:| EVL-006 | S4 | RR | Docs | `eval/README.md` | SRC | Stale status | REQ-DX-105 |\neval/configs/pilot-opencode.json:6:  \"apiKey\": { \"file\": \"~/.config/nexus/config.env\", \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\" },\neval/configs/pilot-opencode.json:7:  \"caFile\": \"~/.config/nexus/t5820-gateway-ca.crt\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:82:- 5 runs per task and configuration.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:106:**Rationale.** These figures are the pilot's pre-registered thresholds (eval/README), tightened where the pilot showed weakness: false VERIFIED, crash accounting. The absolute floor prevents \"beat a weak peer\" from passing. Thresholds are fixed **before** the RC run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:120:- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:189:- Nexus runs in a clean HOME with no homelab configuration: no `config.env` gateway entries, no gateway token file, no `X-Task-Class`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:190:- It talks to `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` on `127.0.0.1`. The proxy forwards to the gateway with the gateway token injected on the proxy side. It strips every gateway extension: `/v1/models` is reduced to `{id, object, owned_by}`, `/v1/tokenize` returns 404, and `X-AIHost-*` response headers and admission headers are removed.\ncli/test/spine.test.ts:317:    const config: HarnessConfig = {\ncli/test/spine.test.ts:326:    const agent = new AutonomousAgent(config);\neval/configs/pilot-aider.json:6:  \"apiKey\": { \"file\": \"~/.config/nexus/config.env\", \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\" },\neval/configs/pilot-aider.json:7:  \"caFile\": \"~/.config/nexus/t5820-gateway-ca.crt\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:10:- `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:26:| 1 | `ServerKind` probe (gateway / vllm / llamacpp / lmstudio / ollama / unknown). Context discovery through `/pr