nfigs/pilot-goose.json:7:  \"caFile\": \"~/.config/nexus/t5820-gateway-ca.crt\",\ncli/test/verifier_timeout.test.ts:8: *  - the completion verifier has an explicit, configurable deadline and reports VERIFIER_TIMED_OUT\ncli/test/verifier_timeout.test.ts:82:    execSync(\"git init -q && git config user.name t && git config user.email t@t.invalid && git add . && git commit -qm base\", { cwd: ws, stdio: \"ignore\" });\ncore/src/file_ops.rs:1294:            path: \"config.json\".into(),\neval/configs/pilot-nexus.json:6:  \"apiKey\": { \"file\": \"~/.config/nexus/config.env\", \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\" },\neval/configs/pilot-nexus.json:7:  \"caFile\": \"~/.config/nexus/t5820-gateway-ca.crt\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:26:| 6 | `read_file` cap at 8 MB, with an `offset`/`length` paging hint in the error. Same for `batch_read`. | `file_ops.rs:205-277`; capability schema in `capabilities.ts` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:30:| 10 | `run_command {background:true, service_name}` registers a service. Services are listed in `/status`, killed on exit, and do not survive the turn's cancel unless registered. | `capabilities.ts`, `runner.rs`, `slash/session_commands.ts` | 1 |\ncli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts:235:    execFileSync(\"git\", [\"config\", \"user.name\", \"Synthetic Fixture\"], { cwd: workspace });\ncli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts:236:    execFileSync(\"git\", [\"config\", \"user.email\", \"fixture@example.invalid\"], { cwd: workspace });\ncli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts:263:    execFileSync(\"git\", [\"config\", \"user.name\", \"Synthetic Fixture\"], { cwd: workspace });\ncli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts:264:    execFileSync(\"git\", [\"config\", \"user.email\", \"fixture@example.invalid\"], { cwd: workspace });\ncli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts:289:    execFileSync(\"git\", [\"config\", \"user.name\", \"Synthetic Fixture\"], { cwd: workspace });\ncli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts:290:    execFileSync(\"git\", [\"config\", \"user.email\", \"fixture@example.invalid\"], { cwd: workspace });\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:22:Only `context_length` and `max_model_len` are parsed (`core/provider_capabilities.ts:29,72`). LM Studio's and llama.cpp's `/v1/models` do not carry these fields (INFERENCE on server behaviour; verify in G1). On those servers sizing falls back to 65536. If the loaded window is smaller, the first large turn ends with a capacity error and no compaction-and-retry (`agent.ts:4684-4689`; PRV-06). On top of that, llama.cpp's overflow body is classified as REQUEST_REJECTED, not CAPACITY_REJECTED (PRV-07, reproduced).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:47:- `~/.config/opencode/t5820-client-token` (`client.ts:63-69`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:69:   - **(a) Live:** Nexus runs in a clean HOME with no homelab configuration, through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`. The proxy strips every gateway extension and, in a second profile, emulates the llama.cpp, vLLM and Ollama `/models` and overflow shapes. In both profiles, Nexus passes the standalone T2 subset and the T4 subset at the ACCEPTANCE §4.2 threshold, and turns are recorded with receipts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:74:   - the gateway token path becomes configurable (`NEXUS_GATEWAY_TOKEN_FILE`), with the homelab path read only if explicitly configured;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:75:   - `X-Task-Class` is sent only to origins that advertise support (gateway capability) or when configured;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:77:9. **REQ-PRV-110.** A custom CA is documented through `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS` in `config.env`. The launcher exports it before node starts, and `nexus doctor` validates it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:78:10. **REQ-TUI-105.** At session start (TUI and REPL) the endpoint is probed with a 3 s `GET /models`. An unreachable or misconfigured endpoint is reported with the URL, the cause, and the fix (`nexus doctor`, `~/.config/nexus/config.env`, `/connect`). A never-reachable endpoint ends the turn with guidance after a bounded wait (default 2 minutes for \"never succeeded this session\", versus the existing 20-minute recovery deadline for \"was working\").\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:82:- **Disc\n... command output truncated for persistence ...\nsource !== \"configured\" && evidence.independent !== true) {\ncli/src/agent.ts:5163:    if (this.configuredVerifierGatesCompletion() && this.turnConfiguredVerifier !== \"PASSED\") {\ncli/src/agent.ts:5205:    console.log(`📁 Workspace: ${this.config.workspace}`);\ncli/src/agent.ts:5206:    console.log(`🐚 Shell: ${this.config.shell}`);\ncli/src/agent.ts:5207:    console.log(`🤖 Model: ${this.config.model} (${this.config.endpoint})\\n`);\ncli/src/agent.ts:5211:    if (this.config.worktree) {\ncli/src/agent.ts:5216:        throw new Error(`Cannot start worktree-isolated task: ${this.config.workspace} is not a valid git repository.`);\ncli/src/agent.ts:5218:      const configuredSandbox = this.config.sandbox === \"bwrap\" || this.config.sandbox === \"docker\"\ncli/src/agent.ts:5219:        ? this.config.sandbox\ncli/src/agent.ts:5221:      if (!isSandboxAvailable(configuredSandbox)) {\ncli/src/agent.ts:5222:        throw new Error(`Cannot start worktree-isolated task: no usable shell sandbox is available (${configuredSandbox}).`);\ncli/src/agent.ts:5226:      this.originalWorkspace = this.config.workspace;\ncli/src/agent.ts:5233:        model: this.config.model,\ncli/src/agent.ts:5234:        endpoint: this.config.endpoint,\ncli/src/agent.ts:5243:      if (this.config.tdd) {\ncli/src/agent.ts:5244:        this.config.tdd = false;\ncli/src/agent.ts:5258:          this.config.tdd = true;\ncli/src/agent.ts:5265:      if (this.activeWorktree && this.config.wo