{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T21:04:17.037Z","ordinal":427431,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-31eefca4-0c8c-4aa5-8e22-e98e8a7a7788","process_id":"91505","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:AGENTS.md | sed -n '1,100p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | rg -n -i 'operation|capabilit|scheduler|config|eval|property|decisionrejected'; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print0 | xargs -0 -r rg -l 'capabilities|operation\\.ts|operation_runner|scheduler|DecisionRejected|eval|config' 2>/dev/null; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json | sort | tail -50; command -v xerj && xerj search \"ConvergenceScheduler operation lifecycle\" --prefix nexus-core"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:AGENTS.md | sed -n '1,100p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | rg -n -i 'operation|capabilit|scheduler|config|eval|property|decisionrejected'; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print0 | xargs -0 -r rg -l 'capabilities|operation\\.ts|operation_runner|scheduler|DecisionRejected|eval|config' 2>/dev/null; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json | sort | tail -50; command -v xerj && xerj search \"ConvergenceScheduler operation lifecycle\" --prefix nexus-core"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Project Guidelines & Agent Instructions\n\n## Commands\n- Build: `make build` or `cargo build` or `npm run build`\n- Test: `make test` or `cargo test` or `npm test`\n- Lint: `cargo clippy` or `npm run lint`\n\n## Code Conventions\n- Maintain documentation integrity and keep existing comments.\n- Always run tests after making changes to verify correctness.\n- Keep functions modular and clearly typed.\n\n## v1.0.0 work and concurrent agents\n- The v1.0.0 plan is in `docs/v1.0.0/` (start at `docs/v1.0.0/README.md`). Implement one claimed PR slice at a time, within the safe change boundary in its plan.\n- When more than one agent may be working, follow `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`. In short:\n  - Claim the slice atomically under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`.\n  - Use one worktree and branch per slice; never edit `~/nexus-code` directly.\n  - Isolate `HOME` for every test or probe run.\n  - Claim hot files before editing them.\n  - Take the `GATEWAY` claim for any inference run.\n  - Never use `pkill -f`.\n  - Check `git log` for foreign commits before every commit.\n  - Leave push, tag and publish to the owner.\n55:| REQ-AGT-001 | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY §A; operator directive | No default cumulative step or time ceiling. Turns end on completion, cancel, demonstrated stagnation, actionable failure or an operator-set budget. Resource-safety valves (provider iterations, 10k scheduler transitions, 5 compaction attempts) are allowed and labelled. | `types.ts:127-133`; `agent.ts:4379-4445` | TEST + SRC (A §5) | tested | N | — | ACC-CONT-04, ACC-QUAL-T3 | K | SPEC-04 |\n69:| REQ-SEC-002 | EXT-002, TOP_TIER B2 | Workspace MCP configs and plugins load only after `nexus trust`, and never in `--read-only`. | `workspace_trust.ts`; `mcp.ts:509-531`; `plugins.ts:47-76` | TEST + SRC | tested | N | Skills and knowledge are not gated (→ REQ-SEC-113) | ACC-TRUST-04 | K | SPEC-03 |\n72:| REQ-PRV-001 | CLOUD_PROVIDERS Authority | Only the operator selects a cloud destination. A project `.env` cannot. | `config.ts:53-72` | TEST (test:cli/test/egress.test.ts::\"ACC-TRUST-02: CIDR classification table, reason codes, and operator origins\") | tested | N | — | ACC-TRUST-02 | B (via REQ-SEC-111) | SPEC-03 |\n74:| REQ-PRV-003 | COMPACTION:7-9; handoff doc | Nexus works without homelab-ai. Gateway features are optional and absent-safe. | `provider_capabilities.ts:184-195` | TEST (scripted) | implemented | 