{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T21:04:18.165Z","ordinal":427432,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17f2d-9cf5-7092-8fff-e0e3cdf6ccba","call_id":"call_0dbf8ac307d943898a076718cea29cb7","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5760)\nTotal output lines: 187\n\n# Project Guidelines & Agent Instructions\n\n## Commands\n- Build: `make build` or `cargo build` or `npm run build`\n- Test: `make test` or `cargo test` or `npm test`\n- Lint: `cargo clippy` or `npm run lint`\n\n## Code Conventions\n- Maintain documentation integrity and keep existing comments.\n- Always run tests after making changes to verify correctness.\n- Keep functions modular and clearly typed.\n\n## v1.0.0 work and concurrent agents\n- The v1.0.0 plan is in `docs/v1.0.0/` (start at `docs/v1.0.0/README.md`). Implement one claimed PR slice at a time, within the safe change boundary in its plan.\n- When more than one agent may be working, follow `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`. In short:\n  - Claim the slice atomically under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`.\n  - Use one worktree and branch per slice; never edit `~/nexus-code` directly.\n  - Isolate `HOME` for every test or probe run.\n  - Claim hot files before editing them.\n  - Take the `GATEWAY` claim for any inference run.\n  - Never use `pkill -f`.\n  - Check `git log` for foreign commits before every commit.\n  - Leave push, tag and publish to the owner.\n55:| REQ-AGT-001 | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY §A; operator directive | No default cumulative step or time ceiling. Turns end on completion, cancel, demonstrated stagnation, actionable failure or an operator-set budget. Resource-safety valves (provider iterations, 10k scheduler transitions, 5 compaction attempts) are allowed and labelled. | `types.ts:127-133`; `agent.ts:4379-4445` | TEST + SRC (A §5) | tested | N | — | ACC-CONT-04, ACC-QUAL-T3 | K | SPEC-04 |\n69:| REQ-SEC-002 | EXT-002, TOP_TIER B2 | Workspace MCP configs and plugins load only after `nexus trust`, and never in `--read-only`. | `workspace_trust.ts`; `mcp.ts:509-531`; `plugins.ts:47-76` | TEST + SRC | tested | N | Skills and knowledge are not gated (→ REQ-SEC-113) | ACC-TRUST-04 | K | SPEC-03 |\n72:| REQ-PRV-001 | CLOUD_PROVIDERS Authority | Only the operator selects a cloud destination. A project `.env` cannot. | `config.ts:53-72` | TEST (test:cli/test/egress.test.ts::\"ACC-TRUST-02: CIDR classification table, reason codes, and operator origins\") | tested | N | — | ACC-TRUST-02 | B (via REQ-SEC-111) | SPEC-03 |\n74:| REQ-PRV-003 | COMPACTION:7-9; handoff doc | Nexus works without homelab-ai. Gateway features are optional and absent-safe. | `provider_capabilities.ts:184-195` | TEST (scripted) | implemented | N | No live standalone evidence (HIST-08) | ACC-INF-10 | B (via REQ-PRV-106) | SPEC-05 |\n81:| REQ-DX-001 | DOCTOR_TROUBLESHOOTING | Doctor runs with no config, model or session. Versioned JSON. Distinct exit codes. Narrow, confirmed, backed-up, idempotent repairs. Redaction. | `doctor.ts` | RT (E §4) | tested | N | DX-01..05 | ACC-PKG-06..09 | K + RR | SPEC-06 |\n92:| EXEC-011 (evaluators score the exact candidate) | DEMONSTRATED | **Contradicted** for `nexus eval` (VER-07) | `nexus eval` is experimental (DEC-07). The qualification harness is `eval/` (REQ-QUAL-106). |\n95:| DEDUP-003 (retain the 36-tool surface pending ablation) | DEMONSTRATED | 38 tools; rare groups offered on demand (0090f9c) | **Superseded**. Ablation evidence is partial (eval pilot). Tool-group behaviour is protected by `tool_groups.test.ts`. |\n104:| ACT-002 configurable delegation depth | DEMONSTRATED | Hard-coded `depth >= 2` | Accepted as a fixed bound for v1 (documented). Configurability is post-v1. |\n105:| EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE I3 (502/504 park), I4 (advisory hides decision), stale-lock race, corrupt lock | open | Not re-verified | Covered by DEC-03 (team/operation experimental). **Post-v1**, tracked as issues. |\n119:| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Without operator opt-in, model-initiated exec and egress require the configured permission decision. Folder trust does not select or change approval mode; unset mode defaults to review. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `index.ts`, `core/approval_policy.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts::\"REQ-SEC-101: the unset mode stays review in trusted and untrusted workspaces\"`; `test:cli/test/config.test.ts::\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\"`; PTY `test:cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts::\"ACC-SAFE-01: launcher permission mode is independent of folder trust\"`; evidence `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md` | tested | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n120:| REQ-SEC-102 | Audit; TOP_TIER B1 | Every capability has an effect class. Review gates every class except read. The gate is enforced at dispatch from the registry. | safety | `core/capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts:3945` | TEST `approval_policy.test.ts` | tested | ACC-SAFE-02 | **B** | HIST-05, SEC-03 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n122:| REQ-SEC-119 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Nexus-initiated verifier runs are `exec` class and follow configured permission mode; review requires a one-time approval showing the script body. Folder trust alone does not authorize execution; all runs are routed through the runner. | safety | `agent.ts:1654,3544,4255`; `tester.ts:145`; `verifier_gating.test.ts`; `workspace_commands.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"trusted and untrusted repos in review mode prompt for verifier and script body, write sentinel only after approval, and cache session decision\"`; `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"denied verifier does not execute verifier and sentinel is not written\"`; `test:cli/test/harness.test.ts::\"run_tests keeps repository 