{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T21:08:36.524Z","ordinal":427702,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-faf26199-5a6c-4667-b579-416825b8a961","process_id":"37457","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/convergence_scheduling.test.ts test/convergence_scheduler_properties.test.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/operation-scheduler-extraction/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/convergence_scheduling.test.ts test/convergence_scheduler_properties.test.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"✔ generated acyclic operations schedule only after dependencies complete and converge (43.297171ms)\n▶ resource eligibility\n  ✔ 1. a 429 marks the resource that returned it ineligible, at model scope (4.06724ms)\n  ✔ 2. Retry-After produces eligible_at = observed + delay (authoritative) (0.624031ms)\n  ✔ 3. rate-limit reset metadata is honoured; with both hints the later window wins (3.298545ms)\n  ✔ 4. no new work is assigned to a known-ineligible resource (8.931847ms)\n  ✔ 5. unrelated providers and models stay eligible (0.613944ms)\n✔ resource eligibility (20.493394ms)\n▶ capability-aware rerouting\n  ✔ 6. an equivalent qualified model is selected when the preferred one is rate-limited (3.97167ms)\n  ✔ 7. an unqualified model is never selected merely because it is available (3.910294ms)\n  ✔ 8. a reroute records why, from and to (2.729868ms)\n✔ capability-aware rerouting (11.474393ms)\n▶ parking and continuing independent work\n  ✔ 9. work parks with its wake condition when no qualified alternate exists (5.926678ms)\n  ✔ 10. independent work continues while a unit is parked (4.907963ms)\n  ✔ 11. dependent work stays non-runnable until its dependencies complete (4.412809ms)\n  ✔ 12. the operation does not WAIT while productive work exists (5.969667ms)\n  ✔ 13. the operation WAITS when no productive work remains, and 14. sleeps until the eligibility time (4.658612ms)\n  ✔ 15. a wake re-evaluates instead of executing the parked work blindly (3.692737ms)\n  ✔ 16. a recovered resource becomes eligible again (0.732896ms)\n  ✔ 17. after recovery another resource may still be the better choice (6.413614ms)\n  ✔ 18. cancellation while waiting preserves the work (1.905273ms)\n✔ parking and continuing independent work (39.681179ms)\n▶ durable waiting across process restart\n  ✔ 19. restart reconstructs the wake condition from durable state (246.312992ms)\n  ✔ 20. an overdue wake after restart re-evaluates immediately (359.733554ms)\n  ✔ 21. a future wake after restart is rescheduled for the remaining time (379.811414ms)\n✔ durable waiting across process restart (986.568371ms)\n▶ provider outage\n  ✔ 22. an endpoint outage reroutes to a qualified resource on another endpoint (2.088108ms)\n  ✔ 23. an outage parks the work when no alternate exists, and it resumes once a probe succeeds (1.657859ms)\n  ✔ 24. an outage of one endpoint coexists with independent work on another (2.404324ms)\n✔ provider outage (6.770338ms)\n▶ replay safety and non-temporary conditions\n  ✔ 25. UNKNOWN execution is never turned into a submission elsewhere (4.78463ms)\n  ✔ 26. auth and permanent failures are not temporary windows (2.088345ms)\n  ✔ 27. simultaneous conditions are tracked independently (0.671628ms)\n  ✔ 28. provider- and account-scope limits cover exactly that provider or credential (0.578027ms)\n  ✔ 29. a model-scope limit covers that model on every endpoint of the provider, and nothing else (0.379652ms)\n  ✔ 30. no busy loop: repeated failures back off and are bounded (3.44608ms)\n✔ replay safety and non-temporary conditions (12.517103ms)\n▶ compatibility and convergence\n  ✔ 31. unit agents are pinned to the resource and never admit more context than it serves (3.86241ms)\n  ✔ 32. durable state survives park, wait and resume (401.903209ms)\n  ✔ 33. completion still requires the original acceptance dependencies (4.273669ms)\n  ✔ 34. a genuine no-safe-transition blocks with one concrete decision instead of looping (1.621168ms)\n✔ compatibility and convergence (412.179666ms)\n▶ provider catalog enrichment (optional)\n  ✔ gateway /v1/models metadata adds capabilities, context and pool; no serving capacity parks the model (1.589258ms)\n  ✔ an expired catalog condition is re-checked before work is sent, not rediscovered with a request (2.163273ms)\n  ✔ one driver per operation: a live holder excludes a second driver; a dead holder's lock is taken over (5.061991ms)\n  ✔ dependency cycles and unknown references are rejected up front (0.666266ms)\n  ✔ scheduler decisions are pure over state (no executor needed) (0.420406ms)\n✔ provider catalog enrichment (optional) (10.489064ms)\nℹ tests 39\nℹ suites 8\nℹ pass 39\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 4676.133097\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":5,"nanos":752422433}},"started_at_ms":1793135310767,"completed_at_ms":1793135316519}}
