{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T22:28:58.367Z","ordinal":429072,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17f7b-217f-7571-a9f6-435986d73294","call_id":"call_b5d337ea28b14d68b9024ef8f32824cb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 30.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1180)\nTotal output lines: 50\n\n▶ PLAN-08 PR-8c: Persistence retention, GC, and indexed sessions (REQ-PER-102, DEC-11, ACC-PER-02)\n  ✔ Session indexing with rebuild-on-miss and performance (1k sessions lists in < 500 ms) (499.157474ms)\n  ✔ ACC-PER-02: seed 10k tasks and 2k sessions; gc --dry-run reports and gc brings store under cap (635803.152671ms)\n  ✔ Checkpoints git ref and snapshot pruning, flights pruning (453.587327ms)\n  ✔ Background daily GC: first-run acknowledgement, NEXUS_GC=auto, and 2s timeout bounding (4.892073ms)\n  ✔ Background daily GC: enforces single end-to-end deadline across planning, identity capture, and execution (18.91044ms)\n  ✔ Planning candidate selection and size cap sorting respects expired deadline (6.639848ms)\n  ✔ Background daily GC: persists summary and lastRunAt even when work budget expires (9.387792ms)\n  ✔ Planning: bounded metadata streaming respects deadline and preserves pin protection on large legacy state envelopes (134.209976ms)\n✔ PLAN-08 PR-8c: Persistence retention, GC, and indexed sessions (REQ-PER-102, DEC-11, ACC-PER-02) (636934.649348ms)\n✔ large escaped JSON metadata keeps pinned records and decodes Unicode workspaces (23.550471ms)\n✔ large metadata preserves the ordinary JSON pin value semantics (52.108553ms)\n✔ large escaped session identity keeps the current session out of retention (14.817356ms)\n✔ metadata reads remain bounded when a small envelope is replaced after stat (72.235465ms)\n✔ a snapshotDir outside the checkpoint store is not deleted (11.133227ms)\n✔ a symlinked snapshots root is not used as the confinement root (3.546812ms)\n✔ a symlinked checkpoint partition cannot redirect snapshot deletion outside the store (2.662717ms)\n✔ a checkpoint root replaced after planning cannot redirect deletion (4.681942ms)\n✔ a checkpoint root replaced by another real directory is rejected by identity (4.216538ms)\n✔ a checkpoint partition replaced after planning cannot redirect deletion (6.424986ms)\n✔ a checkpoint parti…180 tokens truncated…ckpoint store is still reclaimed (3.784379ms)\n✔ configured hook guard forces event-wide disable after inherited enable (35.444406ms)\n✔ configured hook guard fails closed on Git 2.54 (6.670305ms)\n✔ checkpoint gc disables repository hooks and deletes the checkpoint ref (91.763846ms)\n﹣ checkpoint gc disables configured hooks added immediately before ref deletion (76.083988ms) # event-wide repository hook suppression requires Git 2.55 or later\n✔ checkpoint gc preserves a ref when its record changes after planning (78.108903ms)\n✔ checkpoint gc restores the ref if the record changes during ref deletion (106.422149ms)\n✔ checkpoint gc preserves the record and reports failure when ref deletion fails (81.330947ms)\n✔ checkpoint garbage collection never interpolates a checkpoint id into a shell (26.09973ms)\n✔ GC accounts for and removes message journals, history logs, and exact migration backups (82.888346ms)\n✔ GC durably removes a task primary before its associated conversation files (148.558044ms)\n✔ GC preserves task companions when syncing primary removal fails (15.938152ms)\n✔ GC preserves all components of a record modified after planning (7.839688ms)\n✔ GC skips a store while its writer owns the kernel guard (63.555359ms)\n✔ orphan journals and migration backups count toward the size cap and are collected together (70.886577ms)\n✔ a newly published envelope cancels an orphan deletion plan (11.481586ms)\n✔ companion removal failure propagates into deletion disposition and preserves record status (50.402279ms)\n✔ GC reads pin protection from the current envelope rather than a stale newer index (85.603685ms)\n✔ current and pinned tasks remain protected even during test-pollution cleanup (3.648683ms)\n▶ D2 run -j output lifecycle\n  ✔ a result far above 64 KiB arrives byte-exact and valid through a slow pipe, with the intended exit code (3764.174492ms)\n  ✔ a large failing result keeps its non-zero exit code through a slow pipe (2224.060054ms)\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"SESSION_ID=19326"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17ef2-de25-7482-bff6-192772052d26","create_time":1793140138.3676786}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
