 (REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-11, ACC-UPG-12) (2618.137555ms)\n▶ managed client invocation classification\n  ✔ keeps ambiguous maintenance options on the normal client path (1.784481ms)\n  ✔ releases the normal client lease only for recognized metadata and restore commands (0.511074ms)\n✔ managed client invocation classification (4.48809ms)\n▶ durable same-version transaction recovery\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash before-old-move (1059.160067ms)\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash after-old-move (1168.763777ms)\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash after-new-move (1186.878846ms)\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash after-provenance (1166.552383ms)\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash after-link (1496.122535ms)\n  ✔ preserves the only working package after crash after-failed-displacement (1405.06625ms)\n  ✔ retains backups and truthful journal when restoring the link fails (817.866283ms)\n  ✔ preserves a regular launcher file and refuses downloading recovery (421.468517ms)\n  ✔ preserves a regular launcher file and refuses verified recovery (399.873431ms)\n  ✔ preserves a regular launcher substituted after inspection (715.002933ms)\n  ✔ restores an entry displaced by a process interrupted before launcher installation (958.607736ms)\n  ✔ continues after a process is interrupted while restoring the original symlink (453.363363ms)\n  ✔ preserves a regular launcher after an interrupted restore left both hard links (414.212889ms)\n  ✔ admits only one recovery when two contenders both observe the same stale lock (1239.503999ms)\n  ✔ reclaims a stale lock through the kernel guard without contention (772.801049ms)\n  ✔ reports the guard path and stays back while a live reclaimer holds the kernel guard (423.205712ms)\n  ✔ acquires the kernel guard after its holder is killed (684.541298ms)\n  ✔ does not leak descriptors across repeated guard contention (263.571177ms)\n  ✔ fails closed when the flock utility is unavailable (8.867751ms)\n  ✔ rejects a symlinked reclaim guard (3.844015ms)\n  ✔ rejects a FIFO reclaim guard (9.809713ms)\n  ✔ rejects a reclaim guard with unsafe permissions (3.926911ms)\n  ✔ does not touch the lock for a completed journal in a read-only package directory (722.943517ms)\n  ✔ does not finalize a launcher that reports the wrong release (1262.631853ms)\n  ✔ refuses missing runtime components despite a successful version shim (63.426798ms)\n  ✔ uses the actual previous same-version package for explicit binary rollback (808.975737ms)\n  ✔ rejects a redirected backup without touching outside data (31.773036ms)\n  ✔ check-only leaves a pending transaction byte-for-byte unchanged (816.348453ms)\n  ✔ explicit recovery rejects invalid journals with an operational exit (1160.656944ms)\n  ✔ bounds hung probes and kills their process group (279.308973ms)\n✔ durable same-version transaction recovery (20223.983503ms)\n▶ complete private state/config backup restore\n  ✔ reports byte progress while a single large file is still being copied (90.736451ms)\n  ✔ reports only aggregate backup progress and syncs each copied directory once (1113.407588ms)\n  ✔ restores session payloads and config rather than copying an archive into config.env (1468.411071ms)\n  ✔ captures and restores task and session state rooted at NEXUS_STATE_DIR (688.343264ms)\n  ✔ honors NEXUS_STATE_DIR when HOME is a symlink (634.43459ms)\n  ✔ flushes every automatic backup payload and containing directory before returning (98.427191ms)\n  ✔ preserves an existing backup when exclusive creation reports EEXIST (8.78678ms)\n  ✔ does not merge into an existing timestamped state backup directory (9.866991ms)\n  ✔ keeps committed restore barriers until staged payload cleanup succeeds (198.667305ms)\n  ✔ replays a prepared restore after interruption and blocks state access until recovery (227.00579ms)\n  ✔ fails closed when a per-store marker survives without its global journal (3.742044ms)\n  ✔ 